ading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/add-a-server#expected-result","content":"Expected result"},"6":{"id":"/docs/client/add-a-server-4","page_id":"/docs/client/add-a-server","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/add-a-server#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"7":{"id":"/docs/client/add-a-server-5","page_id":"/docs/client/add-a-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/add-a-server#what-it-is","content":"The side panel's \"Add server\" form opens a WebTransport session to one\ncapture server. Each server you add gets a server card in the\n\"Servers\" list. You can add several servers, and all their point\nclouds are drawn in the same 3D view."},"8":{"id":"/docs/client/add-a-server-6","page_id":"/docs/client/add-a-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/add-a-server#how-to-do-it","content":"Start the client (see Run the dev build) and\nopen http\\://localhost:5173/."},"9":{"id":"/docs/client/add-a-server-7","page_id":"/docs/client/add-a-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/add-a-server#how-to-do-it","content":"In **Add server**, type the server's WebTransport URL, for example\n`https://capture-01.local:4433/orbbec`. Replace the host, port and path\nwith your server's."},"10":{"id":"/docs/client/add-a-server-8","page_id":"/docs/client/add-a-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/add-a-server#how-to-do-it","content":"Click **Connect to server**."},"11":{"id":"/docs/client/add-a-server-9","page_id":"/docs/client/add-a-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/add-a-server#how-to-do-it","content":"The URL must follow these rules. The form checks them before connecting:"},"12":{"id":"/docs/client/add-a-server-10","page_id":"/docs/client/add-a-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/add-a-server#how-to-do-it","content":"Rule"},"13":{"id":"/docs/client/add-a-server-11","page_id":"/docs/client/add-a-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/add-a-server#how-to-do-it","content":"Message when broken"},"14":{"id":"/docs/client/add-a-server-12","page_id":"/docs/client/add-a-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/add-a-server#how-to-do-it","content":"Not empty"},"15":{"id":"/docs/client/add-a-server-13","page_id":"/docs/client/add-a-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/add-a-server#how-to-do-it","content":"`enter a server URL, e.g. https://host:4433/orbbec`"},"16":{"id":"/docs/client/add-a-server-14","page_id":"/docs/client/add-a-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/add-a-server#how-to-do-it","content":"A valid absolute URL"},"17":{"id":"/docs/client/add-a-server-15","page_id":"/docs/client/add-a-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/add-a-server#how-to-do-it","content":"`not a URL: …`"},"18":{"id":"/docs/client/add-a-server-16","page_id":"/docs/client/add-a-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/add-a-server#how-to-do-it","content":"Scheme `https:`"},"19":{"id":"/docs/client/add-a-server-17","page_id":"/docs/client/add-a-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/add-a-server#how-to-do-it","content":"`WebTransport needs an https: URL, got …`"},"20":{"id":"/docs/client/add-a-server-18","page_id":"/docs/client/add-a-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/add-a-server#how-to-do-it","content":"No fragment, not even an empty `#`"},"21":{"id":"/docs/client/add-a-server-19","page_id":"/docs/client/add-a-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/add-a-server#how-to-do-it","content":"`WebTransport URLs cannot have a fragment (#…)`"},"22":{"id":"/docs/client/add-a-server-20","page_id":"/docs/client/add-a-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/add-a-server#how-to-do-it","content":"The browser must trust the server's TLS certificate. The client opens the\nsession with no extra options: it does not use\n`serverCertificateHashes`, so a self-signed certificate is accepted only\nif the browser already trusts it."},"23":{"id":"/docs/client/add-a-server-21","page_id":"/docs/client/add-a-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/add-a-server#expected-result","content":"A new server card appears under \"Servers\" at once, with the status\n`connecting`. After the handshake, the card shows the server's name and\nid. The client then subscribes to every camera bundle the server\nannounces, and that server's point cloud should appear in the 3D view.\nThis path is built and tested against simulated servers, but has not yet\nbeen run against a real server or in a browser with HEVC decoding. That\ncheck is tracked in `client/docs/development/ROADMAP.md` (Phase 2,\n\"Check with real decoded HEVC frames in a browser\")."},"24":{"id":"/docs/client/add-a-server-22","page_id":"/docs/client/add-a-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/add-a-server#expected-result","content":"Every line and action of the card is described in\nRead the server card."},"25":{"id":"/docs/client/add-a-server-23","page_id":"/docs/client/add-a-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/add-a-server#expected-result","content":"How connections behave:"},"26":{"id":"/docs/client/add-a-server-24","page_id":"/docs/client/add-a-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/add-a-server#expected-result","content":"**Connect timeout:** a connection attempt that has not completed its\nhandshake after 10 s is closed as `connect timeout`."},"27":{"id":"/docs/client/add-a-server-25","page_id":"/docs/client/add-a-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/add-a-server#expected-result","content":"**Reconnect:**"},"28":{"id":"/docs/client/add-a-server-26","page_id":"/docs/client/add-a-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/add-a-server#expected-result","content":"A lost session is retried automatically after 1 s. The delay doubles\nup to 30 s between attempts, with no attempt limit."},"29":{"id":"/docs/client/add-a-server-27","page_id":"/docs/client/add-a-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/add-a-server#expected-result","content":"It is not retried after Remove, after a protocol version mismatch, or\nafter a conflict. The card's **Reconnect** action starts a new\nsession at once whenever the card shows `error` or `disconnected`.\nIt is unavailable while the card is connecting or connected."},"30":{"id":"/docs/client/add-a-server-28","page_id":"/docs/client/add-a-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/add-a-server#troubleshooting","content":"**`last close: transport error: …` and status `error`:** the session could\nnot be opened."},"31":{"id":"/docs/client/add-a-server-29","page_id":"/docs/client/add-a-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/add-a-server#troubleshooting","content":"Check that the server is running and reachable at that host and port\nover UDP (WebTransport runs on HTTP/3, over QUIC)."},"32":{"id":"/docs/client/add-a-server-30","page_id":"/docs/client/add-a-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/add-a-server#troubleshooting","content":"Check that the browser trusts the server's certificate."},"33":{"id":"/docs/client/add-a-server-31","page_id":"/docs/client/add-a-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/add-a-server#troubleshooting","content":"In a browser without WebTransport, every attempt fails this way."},"34":{"id":"/docs/client/add-a-server-32","page_id":"/docs/client/add-a-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/add-a-server#troubleshooting","content":"**`connect timeout`:** opening the session and completing the\nhandshake took longer than 10 s. The server may be unreachable, or it\nmay not answer the hello; check the server's logs."},"35":{"id":"/docs/client/add-a-server-33","page_id":"/docs/client/add-a-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/add-a-server#troubleshooting","content":"**`Protocol version mismatch; cannot connect.`** or\n`last close: protocol error version-mismatch: …`: the server speaks\nanother major protocol version. Update the client or the server.\nThe client does not retry."},"36":{"id":"/docs/client/add-a-server-34","page_id":"/docs/client/add-a-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/add-a-server#troubleshooting","content":"**Conflict:** two cards point at the same server (for example by IP\naddress and by host name). Remove one."},"37":{"id":"/docs/client/add-a-server-35","page_id":"/docs/client/add-a-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/add-a-server#troubleshooting","content":"**Card `streaming` but `uploaded 0`:**"},"38":{"id":"/docs/client/add-a-server-36","page_id":"/docs/client/add-a-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/add-a-server#troubleshooting","content":"A compatibility line means this browser cannot decode HEVC. See\nBrowser requirements."},"39":{"id":"/docs/client/add-a-server-37","page_id":"/docs/client/add-a-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/add-a-server#troubleshooting","content":"Otherwise, check the bundle rows of the card's layout for an error."},"40":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","type":"page","content":"Browser requirements","breadcrumbs":["HSLU OrbbecStreamer","Client"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements"},"41":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-0","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","content":"What the browser needs for the client, and what the client does when something is missing."},"42":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-1","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#what-it-is","content":"What it is"},"43":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-2","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#how-to-check-your-browser","content":"How to check your browser"},"44":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-3","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#expected-result","content":"Expected result"},"45":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-4","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#known-results","content":"Known results"},"46":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-5","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"47":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-6","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#what-it-is","content":"The client uses three browser features. It still runs when one is missing,\nbut with less functionality. Following the protocol's compatibility rule\n(§16), a browser that cannot decode or render remains a valid **control and\nsetup client**. It can connect and show server state, but it draws no point\nclouds."},"48":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-7","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#what-it-is","content":"Feature"},"49":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-8","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#what-it-is","content":"Used for"},"50":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-9","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#what-it-is","content":"Without it"},"51":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-10","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#what-it-is","content":"WebTransport"},"52":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-11","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#what-it-is","content":"The connection to a live server"},"53":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-12","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#what-it-is","content":"Adding a server by URL fails to connect. Recordings still play."},"54":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-13","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#what-it-is","content":"WebCodecs `VideoDecoder` with HEVC Main (8-bit)"},"55":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-14","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#what-it-is","content":"Colour streams"},"56":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-15","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#what-it-is","content":"Control and setup only: no point clouds"},"57":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-16","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#what-it-is","content":"WebCodecs `VideoDecoder` with HEVC Main10 (10-bit)"},"58":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-17","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#what-it-is","content":"Depth streams"},"59":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-18","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#what-it-is","content":"Control and setup only: no point clouds"},"60":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-19","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#what-it-is","content":"WebGPU, or WebGL2 as fallback"},"61":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-20","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#what-it-is","content":"Drawing the point clouds"},"62":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-21","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#what-it-is","content":"`rendering-incompatible`; control and setup only"},"63":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-22","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#what-it-is","content":"All of these need a **secure context**: `https://`, or `http://localhost`.\nThe dev server listens on `http://localhost:5173`, which counts as secure."},"64":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-23","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#how-to-check-your-browser","content":"Start the dev build (see Run the dev build)."},"65":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-24","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#how-to-check-your-browser","content":"Open http\\://localhost:5173/."},"66":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-25","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#how-to-check-your-browser","content":"Read the top of the side panel:"},"67":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-26","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#how-to-check-your-browser","content":"`renderer: webgpu` or `renderer: webgl2` names the backend that was\ncreated."},"68":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-27","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#how-to-check-your-browser","content":"`decoders: WebCodecs` means the WebCodecs decoder exists. It does not\nyet mean that HEVC is supported."},"69":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-28","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#how-to-check-your-browser","content":"Add a server or open a recording. HEVC support is probed when the\nconnection opens. A compatibility line on the server card means a\nchannel cannot be decoded (see\nRead the server card)."},"70":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-29","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#expected-result","content":"On a fully capable browser, the panel shows `renderer: webgpu` (or\n`webgl2`) and `decoders: WebCodecs`. Server cards show no compatibility line."},"71":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-30","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#expected-result","content":"With something missing, the panel shows one of these, verbatim:"},"72":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-31","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#expected-result","content":"**No WebGPU and no WebGL2:**\n`renderer: rendering-incompatible. Rendering incompatible: neither WebGPU nor WebGL2 is available. This browser can still connect as a control and setup client (§16); no point clouds are drawn.`"},"73":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-32","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#expected-result","content":"The decoders line then reads: `Decoding is off: nothing could be drawn without a rendering backend (§16). client.hello still reports this browser's HEVC support.`"},"74":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-33","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#expected-result","content":"The client still tells each server which HEVC profiles this browser\ncan decode, but it creates no decoder."},"75":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-34","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#expected-result","content":"**No WebCodecs:** `decoders: WebCodecs VideoDecoder is unavailable: control and setup only (§16).`"},"76":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-35","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#expected-result","content":"**HEVC not supported for a channel:** the server card shows a line such as\n`Setup and control only: this browser lacks HEVC colour decoding and HEVC Main10 depth decoding.`"},"77":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-36","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#known-results","content":"These were observed on the project's test machine. Other browsers have not\nbeen tested yet."},"78":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-37","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#known-results","content":"**Headless Chromium 153 (snap) on Linux, over SSH, 2026-09-23:**"},"79":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-38","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#known-results","content":"WebCodecs works; H.264, VP9 and AV1 decode in software."},"80":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-39","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#known-results","content":"No hardware video decoding is available."},"81":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-40","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#known-results","content":"HEVC is reported unsupported for both colour and depth, in every\nhardware-acceleration mode, even with the VA-API flags."},"82":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-41","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#known-results","content":"The client therefore connects and stays control-only. This is why the\nwiring and latency check pages use a synthetic decoder. The decode\ncheck uses real WebCodecs, and so reports the missing support."},"83":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-42","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#known-results","content":"**Real HEVC decoding in a browser has not been verified yet.**"},"84":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-43","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#known-results","content":"The next test is desktop Chrome or Edge with GPU video decode, or\nSafari."},"85":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-44","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#known-results","content":"It is tracked in `client/docs/development/ROADMAP.md` under\n\"Phase 2 — media and rendering\" (\"Check with real decoded HEVC frames in\na browser\")."},"86":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-45","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#known-results","content":"**Rendering in headless Chromium with SwiftShader:**"},"87":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-46","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#known-results","content":"WebGL2 works."},"88":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-47","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#known-results","content":"WebGPU works with `--enable-unsafe-webgpu`."},"89":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-48","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#known-results","content":"WebGPU failed with a lost device on 2026-09-24, while about 20 stray\nheadless Chromium instances were running on the same machine. After\nthey were closed, the wiring check passed on WebGPU (see the roadmap\nitem \"Wiring check on WebGPU\"). Headless WebGPU on SwiftShader is\nsensitive to machine load."},"90":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-49","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#troubleshooting","content":"**`rendering-incompatible` on a desktop browser:** hardware acceleration\nmay be off. Turn on \"Use graphics acceleration when available\" in\nthe browser settings, then check `chrome://gpu` (Chrome or Edge) for\nWebGL2 and WebGPU status."},"91":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-50","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#troubleshooting","content":"**Every server card says the browser lacks HEVC decoding:** the browser has no\nHEVC decoder for this platform. Try another browser or machine with GPU\nvideo decoding. The client still works for control and setup."},"92":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-51","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#troubleshooting","content":"**Nothing works when opened from another machine by IP address:**\nplain `http://` is only a secure context on `localhost`. The page must\nbe served over HTTPS with a certificate that machine trusts; the\nrepository has no HTTPS dev configuration yet."},"93":{"id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements-52","page_id":"/docs/client/browser-requirements","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/browser-requirements#troubleshooting","content":"**`renderer notes` in the panel:** expand them. They say why WebGPU was\nskipped, for example `WebGPU not supported`."},"94":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","type":"page","content":"Calibration","breadcrumbs":["HSLU OrbbecStreamer","Client"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/calibration"},"95":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-0","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration","content":"Run, watch, cancel and commit a server's depth-quantization calibration in the setup workspace; what camera pose and network show today."},"96":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-1","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/calibration#what-it-is","content":"What it is"},"97":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-2","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/calibration#how-to-use-it","content":"How to use it"},"98":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-3","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/calibration#every-section","content":"Every section"},"99":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-4","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/calibration#depth-quantization","content":"Depth quantization"},"100":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-5","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/calibration#camera-pose","content":"Camera pose"},"101":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-6","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/calibration#network","content":"Network"},"102":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-7","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/calibration#expected-result","content":"Expected result"},"103":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-8","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/calibration#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"104":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-9","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#what-it-is","content":"Each server has three calibration kinds. The\nsetup workspace shows one section per\nkind:"},"105":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-10","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#what-it-is","content":"Kind"},"106":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-11","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#what-it-is","content":"What you can do today"},"107":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-12","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#what-it-is","content":"**Camera pose**"},"108":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-13","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#what-it-is","content":"Read its state. The camera-calibration screen is a placeholder: a red, bold, italic `TODO`, with no controls."},"109":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-14","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#what-it-is","content":"**Depth quantization**"},"110":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-15","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#what-it-is","content":"Start, watch, cancel and commit a run."},"111":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-16","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#what-it-is","content":"**Network**"},"112":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-17","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#what-it-is","content":"Nothing: `Not available yet: waits for change request 0018.`"},"113":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-18","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#what-it-is","content":"A calibration run produces a **result**. The result is **not in force**\nuntil you commit it. The client never commits a result by itself. When\nyou leave the workspace, or the lock or the connection is lost, the\nclient discards its own copy of an uncommitted result. What the server\ndoes with that result is not defined by the protocol contract yet\n(change request 0012 is open); the mock server drops it."},"114":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-19","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#what-it-is","content":"The client's reading of \"result\" and \"commit\" follows the client's\nproposal in change request 0012, which the protocol contract has not\ndecided yet."},"115":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-20","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#how-to-use-it","content":"Open the setup workspace for the server first (**Set up** on its card).\nEvery action needs the session line to read\n`active: this client holds the setup lock`."},"116":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-21","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#every-section","content":"Each section starts with its state line, for example\n`state: valid, revision 3`, or\n`state: valid, revision 1: result revision 2 awaits commit` (the text\nafter the colon is the server's message; this one is the mock server's):\nthe state (`missing`, `valid`, `stale`, `running` or `failed`), the\nrevision in force, and the server's message if any. The line is highlighted when a\nkind has `failed`, or when camera pose or depth quantization is not\n`valid` (and not `running`)."},"117":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-22","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#depth-quantization","content":"Select **Start depth quantization**. The line under the buttons reads\n`Start: accepted; the run is starting`, and the state becomes\n`running`."},"118":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-23","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#depth-quantization","content":"Watch the progress. The server sends it only to the client that holds\nthe lock:"},"119":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-24","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#depth-quantization","content":"**elapsed:** time since the run started, for example `1.0 s`;"},"120":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-25","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#depth-quantization","content":"**valid samples:** for example `4 000`;"},"121":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-26","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#depth-quantization","content":"**observed range:** for example `500 to 5000 mm`;"},"122":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-27","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#depth-quantization","content":"**reconstruction error:** for example `1.50 mm`;"},"123":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-28","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#depth-quantization","content":"**histogram:** how many pixels had each depth code. The chart covers\nthe valid codes 2 to 1022. The line under it gives the counts of the\nthree special codes: `invalid (0)`, `below minimum (1)` and\n`above maximum (1023)`. Switch the **scale** between `log` (the\ndefault, which keeps small counts visible) and `linear`."},"124":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-29","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#depth-quantization","content":"A number the server did not send reads `not reported`."},"125":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-30","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#depth-quantization","content":"Wait for the result. When the run produced one, the section shows\n`Result ready: revision 4, not in force until committed.`, followed by\nthe server's message if any. The state line still shows the old\nrevision."},"126":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-31","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#depth-quantization","content":"Select **Commit depth quantization**. The line reads\n`Commit: accepted; the new revision comes into force with the server update`.\nMoments later the state line reads `valid, revision 4`, and every\nclient shows the new revision on its server card."},"127":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-32","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#depth-quantization","content":"To stop a run, select **Cancel depth quantization**. The line reads\n`Cancel: accepted; the run is cancelled and nothing is committed`. The\nstate line then shows the state the server reports (the mock server\nreturns to the state from before the run)."},"128":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-33","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#depth-quantization","content":"When the server reports a result for the cancelled or failed run, the\nsection also says\n`The last run produced no result to commit: <message>. Revision 3 stays in force.`\nWhether that line appears after a cancel depends on whether the server\nsends that result before it answers the cancel. The protocol contract\ndoes not fix that order yet (change request 0008); the mock server sends\nthe result first."},"129":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-34","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#depth-quantization","content":"A run that fails shows the state `failed`, and **Commit** stays\nunavailable."},"130":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-35","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#depth-quantization","content":"Only the newest action keeps its line under the buttons."},"131":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-36","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#depth-quantization","content":"**When a button is unavailable**, the reason is written under it. While\na request is waiting for the server's answer, its button shows\n`in progress`."},"132":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-37","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#depth-quantization","content":"Reason"},"133":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-38","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#depth-quantization","content":"Meaning"},"134":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-39","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#depth-quantization","content":"`the setup session is not active`"},"135":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-40","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#depth-quantization","content":"The workspace does not hold the lock (acquiring, leaving or ended)."},"136":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-41","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#depth-quantization","content":"`the depth-quantization calibration is running`"},"137":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-42","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#depth-quantization","content":"Start and Commit wait until the run ends."},"138":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-43","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#depth-quantization","content":"`the depth-quantization calibration is not running`"},"139":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-44","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#depth-quantization","content":"Nothing to cancel."},"140":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-45","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#depth-quantization","content":"`no accepted depth-quantization result to commit`"},"141":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-46","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#depth-quantization","content":"Run the calibration first; a failed or cancelled run has nothing to commit."},"142":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-47","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#camera-pose","content":"The section shows the state line and the red `TODO` placeholder, nothing\nelse. The camera-calibration screen is a placeholder; there is no way to\nstart a camera-pose calibration from the client yet. It is tracked in\n`client/docs/development/ROADMAP.md`, \"Phase 1D — UI\", item \"Focused\nsetup workspace; camera-calibration placeholder …\"."},"143":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-48","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#network","content":"The section shows the state line and\n`Not available yet: waits for change request 0018.` Change request 0018\n(network calibration stream) is proposed, not yet part of the protocol\ncontract. It is tracked in `client/docs/development/ROADMAP.md`,\n\"Phase 1C — connections (remaining)\", item \"Temporary\nnetwork-calibration stream\"."},"144":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-49","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#expected-result","content":"After **Start**, progress numbers appear within the server's first\nprogress interval and update while the run lasts; the histogram\nredraws with each update."},"145":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-50","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#expected-result","content":"After the run, `Result ready: revision N, not in force until committed.`\nappears and **Commit depth quantization** becomes available."},"146":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-51","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#expected-result","content":"After **Commit**, the state line shows `valid, revision N` on this\nclient and on every other client's server card."},"147":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-52","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#expected-result","content":"After **Cancel**, the revision in force does not change."},"148":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-53","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#expected-result","content":"When you leave or lose the lock, the client commits nothing, and the\nrevision in force does not change."},"149":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-54","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#troubleshooting","content":"**The result was not committed:** a result waits for **Commit**. If you\nleft the workspace or lost the lock first, the client discarded its\ncopy (the exit box says\n`The client discarded the uncommitted depth quantization result.`).\nStart the run again and commit it."},"150":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-55","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#troubleshooting","content":"**Forced out in the middle of a run:** the client commits nothing. What\nthe server does with a run whose lock ends is not defined by the\nprotocol contract yet (change request 0012 is open); the mock server\ncancels it. Check the state line when you are back in: if it still\nshows `running`, the run continued on the server. See\nSetup workspace."},"151":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-56","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#troubleshooting","content":"**`Start rejected (<code>): <message>`** (or Cancel, Commit): the server\nrefused the request. The code and message are the server's own. From\nthe mock server, for example: `calibration-running` (another run is\nin progress), `calibration-not-running`, `not-lock-owner`."},"152":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-57","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#troubleshooting","content":"**`Commit failed (timeout): …`:** the server did not answer in time.\nThe state line tells you whether the new revision is in force. If not,\nand the result is still shown, select **Commit** again."},"153":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-58","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#troubleshooting","content":"**`histogram: not reported by the server`:** the server sent no\nhistogram with its progress. The numbers above still apply."},"154":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-59","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#troubleshooting","content":"**`histogram: depth histogram has N bins, expected 1024`:** the server\nsent a histogram of the wrong size; the client does not draw it."},"155":{"id":"/docs/client/calibration-60","page_id":"/docs/client/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/calibration#troubleshooting","content":"**Commit accepted but the state line still shows the old revision:**\nthe new revision comes into force with the server's next update. It\nnormally follows at once; if it does not, check the card for\n`resynchronising` or a lost connection."},"156":{"id":"/docs/client/dev-build","page_id":"/docs/client/dev-build","type":"page","content":"Run the dev build","breadcrumbs":["HSLU OrbbecStreamer","Client"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/dev-build"},"157":{"id":"/docs/client/dev-build-0","page_id":"/docs/client/dev-build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/dev-build","content":"Install the client, start the Vite dev server, build and preview it, and open the dev check pages."},"158":{"id":"/docs/client/d