nt":"**Query parameters:**"},"206":{"id":"/docs/client/dev-build-49","page_id":"/docs/client/dev-build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/dev-build#dev-check-pages","content":"`?autorun=1` for the render, wiring, latency, cards, setup and\nplacement checks;"},"207":{"id":"/docs/client/dev-build-50","page_id":"/docs/client/dev-build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/dev-build#dev-check-pages","content":"`?autorun=samples` for the decode check;"},"208":{"id":"/docs/client/dev-build-51","page_id":"/docs/client/dev-build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/dev-build#dev-check-pages","content":"`?engine=webgl2` or `?engine=webgpu` forces a backend where the page\nsupports it."},"209":{"id":"/docs/client/dev-build-52","page_id":"/docs/client/dev-build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/dev-build#dev-check-pages","content":"**Reading the result:** each page sets `body[data-state]` to `done` or\n`failed` and exposes its report on `window`, for example\n`window.__wiringCheckReport`."},"210":{"id":"/docs/client/dev-build-53","page_id":"/docs/client/dev-build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/dev-build#dev-check-pages","content":"The wiring check's read-back overlay:"},"211":{"id":"/docs/client/dev-build-54","page_id":"/docs/client/dev-build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/dev-build#dev-check-pages","content":"`?readback=1` draws the read-back frame into an overlay. This is for\nheadless screenshots that miss a WebGPU canvas."},"212":{"id":"/docs/client/dev-build-55","page_id":"/docs/client/dev-build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/dev-build#dev-check-pages","content":"The report JSON sits in a collapsed \"report JSON\" panel at the bottom\nright."},"213":{"id":"/docs/client/dev-build-56","page_id":"/docs/client/dev-build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/dev-build#dev-check-pages","content":"The decode, wiring and latency checks fetch sample recordings from\n`client/reference/hevc-web/`. That folder is a local, untracked copy of a\ncolleague's reference client and is **not in the repository**. Without\nit:"},"214":{"id":"/docs/client/dev-build-57","page_id":"/docs/client/dev-build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/dev-build#dev-check-pages","content":"the decode check fails at once, reporting a missing file;"},"215":{"id":"/docs/client/dev-build-58","page_id":"/docs/client/dev-build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/dev-build#dev-check-pages","content":"the wiring and latency checks fail only after about 30 s with \"no pair\nuploaded\". The dev server answers a missing `.hevc` path with its HTML\npage, not a 404."},"216":{"id":"/docs/client/dev-build-59","page_id":"/docs/client/dev-build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/dev-build#dev-check-pages","content":"The decode check also accepts files you pick yourself. The render check\nneeds no files."},"217":{"id":"/docs/client/dev-build-60","page_id":"/docs/client/dev-build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/dev-build#dev-check-pages","content":"For testing without hardware, see also the\nMock server."},"218":{"id":"/docs/client/dev-build-61","page_id":"/docs/client/dev-build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/dev-build#troubleshooting","content":"**`Error: Port 5173 is already in use`:** the dev server uses a fixed\nport (`strictPort`)."},"219":{"id":"/docs/client/dev-build-62","page_id":"/docs/client/dev-build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/dev-build#troubleshooting","content":"Stop the other dev server."},"220":{"id":"/docs/client/dev-build-63","page_id":"/docs/client/dev-build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/dev-build#troubleshooting","content":"Or start this one on another port and open that port instead:"},"221":{"id":"/docs/client/dev-build-64","page_id":"/docs/client/dev-build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/dev-build#troubleshooting","content":"**`npm: command not found`:**"},"222":{"id":"/docs/client/dev-build-65","page_id":"/docs/client/dev-build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/dev-build#troubleshooting","content":"On some machines Node is installed without npm, for example through\npnpm. Install npm with your Node distribution."},"223":{"id":"/docs/client/dev-build-66","page_id":"/docs/client/dev-build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/dev-build#troubleshooting","content":"Once `node_modules/` exists, the same tools run directly from\n`client/`:"},"224":{"id":"/docs/client/dev-build-67","page_id":"/docs/client/dev-build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/dev-build#troubleshooting","content":"**The panel says `renderer: rendering-incompatible`:** see\nBrowser requirements."},"225":{"id":"/docs/client/dev-build-68","page_id":"/docs/client/dev-build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/dev-build#troubleshooting","content":"**Opened from another machine and nothing connects:** the dev server\nlistens on `localhost` only, and plain HTTP is a secure context only on\n`localhost`."},"226":{"id":"/docs/client/dev-build-69","page_id":"/docs/client/dev-build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/dev-build#troubleshooting","content":"`--host` exposes the server on the network, but the page then runs\nover plain HTTP, and WebTransport, WebCodecs and WebGPU are\nunavailable."},"227":{"id":"/docs/client/dev-build-70","page_id":"/docs/client/dev-build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/dev-build#troubleshooting","content":"Serving over HTTPS needs a `server.https` certificate in\n`client/vite.config.ts`. The repository does not configure one yet."},"228":{"id":"/docs/client/dev-build-71","page_id":"/docs/client/dev-build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/dev-build#troubleshooting","content":"**The decode check reports a missing file, or the wiring or latency\ncheck fails after about 30 s with no pair uploaded:** the reference\nrecordings in `client/reference/hevc-web/` are missing. See above."},"229":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","type":"page","content":"Cards check","breadcrumbs":["HSLU OrbbecStreamer","Client","Developer"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check"},"230":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check-0","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","content":"A dev page that runs two clients of one mock server side by side and drives their server cards through a scripted scenario."},"231":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check-1","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check#what-it-is","content":"What it is"},"232":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check-2","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check#how-to-use-it","content":"How to use it"},"233":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check-3","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check#expected-result","content":"Expected result"},"234":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check-4","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"235":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check-5","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check#what-it-is","content":"The cards check (`client/dev/cards-check.html`, code in\n`client/src/dev/cardsCheck.tsx` and `client/src/dev/cardsScenario.ts`) is\na dev-only page for the server cards. It is\nnever part of the production build."},"236":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check-6","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check#what-it-is","content":"It runs two clients, **Client A** and **Client B**, against one\nmock server, and shows each\nclient's server cards in its own column. The cards are the app's own\ncards. The scripted card actions (lock, refresh, shared updates,\nreconnect) go through the same model function as the card buttons. The\ncalibration and placement steps (4 and 5) call client A's connection\ndirectly; the setup workspace has its own page, the\nsetup check.\nNothing is drawn in 3D: each client has a GPU-free renderer."},"237":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check-7","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check#what-it-is","content":"The mock serves the reference recordings when\n`client/reference/hevc-web/` exists, decoded by the dev pages' synthetic\ndecoder (the local headless Chromium cannot decode HEVC). Otherwise it is\nsnapshot-only, with no media."},"238":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check-8","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check#how-to-use-it","content":"Start the dev server in `client/`:"},"239":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check-9","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check#how-to-use-it","content":"Open this URL:"},"240":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check-10","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check#how-to-use-it","content":"URL parameters:"},"241":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check-11","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check#how-to-use-it","content":"Parameter"},"242":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check-12","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check#how-to-use-it","content":"Effect"},"243":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check-13","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check#how-to-use-it","content":"`autorun=1`"},"244":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check-14","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check#how-to-use-it","content":"Run the scripted scenario on load. Without it, press **Run scenario**."},"245":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check-15","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check#how-to-use-it","content":"`media=0`"},"246":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check-16","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check#how-to-use-it","content":"Use a snapshot-only mock even when the recordings exist."},"247":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check-17","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check#how-to-use-it","content":"The scenario, in order:"},"248":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check-18","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check#how-to-use-it","content":"Both clients connect."},"249":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check-19","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check#how-to-use-it","content":"A acquires the lock. B shows `held by Client A (…)`, and B's\n**Acquire lock** is unavailable with the reason\n`the lock is held by Client A`."},"250":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check-20","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check#how-to-use-it","content":"B sends an acquire anyway, through the model function the button\ncalls (the unavailable button itself sends nothing). The mock server\nrefuses it, and the page log (not B's card) shows\n`Client B: Acquire lock rejected (lock-held): setup lock held by Client A`.\n`lock-held` is the mock server's code; a real server may use another."},"251":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check-21","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check#how-to-use-it","content":"B turns shared updates off, and A commits a placement. B still gets\nthe new placement, because the change restarts the streams and B\nfetches the full state by itself."},"252":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check-22","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check#how-to-use-it","content":"A runs a depth-quantization calibration. B shows it `running`. The\nresult is withheld from B, so B's card shows stale metadata until B\nrefreshes. After A commits, B shows the calibration `valid` at a new\nrevision."},"253":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check-23","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check#how-to-use-it","content":"A releases the lock. B acquires it (A shows `held by Client B (…)`),\nthen releases it."},"254":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check-24","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check#how-to-use-it","content":"The mock drops B's session. B's card shows `error` and\n`reconnect scheduled`, and B's **Reconnect** restores the session.\nWith the reference recordings, the step also waits until B's new\nsession uploads frames and its bundle shows `ready, drawing`."},"255":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check-25","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check#how-to-use-it","content":"Buttons for trying things by hand:"},"256":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check-26","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check#how-to-use-it","content":"**Drop A's session** and **Drop B's session**: the mock server loses\nthat client's session."},"257":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check-27","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check#how-to-use-it","content":"**Expire the lease**: the mock server expires the current lock."},"258":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check-28","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check#how-to-use-it","content":"**Pause for setup** and **Stop streaming**: server-side streaming\nchanges."},"259":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check-29","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check#how-to-use-it","content":"The card buttons work as in the app."},"260":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check-30","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check#expected-result","content":"The page ends with `body[data-state]` set to `done`, the log line\n`verdict: 7 steps passed`, and both columns showing a live card."},"261":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check-31","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check#expected-result","content":"`window.__cardsCheckReport` holds the report: `state`, `media`,\n`steps[]` (`name`, `ok`, `detail`), `log`, `errors` and `verdict`. The\nsame JSON is in the collapsed \"report JSON\" panel."},"262":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check-32","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check#expected-result","content":"Recorded runs, all on 2026-09-28 with headless snap Chromium 153 and\nthe reference recordings:"},"263":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check-33","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check#expected-result","content":"the client team lead ran it: `done`, 7 of 7 steps;"},"264":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check-34","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check#expected-result","content":"the UI engineer's two reruns after the per-session counts fix:\n`done`, 7 of 7 steps, no errors. The last step reported B at\n`decoded 1, uploaded 1, dropped 0 this session`. A screenshot a moment\nlater showed both columns `ready, drawing`, with decoded pairs equal to\nuploaded on each card (A 35 / 35, B 12 / 12)."},"265":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check-35","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check#expected-result","content":"**Counts on this page.** Both clients are wired the same way: a GPU-free\nrenderer that accepts every upload and draws nothing. The counts are per\nsession, so after B's Reconnect they start again from zero, while A's keep\ngrowing. A card that shows `decoded pairs 0 · uploaded 0` and\n`ready, no frame yet` just after the reconnect has not received its new\nsession's first frames yet."},"266":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check-36","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check#expected-result","content":"The same scenario runs in Node on a simulated clock as part of\n`npm test` (`client/src/tests/serverCards.test.ts`)."},"267":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check-37","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check#troubleshooting","content":"**`failed` with `timed out waiting for: …`:** the step named in\n`verdict` did not reach the expected card state within 8 s. The text\nafter it shows both cards' status and lock line at that moment."},"268":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check-38","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check#troubleshooting","content":"**`failed` with `watchdog: not done after 60 s`:** the run hung. Reload\nthe page, and check the browser console."},"269":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check-39","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/cards-check#troubleshooting","content":"**`media` is `snapshot only, no media` although you want frames:**\n`client/reference/hevc-web/` is missing or incomplete; `fallbackReason`\nin the report says which. The scenario does not need media; the counts\nsimply stay at 0. See\nLatency for how to get the folder."},"270":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","type":"page","content":"Latency measurement","breadcrumbs":["HSLU OrbbecStreamer","Client","Developer"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/developer/latency"},"271":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-0","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency","content":"Measure where the client spends time between the network and the screen, in the browser and in Node."},"272":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-1","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#what-it-is","content":"What it is"},"273":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-2","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#stages","content":"Stages"},"274":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-3","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#run-the-latency-check-page","content":"Run the latency check page"},"275":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-4","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#cross-origin-isolation","content":"Cross-origin isolation"},"276":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-5","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#expected-result","content":"Expected result"},"277":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-6","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#which-stages-mean-something-on-this-page","content":"Which stages mean something on this page"},"278":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-7","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#use-the-probe-in-your-own-code","content":"Use the probe in your own code"},"279":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-8","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#run-the-end-to-end-benchmark","content":"Run the end-to-end benchmark"},"280":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-9","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#compare-against-another-commit","content":"Compare against another commit"},"281":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-10","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"282":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-11","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#other-dev-check-pages","content":"Other dev check pages"},"283":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-12","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#what-it-is","content":"The client has three tools for measuring its own latency:"},"284":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-13","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#what-it-is","content":"**The per-stage latency probe** (`client/src/connections/latencyProbe.ts`).\nIt times each frame through the client, from the last network byte to the\nanimation frame after the draw, and reports p50/p90/p99/max per stage.\nIt is off unless a pipeline asks for it. When off, no clock is read on the\nmedia path."},"285":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-14","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#what-it-is","content":"**The latency check page** (`client/dev/latency-check.html`). It runs the\nprobe in a real browser over two recordings and shows the stage table."},"286":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-15","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#what-it-is","content":"**The end-to-end benchmark** (`npm run bench:e2e`). It runs the client\nmedia path in Node with the browser parts simulated, and can compare two\ncommits."},"287":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-16","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#what-it-is","content":"The main app does not turn the probe on. Only the latency check page and\nyour own code do."},"288":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-17","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#stages","content":"All values are in milliseconds."},"289":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-18","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#stages","content":"Stage"},"290":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-19","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#stages","content":"Channel"},"291":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-20","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#stages","content":"From → to"},"292":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-21","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#stages","content":"`network`"},"293":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-22","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#stages","content":"colour, depth"},"294":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-23","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#stages","content":"capture (server clock, converted with the clock-sync offset) → last byte of the record read by the client"},"295":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-24","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#stages","content":"`transport`"},"296":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-25","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#stages","content":"colour, depth"},"297":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-26","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#stages","content":"last byte read → record handed to its decoder (framing, router, keyframe gate)"},"298":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-27","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#stages","content":"`queue`"},"299":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-28","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#stages","content":"colour, depth"},"300":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-29","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#stages","content":"record handed to the decoder → `decode()` returned"},"301":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-30","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type"