docs/client/developer/latency#stages","content":"last byte of the later channel → `present`"},"322":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-51","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#stages","content":"`captureToPresent`"},"323":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-52","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#stages","content":"pair"},"324":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-53","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#stages","content":"capture → `present`"},"325":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-54","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#stages","content":"A stage is left out of the report until it has a sample. For example,\n`network` has no samples until the clock-sync offset is known. The window is\nthe last 512 samples per stage and channel."},"326":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-55","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#run-the-latency-check-page","content":"You need `client/reference/hevc-web/` with `gpu-output-color.hevc`,\n`gpu-output-depth.hevc` and, optionally, `public/hevcsetup.json`."},"327":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-56","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#run-the-latency-check-page","content":"This folder is not in the repository, and neither is `hevc-web.zip`; ask\nthe client team for the archive. Put `hevc-web.zip` in `client/`, then run\nthis in `client/`:"},"328":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-57","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#run-the-latency-check-page","content":"Start the dev server in `client/`:"},"329":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-58","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#run-the-latency-check-page","content":"Open this URL in Chrome:"},"330":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-59","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#run-the-latency-check-page","content":"URL parameters:"},"331":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-60","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#run-the-latency-check-page","content":"Parameter"},"332":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-61","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#run-the-latency-check-page","content":"Effect"},"333":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-62","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#run-the-latency-check-page","content":"`autorun=1`"},"334":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-63","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#run-the-latency-check-page","content":"Start on load. Without it, press **Start**."},"335":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-64","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#run-the-latency-check-page","content":"`engine=webgl2` or `engine=webgpu`"},"336":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-65","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#run-the-latency-check-page","content":"Force a rendering engine. Without it, WebGPU is tried first and WebGL2 is the fallback."},"337":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-66","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#run-the-latency-check-page","content":"`seconds=N`"},"338":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-67","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#run-the-latency-check-page","content":"Measuring time after the first upload, default 8, maximum 60."},"339":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-68","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#run-the-latency-check-page","content":"What the page does:"},"340":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-69","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#run-the-latency-check-page","content":"It plays both recordings through the real connection, decoding, pairing,\nfeed and renderer code. It uses a **synthetic decoder** that ignores the\nHEVC bytes and emits generated frames."},"341":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-70","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#run-the-latency-check-page","content":"It waits for both servers to upload a pair (at most 30 s), then discards\n1 s of start-up samples, then measures for `seconds`."},"342":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-71","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#cross-origin-isolation","content":"The dev server sends `Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin` and\n`Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp`. This makes the page\ncross-origin isolated, so `performance.now()` keeps a 5 µs resolution in\nChrome instead of 100 µs. Many client stages take only tens of µs, so they\nneed the fine timer. `vite preview` and the production build do not send\nthese headers."},"343":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-72","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#expected-result","content":"When the run ends, `document.body.dataset.state` is `done` or `failed`. The\nHUD shows:"},"344":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-73","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#expected-result","content":"a status line: state, engine, `crossOriginIsolated`, measured timer\nresolution;"},"345":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-74","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#expected-result","content":"one stage table per server, with `n`, p50, p90, p99 and max in ms."},"346":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-75","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#expected-result","content":"The full report is under **report JSON** at the bottom right, and in\n`window.__latencyCheckReport`. It contains:"},"347":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-76","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#expected-result","content":"`crossOriginIsolated` and `timerResolutionMs`;"},"348":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-77","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#expected-result","content":"`entries[].latency.stages[]`, where each stage has `stage`, `channel`,\n`count`, `p50`, `p90`, `p99` and `max`;"},"349":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-78","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#expected-result","content":"`errors`, `notes` and `verdict`."},"350":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-79","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#expected-result","content":"`done` means every server uploaded pairs, there were no errors, and every\nserver has `present` samples. The recorded run is in\n`client/docs/development/latency-audit.md` §9.2: headless Chromium, WebGL2\non SwiftShader, `seconds=8`, timer resolution 0.005 ms. Its p50 values:"},"351":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-80","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#expected-result","content":"Stage"},"352":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-81","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#expected-result","content":"p50"},"353":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-82","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#expected-result","content":"`transport`"},"354":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-83","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#expected-result","content":"0.015 ms"},"355":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-84","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#expected-result","content":"`queue`"},"356":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-85","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#expected-result","content":"0.005 ms or less"},"357":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-86","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#expected-result","content":"`depthRead`"},"358":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-87","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#expected-result","content":"0.10 ms"},"359":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-88","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#expected-result","content":"`upload`"},"360":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-89","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#expected-result","content":"3.17 ms"},"361":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-90","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#expected-result","content":"`draw`"},"362":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-91","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#expected-result","content":"30.5 ms"},"363":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-92","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#expected-result","content":"`present`"},"364":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-93","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#expected-result","content":"67.7 ms"},"365":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-94","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#which-stages-mean-something-on-this-page","content":"Stage"},"366":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-95","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#which-stages-mean-something-on-this-page","content":"Meaningful here?"},"367":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-96","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#which-stages-mean-something-on-this-page","content":"`transport`, `queue`, `depthRead`"},"368":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-97","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#which-stages-mean-something-on-this-page","content":"Yes. Production code."},"369":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-98","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#which-stages-mean-something-on-this-page","content":"`upload`"},"370":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-99","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#which-stages-mean-something-on-this-page","content":"Yes, for the engine in use. On SwiftShader it is software rendering."},"371":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-100","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#which-stages-mean-something-on-this-page","content":"`decode`"},"372":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-101","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#which-stages-mean-something-on-this-page","content":"No. It times the synthetic decoder, not WebCodecs."},"373":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-102","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#which-stages-mean-something-on-this-page","content":"`pairWait`"},"374":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-103","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#which-stages-mean-something-on-this-page","content":"Partly. The synthetic decoder outputs colour about 15 ms before depth, so colour `pairWait` shows that skew."},"375":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-104","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#which-stages-mean-something-on-this-page","content":"`network`, `captureToPresent`"},"376":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-105","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#which-stages-mean-something-on-this-page","content":"No. Recordings have no network, and the capture time comes from the recording's clock."},"377":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-106","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/latency#which-stages-mean-something-on-this-page","content":"`draw`, `present`, `clientTotal`"},"378":{"id":"/docs/client/developer/latency-107","page_id":"/docs/client/developer/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/developer/laten