tting-started-notes-31","page_id":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes#ports","content":"5173"},"610":{"id":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes-32","page_id":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes#ports","content":"Vite dev server"},"611":{"id":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes-33","page_id":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes#ports","content":"Fixed (`strictPort`): it fails with \"Port 5173 is already in use\" instead of picking another port. Sends `Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin` and `Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp` (for full-resolution timers in the latency check)."},"612":{"id":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes-34","page_id":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes#ports","content":"4173"},"613":{"id":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes-35","page_id":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes#ports","content":"`vite preview`"},"614":{"id":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes-36","page_id":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes#ports","content":"Vite's default preview port, without those two headers"},"615":{"id":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes-37","page_id":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes#ports","content":"The client should make no outgoing connection at startup (not verified with a network trace). It connects only to\nservers the user adds."},"616":{"id":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes-38","page_id":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes#reaching-a-server","content":"**The URL:** the user types it into the panel's \"Add server\" form. It\nmust be an absolute `https:` URL with no fragment."},"617":{"id":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes-39","page_id":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes#reaching-a-server","content":"**Certificates:**"},"618":{"id":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes-40","page_id":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes#reaching-a-server","content":"The client opens WebTransport with no options, so it does **not**\nsupport `serverCertificateHashes`."},"619":{"id":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes-41","page_id":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes#reaching-a-server","content":"The server's TLS certificate must be trusted by the browser."},"620":{"id":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes-42","page_id":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes#reaching-a-server","content":"How the server obtains or publishes its certificate is for the server\ndocumentation."},"621":{"id":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes-43","page_id":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes#reaching-a-server","content":"**Secure context:** the page itself must be one. `http://localhost:5173`\nqualifies. Opening the dev server from another machine by IP address\nover plain HTTP does not, and the repository has no HTTPS dev\nconfiguration yet."},"622":{"id":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes-44","page_id":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes#reaching-a-server","content":"**No server needed to try the client:** the \"Open recording\" form plays\n`.hevc` recordings as if they were servers. See\nPlay back .hevc recordings."},"623":{"id":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes-45","page_id":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes#not-yet-available","content":"Do not describe these as working:"},"624":{"id":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes-46","page_id":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes#not-yet-available","content":"The **camera-pose calibration screen** (a placeholder until the\nprotocol contract defines it) and **network calibration** (change\nrequest 0018). The setup workspace, depth-quantization calibration,\nplacement editing and client-local world anchors exist; see\nSetup workspace,\nCalibration and\nPlacement editing."},"625":{"id":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes-47","page_id":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes#not-yet-available","content":"**WebXR** (Phase 2)."},"626":{"id":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes-48","page_id":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/getting-started-notes#not-yet-available","content":"See `client/docs/development/ROADMAP.md`."},"627":{"id":"/docs/client","page_id":"/docs/client","type":"page","content":"Client","breadcrumbs":["HSLU OrbbecStreamer","Client"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/client"},"628":{"id":"/docs/client-0","page_id":"/docs/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client","content":"The browser client that connects to capture servers and renders their point clouds."},"629":{"id":"/docs/client-1","page_id":"/docs/client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client#what-it-is","content":"What it is"},"630":{"id":"/docs/client-2","page_id":"/docs/client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client#status","content":"Status"},"631":{"id":"/docs/client-3","page_id":"/docs/client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client#pages","content":"Pages"},"632":{"id":"/docs/client-4","page_id":"/docs/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client#what-it-is","content":"The OrbbecStreamer client is a browser application. It does three things:"},"633":{"id":"/docs/client-5","page_id":"/docs/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client#what-it-is","content":"It connects to one or more capture servers over WebTransport."},"634":{"id":"/docs/client-6","page_id":"/docs/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client#what-it-is","content":"It decodes their HEVC colour and depth streams with WebCodecs."},"635":{"id":"/docs/client-7","page_id":"/docs/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client#what-it-is","content":"It rebuilds metric point clouds on the GPU and draws every server's\nclouds in one shared Babylon.js scene, using WebGPU or falling back to\nWebGL2."},"636":{"id":"/docs/client-8","page_id":"/docs/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client#what-it-is","content":"The client lives in `client/` in the repository and runs from a Vite\ndevelopment server. See Run the dev build."},"637":{"id":"/docs/client-9","page_id":"/docs/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client#status","content":"The client works today as a thin application shell. Its **side panel** can:"},"638":{"id":"/docs/client-10","page_id":"/docs/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client#status","content":"add a server by WebTransport URL;"},"639":{"id":"/docs/client-11","page_id":"/docs/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client#status","content":"open a recording (colour `.hevc`, depth `.hevc` and a manifest) and play\nit as if it were a server;"},"640":{"id":"/docs/client-12","page_id":"/docs/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client#status","content":"show a **server card** for every connection: its status, setup lock,\ncalibration state, stream layout, frame counts, RTT and network budget,\nand the shared-update toggle;"},"641":{"id":"/docs/client-13","page_id":"/docs/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client#status","content":"take and release a server's setup lock, refresh its state, reconnect\nit, and remove it;"},