aving-setup-keeps-the-draft","content":"Leaving setup keeps the draft"},"714":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-9","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#expected-result","content":"Expected result"},"715":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-10","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"716":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-11","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#what-it-is","content":"A server's **placement** says where the server sits relative to a named\nanchor (for example a marker or a corner of the room): a translation in\nmetres and a rotation. Every client draws that server's point cloud with\nit, so a committed placement is shared by all clients."},"717":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-12","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#what-it-is","content":"The **Placement** section of the setup workspace\nedits it in two stages:"},"718":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-13","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#what-it-is","content":"**A local draft.** You change the placement in this browser. Your 3D\nview shows the draft at once, but nothing is sent to the server."},"719":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-14","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#what-it-is","content":"**Commit.** **Commit placement** sends the draft to the server. Only\nthen does it become the server's placement, with a new revision number."},"720":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-15","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#what-it-is","content":"The client never commits a draft by itself. Leaving setup, losing the\nlock or reconnecting never sends it."},"721":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-16","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#what-it-is","content":"Placements must be rigid: a translation plus a rotation. Scaling,\nshearing and mirroring are not possible."},"722":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-17","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#what-it-is","content":"Where each **anchor** sits in your 3D scene is a separate, client-local\nsetting; see World anchors."},"723":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-18","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#open-the-placement-section","content":"On the server's card, select **Set up**. The setup workspace opens and\ntakes the server's setup lock. See Setup workspace."},"724":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-19","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#open-the-placement-section","content":"Scroll to the **Placement** section, below the calibration sections."},"725":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-20","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#open-the-placement-section","content":"It shows the server's current placement:"},"726":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-21","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#open-the-placement-section","content":"**server placement:** the anchor and the revision, for example\n`anchor anchor-dev, revision 3`;"},"727":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-22","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#open-the-placement-section","content":"**translation:** for example `x 0.500 · y 0.000 · z 1.000 m`;"},"728":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-23","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#open-the-placement-section","content":"**rotation:** for example `yaw 30.0 · pitch 0.0 · roll 0.0°`."},"729":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-24","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#start-a-draft","content":"Select **Edit placement**. The client makes a draft equal to the server's\nplacement and shows:"},"730":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-25","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#start-a-draft","content":"`draft based on revision 3 · anchor anchor-dev`: the revision the draft\nstarts from. The commit sends it as the expected revision."},"731":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-26","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#start-a-draft","content":"`same as the server placement` until you change something, then\n`changed locally, not committed (the 3D view shows the draft)`."},"732":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-27","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#start-a-draft","content":"Six fields, **Move in 3D**, and the draft actions."},"733":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-28","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#start-a-draft","content":"A note: the draft is local to this browser tab and held in memory only,\nand only **Commit placement** sends it."},"734":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-29","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#edit-with-numbers","content":"The fields hold the draft pose:"},"735":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-30","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#edit-with-numbers","content":"Field"},"736":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-31","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#edit-with-numbers","content":"Unit"},"737":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-32","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#edit-with-numbers","content":"Meaning"},"738":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-33","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#edit-with-numbers","content":"**x (m)**, **y (m)**, **z (m)**"},"739":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-34","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#edit-with-numbers","content":"metres"},"740":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-35","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#edit-with-numbers","content":"Position of the server's origin relative to the anchor. +X right, +Y up, +Z forward."},"741":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-36","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#edit-with-numbers","content":"**yaw (°)**"},"742":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-37","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#edit-with-numbers","content":"degrees"},"743":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-38","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#edit-with-numbers","content":"Turn about the vertical (+Y) axis."},"744":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-39","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#edit-with-numbers","content":"**pitch (°)**"},"745":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-40","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#edit-with-numbers","content":"degrees"},"746":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-41","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#edit-with-numbers","content":"Tilt about the +X axis."},"747":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-42","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#edit-with-numbers","content":"**roll (°)**"},"748":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-43","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#edit-with-numbers","content":"degrees"},"749":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-44","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#edit-with-numbers","content":"Turn about the +Z axis."},"750":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-45","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#edit-with-numbers","content":"The rotation is applied as roll first, then pitch, then yaw\n(`R = Ry(yaw) · Rx(pitch) · Rz(roll)`). A positive yaw turns +Z towards\n+X."},"751":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-46","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#edit-with-numbers","content":"Type a number. It applies as soon as it is valid, and your 3D view\nfollows. A comma works as the decimal mark."},"752":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-47","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#edit-with-numbers","content":"**Arrow Up** and **Arrow Down** step by 0.01 m or 1°; hold **Shift**\nfor ten times that. The **−** and **+** buttons next to each field do\nthe same with the mouse."},"753":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-48","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#edit-with-numbers","content":"**Enter** applies the field. **Escape** shows the last applied values\nagain."},"754":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-49","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#edit-with-numbers","content":"An invalid entry is not applied. Its reason appears under the field\nwhen you leave it or press **Enter**, for example\n`x: \"abc\" is not a number (not applied)`. The limits are ±1000 m and\n±360°."},"755":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-50","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#edit-with-numbers","content":"While a field has focus, the fields keep exactly what you typed. When you\nleave the field or press **Enter**, they show the applied pose rounded to\n1 mm and 0.1° and in standard ranges:"},"756":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-51","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#edit-with-numbers","content":"**pitch** from -90° to 90°, **yaw** and **roll** from -180° to 180°;"},"757":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-52","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#edit-with-numbers","content":"so yaw 200 is shown as -160, and pitch 100 with yaw 10 is shown as\npitch 80, yaw -170, roll 180. Both are the same rotation you typed;\nnothing moves."},"758":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-53","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#edit-with-numbers","content":"At pitch exactly ±90°, yaw and roll turn about the same axis. The\nclient then shows roll 0 and puts the whole turn in yaw."},"759":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-54","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#edit-with-numbers","content":"A change from elsewhere (the 3D handle, a rebase, the server's placement)\nreplaces the fields at once, in the same standard form."},"760":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-55","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#edit-in-3d","content":"Tick **Move in 3D (drag the handle on the server's cloud)**. A handle\nappears at the server's origin in the 3D view."},"761":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-56","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#edit-in-3d","content":"Under **handle**, choose **translate** (arrows: move along an axis) or\n**rotate** (rings: turn about an axis)."},"762":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-57","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#edit-in-3d","content":"Drag an arrow or a ring. The draft and the fields follow the drag, and\nthe section shows `changed locally, not committed (the 3D view shows the draft)`.\nNothing is sent until you select **Commit placement**."},"763":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-58","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#edit-in-3d","content":"Typing in the fields moves the handle too. The handle only translates and\nrotates; it has no scale control. Untick **Move in 3D** to remove it. It\nis also removed when you discard the draft or select **Commit placement**,\nand the checkbox shows `a placement commit is in progress` until the\ncommit is settled."},"764":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-59","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#edit-in-3d","content":"Verified on 2026-09-28 in headless Chromium 153 with software rendering\n(SwiftShader), on both WebGL2 and WebGPU: dragging a translate arrow moved\nx (to 0.104 m), and dragging a rotate ring turned yaw (to about -45°),\nwith nothing sent. It has not been tried on real GPU hardware yet."},"765":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-60","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#commit-discard-or-rebase","content":"**Commit placement (expected revision N)** sends the draft to the server\nwith `N`, the revision the draft started from. The protocol names this\nexpected revision but does not define exactly what a server does with\nit; the expected behaviour, and what the mock server does, is to accept\nthe commit only while its placement is still at revision `N`. You need\nthe setup lock, which the setup workspace holds."},"766":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-61","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#commit-discard-or-rebase","content":"**Discard draft** drops the draft. Your 3D view shows the server's\nplacement again. Nothing is sent."},"767":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-62","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#commit-discard-or-rebase","content":"**Rebase on server placement (revision M)** appears when the draft is\nstale (see Troubleshooting). It keeps your pose and\nmakes revision `M` the base, so you can commit."},"768":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-63","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#commit-discard-or-rebase","content":"While a commit is on its way, the fields are read-only and the button\nshows `in progress`."},"769":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-64","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#commit-discard-or-rebase","content":"Results appear under the section:"},"770":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-65","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#commit-discard-or-rebase","content":"Result"},"771":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-66","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#commit-discard-or-rebase","content":"Meaning"},"772":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-67","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#commit-discard-or-rebase","content":"`Commit placement: sent with expected revision 3; waiting for the server…`"},"773":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-68","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#commit-discard-or-rebase","content":"Sent, no answer yet."},"774":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-69","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#commit-discard-or-rebase","content":"`Commit placement: accepted (expected revision 3); waiting for the new server placement.`"},"775":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-70","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#commit-discard-or-rebase","content":"The server accepted it; the new placement is on its way."},"776":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-71","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#commit-discard-or-rebase","content":"`Commit placement: accepted; the server placement is now revision 4.`"},"777":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-72","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#commit-discard-or-rebase","content":"Done. The draft is cleared, and every client draws the new placement."},"778":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-73","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#commit-discard-or-rebase","content":"`Commit placement rejected (<code>): <message>. …`"},"779":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-74","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#commit-discard-or-rebase","content":"The server refused it. The draft is kept."},"780":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-75","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#commit-discard-or-rebase","content":"`Commit placement failed (<reason>): <message>. The draft is kept.`"},"781":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-76","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#commit-discard-or-rebase","content":"No answer from the server (for example `timeout`), or the connection was lost."},"782":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-77","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#commit-discard-or-rebase","content":"When a commit is not possible, the button is unavailable and says why\nunder it (for example `committing a placement needs the setup lock`), so\nnothing is sent."},"783":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-78","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#leaving-setup-keeps-the-draft","content":"The draft belongs to this browser tab, to this server's card and to the\nserver it was made for. It is held in memory only. It is kept:"},"784":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-79","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#leaving-setup-keeps-the-draft","content":"when you leave setup: it comes back the next time you select **Set up**;"},"785":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-80","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#leaving-setup-keeps-the-draft","content":"when you are forced out of setup, or the connection drops and\nreconnects to the same server."},"786":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-81","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#leaving-setup-keeps-the-draft","content":"It is lost when you select **Discard draft**, when a commit of it is\napplied, when you select **Remove** on the server's card, and when you\n**reload or close the tab**. If the card's connection reaches a different\nserver after a reconnect, the draft is dropped with the notice\n`The connection now reaches server <new>, not <old>: the placement draft for <old> was dropped… Nothing was sent.`\nA draft is never sent without **Commit placement**."},"787":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-82","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#leaving-setup-keeps-the-draft","content":"Your 3D view shows the draft only while the setup workspace for that\nserver is open. Outside it, every server is drawn at its committed\nplacement."},"788":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-83","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#expected-result","content":"While you edit, only your 3D view moves the server's cloud. Other\nclients and the server still have revision `N`."},"789":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-84","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#expected-result","content":"After **Commit placement**, the section shows\n`Commit placement: accepted; the server placement is now revision N+1.`,\nthe server placement line shows the new revision, and every connected\nclient draws the cloud at the new placement."},"790":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-85","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#expected-result","content":"The cloud may freeze or disappear for a moment after a commit: the\nserver restarts its streams for the new placement, and the client never\ndraws a frame with the placement of another revision."},"791":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-86","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"Symptom"},"792":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-87","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"Cause"},"793":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-88","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"What to do"},"794":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-89","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"`stale: the server placement changed to revision M since this draft was based on revision N. …`, and **Commit placement** is unavailable with `the server placement changed (revision N -> M); discard or rebase the draft`"},"795":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-90","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"Another operator committed a placement after you started your draft."},"796":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-91","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"Select **Rebase on server placement (revision M)** to keep your pose on top of the new revision, then commit. Or select **Discard draft** and start again from the new placement."},"797":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-92","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"`Commit placement rejected (stale-revision): expectedRevision N is not the current placement revision M. …`"},"798":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-93","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"The server's placement moved before your commit arrived (a rare race: normally the client blocks a stale commit first). `stale-revision` is the mock server's code; a real server may use another."},"799":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-94","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"Rebase, then commit again."},"800":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-95","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"**Commit placement** says `committing a placement needs the setup lock`"},"801":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-96","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"This client does not hold the lock: you were forced out of setup, or the lock expired."},"802":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-97","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"Select **Enter setup again**. The draft is still there."},"803":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-98","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"**Commit placement** says `waiting for the server state to refresh`"},"804":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-99","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"The client is fetching a fresh copy of the server's state."},"805":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-100","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"Wait a moment."},"806":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-101","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"**Commit placement** says `the draft equals the server placement`"},"807":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-102","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"There is nothing to commit."},"808":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-103","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"Change a field, or select **Discard draft**."},"809":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-104","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"`Not applied: anchorFromServer must be rigid (§9): …`"},"810":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-105","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"A pose with scale, shear or mirroring was refused. The fields and the handle cannot produce one, so this is a bug."},"811":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-106","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"Report it with the values you entered."},"812":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-107","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"**Edit placement** says `no server placement known yet`"},"813":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-108","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"The client has not received the server's state yet."},"814":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-109","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"Wait until the card shows a live status."},"815":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-110","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"**Edit placement** says `the server placement is not rigid`"},"816":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-111","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"The server sent a placement with scale or shear."},"817":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-112","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"Fix the placement on the server side."},"818":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-113","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"`Move in 3D is not available: no rendering backend (§16): nothing is drawn`"},"819":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-114","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"The browser has no WebGPU or WebGL2, so there is no 3D view."},"820":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-115","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"Edit with the fields; see Browser requirements."},"821":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-116","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"`Move in 3D is not available: the server is not drawn in this session`"},"822":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-117","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"The server's cloud is not in the 3D view right now (the session is still starting, or the card shows a conflict)."},"823":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-118","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"Wait until the card is live, then tick **Move in 3D** again."},"824":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-119","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"**Move in 3D** shows `a placement commit is in progress`"},"825":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-120","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"A commit is on its way; the draft cannot change until it is settled."},"826":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-121","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"Wait for the result."},"827":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-122","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"The draft is gone after a reload"},"828":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-123","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"Drafts are held in memory only."},"829":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-124","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"Start again with **Edit placement**. Commit drafts you want to keep."},"830":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-125","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"`The connection now reaches server <new>, not <old>: …`"},"831":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-126","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"After a reconnect, the card reaches a different server, so the old draft no longer applies. Nothing was sent."},"832":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-127","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"Check the card's address; start a new draft if needed."},"833":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-128","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"After leaving a field, yaw, pitch or roll show other numbers than you typed (yaw 200 shows -160; pitch 100 shows 80 with yaw and roll changed by 180)"},"834":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-129","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"The fields show the same rotation in standard ranges once you leave them."},"835":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-130","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"Expected; the placement is unchanged."},"836":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-131","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"At pitch ±90°, roll jumps to 0 and yaw changes"},"837":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-132","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"At ±90° pitch, yaw and roll turn about the same axis, so the client reports the whole turn as yaw."},"838":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-133","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"Expected. The placement itself is unchanged."},"839":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-134","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"A recording's placement cannot be committed"},"840":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-135","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"Recordings refuse the setup lock (`unsupported-by-file-source`)."},"841":{"id":"/docs/client/placement-editing-136","page_id":"/docs/client/placement-editing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/placement-editing#troubleshooting","content":"Edit the placement in the recording's manifest instead; see Play back .hevc recordings."},"842":{"id":"/docs/client/playback","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","type":"page","content":"Play back .hevc recordings","breadcrumbs":["HSLU OrbbecStreamer","Client"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/playback"},"843":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-0","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback","content":"Play a colour and a depth .hevc file through the full client pipeline, without a server."},"844":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-1","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/playback#what-it-is","content":"What it is"},"845":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-2","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/playback#file-requirements","content":"File requirements"},"846":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-3","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/playback#how-to-do-it","content":"How to do it"},"847":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-4","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/playback#1-get-two-compatible-files","content":"1\\. Get two compatible files"},"848":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-5","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/playback#2-write-the-manifest","content":"2\\. Write the manifest"},"849":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-6","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/playback#3-open-it-in-the-client","content":"3\\. Open it in the client"},"850":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-7","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/playback#expected-result","content":"Expected result"},"851":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-8","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/playback#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"852":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-9","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/playback#nothing-decodes-decoded-pairs-stays-0","content":"Nothing decodes (`decoded pairs` stays 0)"},"853":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-10","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-under-the-open-recording-form","content":"Messages under the Open recording form"},"854":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-11","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"Messages on the card"},"855":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-12","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/playback#other-problems","content":"Other problems"},"856":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-13","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#what-it-is","content":"A recording is three files:"},"857":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-14","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#what-it-is","content":"a colour `.hevc` file;"},"858":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-15","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#what-it-is","content":"a depth `.hevc` file;"},"859":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-16","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#what-it-is","content":"a recording manifest (`.json`) that describes the camera, the depth range\nand the frame rate."},"860":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-17","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#what-it-is","content":"The client plays a recording through its normal pipeline: connection,\nkeyframe gating, WebCodecs decoding, colour/depth pairing and point-cloud\nrendering. A simulated server inside the browser stands in for a capture\nserver, so no server and no camera are needed."},"861":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-18","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#what-it-is","content":"What the simulated server does:"},"862":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-19","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#what-it-is","content":"It sends one colour frame and one depth frame per tick, at the manifest's\n`frameRate`. The `.hevc` files have no timing of their own."},"863":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-20","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#what-it-is","content":"Frame *n* of the colour file is paired with frame *n* of the depth file."},"864":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-21","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#what-it-is","content":"With `\"loop\": true` it starts again at the first frame after the last one.\nWith `\"loop\": false` it stops after the last frame."},"865":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-22","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#what-it-is","content":"A recording has no setup to change. Lock, calibration and placement\nrequests are refused with the code `unsupported-by-file-source`."},"866":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-23","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#file-requirements","content":"The client checks all of these when you open the recording. The exact\nmessages are listed under Troubleshooting."},"867":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-24","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#file-requirements","content":"Both `.hevc` files:"},"868":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-25","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#file-requirements","content":"are raw H.265 Annex-B streams, where NAL units are separated by\n`00 00 01` or `00 00 00 01` start codes. MP4, MKV and other containers are\nnot accepted;"},"869":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-26","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#file-requirements","content":"start with a keyframe (an IDR, CRA or BLA picture) that carries the VPS,\nSPS and PPS;"},"870":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-27","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#file-requirements","content":"carry the VPS, SPS and PPS again in every keyframe;"},"871":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-28","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#file-requirements","content":"keep one format for the whole file: the SPS never changes the picture\nsize, profile, level or bit depth;"},"872":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-29","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#file-requirements","content":"use the HEVC Main or Main10 profile;"},"873":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-30","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#file-requirements","content":"contain only whole pictures: the file does not start in the middle of a\npicture and does not end with parameter sets alone."},"874":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-31","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#file-requirements","content":"The pair of files:"},"875":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-32","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#file-requirements","content":"has the same number of frames (access units) in colour and in depth;"},"876":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-33","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#file-requirements","content":"has keyframes at the same frame positions in colour and in depth."},"877":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-34","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#file-requirements","content":"The depth file:"},"878":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-35","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#file-requirements","content":"is Main10, with 10-bit luma and 4:2:0 chroma. Each depth pixel is a 10-bit\ncode that the client turns into millimetres with the manifest's lookup\ntable."},"879":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-36","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#file-requirements","content":"Frame size:"},"880":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-37","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#file-requirements","content":"The coded size comes from the SPS. By default the usable (logical) region\nis the SPS conformance window, which is the whole picture when the encoder\ndid not crop."},"881":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-38","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#file-requirements","content":"Each camera tile must fit inside that region."},"882":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-39","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#file-requirements","content":"Each camera's tile must have the size given by its `depthIntrinsics` width\nand height."},"883":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-40","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#file-requirements","content":"Colour and depth tiles of a camera must have the same size."},"884":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-41","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#file-requirements","content":"Use no B-frames. With B-frames the keyframe check failed in our tests. The\nfiles must also be small enough to hold in memory: the browser reads both\nfiles whole."},"885":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-42","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#1-get-two-compatible-files","content":"Use a colour and a depth recording that meet the requirements above."},"886":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-43","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#1-get-two-compatible-files","content":"To try the feature without a recording, generate a synthetic pair of test\npatterns with FFmpeg and libx265 (tested with FFmpeg 8 and Node 24). The\n\"depth\" file here is a colour test pattern encoded as Main10, so the point\ncloud it produces is meaningless. It only shows that playback works."},"887":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-44","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#1-get-two-compatible-files","content":"What the options do:"},"888":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-45","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#1-get-two-compatible-files","content":"`keyint=30:min-keyint=30:scenecut=0` puts a keyframe at exactly every\n30th frame in both files, so the keyframes line up."},"889":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-46","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#1-get-two-compatible-files","content":"`bframes=0` turns off B-frames."},"890":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-47","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#1-get-two-compatible-files","content":"`repeat-headers=1` puts the VPS, SPS and PPS in every keyframe."},"891":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-48","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#1-get-two-compatible-files","content":"`yuv420p10le` makes the depth file Main10 with 10-bit 4:2:0."},"892":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-49","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#2-write-the-manifest","content":"The manifest includes a depth lookup table with exactly 1024 entries, so the\neasiest way to write it is with a script. Save this as `make-manifest.mjs`\nin the same folder."},"893":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-50","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#2-write-the-manifest","content":"It describes one 640x576 camera. Replace the camera values with your own\nwhere needed:"},"894":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-51","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#2-write-the-manifest","content":"`depthIntrinsics` (`fx`, `fy`, `cx`, `cy`);"},"895":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-52","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#2-write-the-manifest","content":"`MIN_MM` and `MAX_MM`;"},"896":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-53","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#2-write-the-manifest","content":"`frameRate`."},"897":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-54","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#2-write-the-manifest","content":"Run it:"},"898":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-55","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#2-write-the-manifest","content":"It prints `wrote manifest.json`."},"899":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-56","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#2-write-the-manifest","content":"Manifest fields:"},"900":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-57","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#2-write-the-manifest","content":"Field"},"901":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-58","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#2-write-the-manifest","content":"Meaning"},"902":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-59","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#2-write-the-manifest","content":"`serverId`, `serverName`"},"903":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-60","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#2-write-the-manifest","content":"Identity of the simulated server. The server card is titled with `serverName`. Two open recordings with the same `serverId` conflict."},"904":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-61","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#2-write-the-manifest","content":"`streamLayout`"},"905":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-62","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#2-write-the-manifest","content":"`per-camera` (one bundle per camera) or `concatenated` (exactly one bundle whose picture holds every camera as a tile)."},"906":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-63","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#2-write-the-manifest","content":"`frameRate`"},"907":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-64","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#2-write-the-manifest","content":"Frames per second on both channels, above 0 and at most 1000."},"908":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-65","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#2-write-the-manifest","content":"`loop`"},"909":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-66","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#2-write-the-manifest","content":"`true`: restart at the first frame. `false`: stop after the last frame."},"910":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-67","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#2-write-the-manifest","content":"`startCaptureTimeUs`"},"911":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-68","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#2-write-the-manifest","content":"Capture timestamp of the first frame, in microseconds. A number, or a decimal string. At most 2^53 − 1."},"912":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-69","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#2-write-the-manifest","content":"`cameras`"},"913":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-70","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#2-write-the-manifest","content":"Camera geometry, one entry per camera: `cameraId`, `label`, `depthIntrinsics` (`width`, `height`, `fx`, `fy`, `cx`, `cy` in pixels), `serverFromDepthCamera` (a rigid 4×4 matrix, 16 numbers, column-major), `connected`."},"914":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-71","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#2-write-the-manifest","content":"`quantization`"},"915":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-72","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#2-write-the-manifest","content":"The depth profile: range in millimetres, the fixed codes 0/1/2/1022/1023, and `reconstructionLutMm`, 1024 millimetre values. Entry 0 must be 0, entries 1 and 2 must equal `minimumDepthMm`, entries 1022 and 1023 must equal `maximumDepthMm`, and entries 2 to 1022 must never decrease."},"916":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-73","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#2-write-the-manifest","content":"`placement`"},"917":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-74","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#2-write-the-manifest","content":"`anchorId`, `anchorFromServer` (a rigid 4×4 matrix) and `revision`."},"918":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-75","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#2-write-the-manifest","content":"`calibrationRevision`, `metadataRevision`"},"919":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-76","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#2-write-the-manifest","content":"Non-negative integers. Any value works for a recording."},"920":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-77","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#2-write-the-manifest","content":"`bundles`"},"921":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-78","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#2-write-the-manifest","content":"One entry per bundle: `bundleId`, `cameraIds`, `tiles` (`cameraId`, `x`, `y`, `width`, `height`, relative to the logical region), and `color` / `depth`, each `{ \"file\": \"<key>\" }`, optionally with `\"logical\": { \"x\", \"y\", \"width\", \"height\" }` to override the logical region."},"922":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-79","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#2-write-the-manifest","content":"The `file` values are keys, not paths. When you open the recording, the\ncolour file you pick is used for the `color.file` key and the depth file for\nthe `depth.file` key, whatever the picked files are called. The \"Open\nrecording\" form opens exactly one colour and one depth file, so every bundle\nmust name the same `color.file`, every bundle the same `depth.file`, and the\ntwo keys must differ."},"923":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-80","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#3-open-it-in-the-client","content":"Start the client:"},"924":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-81","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#3-open-it-in-the-client","content":"Open http\\://localhost:5173 in a browser that can decode HEVC (see\nTroubleshooting)."},"925":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-82","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#3-open-it-in-the-client","content":"In the side panel, under **Open recording**, choose the files:"},"926":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-83","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#3-open-it-in-the-client","content":"**Colour .hevc**: `colour.hevc`"},"927":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-84","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#3-open-it-in-the-client","content":"**Depth .hevc (Main10)**: `depth.hevc`"},"928":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-85","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#3-open-it-in-the-client","content":"**Manifest .json**: `manifest.json`"},"929":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-86","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#3-open-it-in-the-client","content":"Select **Play recording**."},"930":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-87","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#3-open-it-in-the-client","content":"The form checks the manifest first; the `.hevc` files are read only if it is\nvalid. The bitstream checks run next, and any problem they find appears on\nthe new server card."},"931":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-88","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#expected-result","content":"A new server card appears under **Servers** (see\nRead the server card):"},"932":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-89","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#expected-result","content":"the status label reads `streaming`;"},"933":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-90","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#expected-result","content":"the title is the manifest's `serverName` (`Recorded rig`);"},"934":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-91","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#expected-result","content":"the next line reads\n`serverId: recorded-rig · recording file://recorded-rig`;"},"935":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-92","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#expected-result","content":"the layout has one row per bundle, for example\n`bundle-cam0: 1 camera, available; ready, drawing` once frames reach the\nrenderer (`ready, no frame yet` before that);"},"936":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-93","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#expected-result","content":"`decoded pairs` and `uploaded` keep increasing while the recording plays."},"937":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-94","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#expected-result","content":"The point cloud should appear in the viewport. The whole pipeline is built\nand tested, but decoding has not yet been checked in a real desktop browser\nwith HEVC support. That check is tracked in\n`client/docs/development/ROADMAP.md` (Phase 2, \"Check with real decoded HEVC frames in a browser\")."},"938":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-95","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#expected-result","content":"With `\"loop\": true` it loops\nforever. With `\"loop\": false`, frames stop after the last one and the card\nstays connected. Select **Remove** to close it. A recording never\nreconnects by itself. To replay it, select **Remove** on its card, then\nopen it again."},"939":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-96","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#nothing-decodes-decoded-pairs-stays-0","content":"The browser cannot decode HEVC. This is a known limitation of some browsers\nand platforms, and the client then works for control and setup only. You\nsee one of these:"},"940":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-97","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#nothing-decodes-decoded-pairs-stays-0","content":"on the card: `Setup and control only: this browser lacks HEVC colour decoding and HEVC Main10 depth decoding.`;"},"941":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-98","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#nothing-decodes-decoded-pairs-stays-0","content":"at the top of the panel: `decoders: WebCodecs VideoDecoder is unavailable: control and setup only (§16).`"},"942":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-99","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#nothing-decodes-decoded-pairs-stays-0","content":"Use a browser that can decode HEVC and HEVC Main10, usually through GPU\nvideo decoding. In our one test so far, headless Chromium on Linux could\ndecode neither."},"943":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-100","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-under-the-open-recording-form","content":"Message"},"944":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-101","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-under-the-open-recording-form","content":"Cause and fix"},"945":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-102","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-under-the-open-recording-form","content":"`choose the colour .hevc file` (or depth, or `choose the recording manifest (.json)`)"},"946":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-103","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-under-the-open-recording-form","content":"A file was not picked. Pick all three."},"947":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-104","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-under-the-open-recording-form","content":"`manifest is not JSON: …`"},"948":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-105","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-under-the-open-recording-form","content":"The manifest file is not valid JSON. Regenerate it with the script."},"949":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-106","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-under-the-open-recording-form","content":"`manifest: <field>: <problem>`, for example `manifest: placement: Required` or `manifest: frameRate: Number must be greater than 0`"},"950":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-107","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-under-the-open-recording-form","content":"A manifest field is missing or has the wrong type or range. See the field table."},"951":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-108","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-under-the-open-recording-form","content":"`manifest names 2 colour files; this form opens exactly one` (or depth)"},"952":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-109","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-under-the-open-recording-form","content":"Bundles name different files. Give every bundle the same `color.file` and the same `depth.file`."},"953":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-110","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-under-the-open-recording-form","content":"`manifest uses '<key>' for both colour and depth`"},"954":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-111","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-under-the-open-recording-form","content":"`color.file` and `depth.file` are equal. Use two different keys."},"955":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-112","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-under-the-open-recording-form","content":"`colour file '<name>' is empty` (or depth)"},"956":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-113","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-under-the-open-recording-form","content":"The picked file has 0 bytes."},"957":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-114","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-under-the-open-recording-form","content":"`could not read the files: …`"},"958":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-115","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-under-the-open-recording-form","content":"The browser could not read a picked file. Pick it again."},"959":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-116","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"When the bitstream checks fail, the card shows status `error`, the title\n`file://invalid-recording`, and the problems as a list. Nothing plays."},"960":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-117","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"Message"},"961":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-118","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"Cause and fix"},"962":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-119","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"`bundle '<id>' color: malformed Annex-B (no-start-code) …`"},"963":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-120","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"The file is not a raw Annex-B stream, for example an MP4. Extract the raw stream, for example `ffmpeg -i in.mp4 -c:v copy -bsf:v hevc_mp4toannexb out.hevc`."},"964":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-121","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"`… malformed Annex-B (leading-garbage) …`"},"965":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-122","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"Bytes before the first start code. The file is not raw Annex-B, or it is cut at the start."},"966":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-123","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"`… malformed Annex-B (truncated-nal-header / forbidden-zero-bit / invalid-temporal-id / truncated-slice-header) …`"},"967":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-124","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"Corrupt or truncated NAL units. Re-encode or re-export the file."},"968":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-125","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"`… malformed Annex-B (access-unit-without-picture) …`"},"969":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-126","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"A group of NAL units has no picture, for example parameter sets at the very end. Re-export the file."},"970":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-127","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"`… malformed Annex-B (missing-first-slice) …`"},"971":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-128","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"The file starts in the middle of a picture. Cut it at a picture boundary."},"972":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-129","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"`… access unit 0 must be a keyframe carrying VPS, SPS and PPS`"},"973":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-130","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"The file does not start with a keyframe that carries the parameter sets. Cut it at a keyframe, or re-encode."},"974":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-131","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"`… keyframe access unit <n> does not carry VPS, SPS and PPS`"},"975":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-132","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"A later keyframe lacks the parameter sets. Encode with the parameter sets repeated (x265: `repeat-headers=1`)."},"976":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-133","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"`… access unit <n>: SPS: …`"},"977":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-134","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"The SPS cannot be read. The file is corrupt or uses syntax the client does not parse."},"978":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-135","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"`… HEVC profile_idc <n> is neither Main nor Main10`"},"979":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-136","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"Another HEVC profile, such as 4:4:4 or 12-bit. Re-encode as Main (colour) or Main10 (depth)."},"980":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-137","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"`… the SPS in access unit <n> changes the stream format`"},"981":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-138","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"The size, profile, level or bit depth changes mid-file. Split the file there, or re-encode."},"982":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-139","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"`bundle '<id>': colour has <a> access units, depth has <b>; a frame set needs one of each`"},"983":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-140","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"The two files have different frame counts. Trim them to the same frames."},"984":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-141","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"`bundle '<id>': keyframes are not aligned at access unit <n> …`"},"985":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-142","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"Keyframes are at different positions in the two files. Encode both with the same fixed keyframe interval, no scene-cut keyframes and no B-frames (x265: `keyint=30:min-keyint=30:scenecut=0:bframes=0`)."},"986":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-143","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"`snapshot: bundle '<id>' depth bitstream has 8-bit luma, §8 needs 10` together with `snapshot: depth channel must use HEVC Main10, got 'main'`"},"987":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-144","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"The depth file is 8-bit Main, or the colour and depth files were picked the other way round."},"988":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-145","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"`snapshot: … depth bitstream has chroma_format_idc <n>, expected 4:2:0`"},"989":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-146","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"Depth must be 4:2:0. Re-encode with `yuv420p10le`."},"990":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-147","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"`snapshot: Camera '<id>' depth tile is <w>x<h> but its intrinsics declare <w>x<h>`"},"991":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-148","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"The tile size and the camera's `depthIntrinsics` size differ. Make them equal."},"992":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-149","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"`snapshot: … tile 0 (camera '<id>') extends past the <w>x<h> logical image`"},"993":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-150","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"A tile does not fit the picture. Check the tile and the picture size."},"994":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-151","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"`snapshot: Per-camera … tile for '<id>' must cover the full logical image`"},"995":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-152","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"With `per-camera`, the single tile must be the whole picture."},"996":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-153","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"`snapshot: Per-camera layout must expose one bundle per camera …` or `snapshot: Concatenated layout must expose exactly one bundle …`"},"997":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-154","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"The bundle count does not fit `streamLayout`."},"998":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-155","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"`snapshot: quantization: …`"},"999":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-156","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"The depth lookup table breaks a rule (see `quantization` in the field table). Regenerate it with the script."},"1000":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-157","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"`startCaptureTimeUs … cannot be sent in control JSON`"},"1001":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-158","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#messages-on-the-card","content":"Use a value of at most 9007199254740991."},"1002":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-159","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#other-problems","content":"**`conflict: server <serverId> is already rendered by …`**: the same\nrecording, or another source with the same `serverId`, is already open.\nRemove the other card, or give the manifest a different `serverId`."},"1003":{"id":"/docs/client/playback-160","page_id":"/docs/client/playback","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/playback#other-problems","content":"**Playback runs too fast or too slow**: `frameRate` in the manifest sets\nthe speed. Set it to the rate the files were recorded at."},"1004":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","type":"page","content":"Read the server card","breadcrumbs":["HSLU OrbbecStreamer","Client"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/server-card"},"1005":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-0","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card","content":"What each line of a server card means, what its actions do, and how to fix a refused lock, stale metadata or a lost connection."},"1006":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-1","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/server-card#what-it-is","content":"What it is"},"1007":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-2","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/server-card#how-to-use-it","content":"How to use it"},"1008":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-3","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/server-card#header","content":"Header"},"1009":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-4","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"Fields"},"1010":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-5","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/server-card#actions","content":"Actions"},"1011":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-6","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/server-card#status-labels","content":"Status labels"},"1012":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-7","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/server-card#expected-result","content":"Expected result"},"1013":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-8","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/server-card#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"1014":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-9","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#what-it-is","content":"Every server you add, and every recording you open, gets a **server card**\nin the side panel under **Servers**. The card shows that server's state as\nthis client sees it, and has the actions for it: open the setup workspace,\ntake or release the setup lock, refresh the state, reconnect, and remove."},"1015":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-10","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#what-it-is","content":"The card refreshes on every state change, and every 0.5 s for the lease\ncountdown, the RTT and the frame counters."},"1016":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-11","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#header","content":"**Status label:** one word derived from the server's state. See\nStatus labels."},"1017":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-12","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#header","content":"**Title:** the server's name, or the URL until the server has answered."},"1018":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-13","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#header","content":"**Notes under the header**, shown only when they apply:"},"1019":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-14","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#header","content":"`waiting for the camera-pose calibration; the server accepts it without other setup`:\nthe status is `needs-setup`, and the server is waiting for its\ncamera-pose calibration, which it will accept without other setup."},"1020":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-15","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#header","content":"`resynchronising: waiting for a full snapshot`: the client saw an\nunexpected update and is fetching the server's full state."},"1021":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-16","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#header","content":"`reconnect scheduled`: the session was lost and the client will try\nagain by itself."},"1022":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-17","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#header","content":"**Id line:** `serverId: …` (or `serverId: not known yet`), then the\nsource:"},"1023":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-18","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#header","content":"`webtransport https://capture-01.local:4433/orbbec` for a server;"},"1024":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-19","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#header","content":"`recording file://<serverId>` for a recording."},"1025":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-20","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#header","content":"**Compatibility line**, shown only when something is missing:"},"1026":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-21","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#header","content":"`Setup and control only: this browser lacks HEVC Main10 depth decoding.`\n(or colour decoding, or a WebGPU or WebGL2 backend): this browser\ncannot decode or render the server's streams. The card and its lock\nstill work. See\nBrowser requirements."},"1027":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-22","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#header","content":"`Protocol version mismatch; cannot connect.`: the server speaks\nanother major protocol version. The client closes the session and\ndoes not retry."},"1028":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-23","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#header","content":"**Conflict**, shown when another card already shows the same server id:\n`conflict: server capture-01 is already rendered by entry-1; this entry is disconnected`."},"1029":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-24","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#header","content":"**Last close:** why the last session ended, for example\n`last close: transport error: …`."},"1030":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-25","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#header","content":"**Source issues:** a list of problems when a recording cannot be opened.\nSee Play back .hevc recordings."},"1031":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-26","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"The lock, calibration and layout fields show `not known (not connected)`\nwhile there is no live session."},"1032":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-27","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"Field"},"1033":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-28","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"What it shows"},"1034":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-29","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"**lock**"},"1035":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-30","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"`unlocked`; `held by this client, expires in 12 s`; or `held by Client A (client-…), last announced expiry in 9 s` (the other client's name and id)."},"1036":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-31","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"**calibration**"},"1037":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-32","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"One row per kind: `camera-pose`, `depth-quantization` and `network`, each with its state (`missing`, `valid`, `stale`, `running` or `failed`), its revision, and the server's message if any. For example `camera-pose: valid, revision 3`."},"1038":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-33","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"**layout**"},"1039":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-34","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"The stream layout (`concatenated` or `per-camera`) and the bundle count, then one row per bundle: its camera count, its availability, and its render status."},"1040":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-35","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"**counts**"},"1041":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-36","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"`this session: decoded pairs N · uploaded N · dropped N · streams N`."},"1042":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-37","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"**network**"},"1043":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-38","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"The minimum round-trip time from clock sync (`min RTT 0.42 ms`), and the server's network budget."},"1044":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-39","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"**shared updates**"},"1045":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-40","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"The **Receive shared updates** checkbox, and a stale-metadata notice when one applies."},"1046":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-41","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"**Lock expiry.** The server sends the expiry in its own clock. The card\nconverts it into a countdown with the clock offset measured by clock\nsync. Until clock sync has a result, it shows the raw server time\ninstead, for example\n`expires at server time 16.000 s (clock offset not known yet)`. When the\ncountdown reaches zero before the server has announced the change, it\nshows `expiry time reached, waiting for the server`. While this client\nholds the lock, it renews it every 5 s, so the countdown restarts from\n15 s."},"1047":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-42","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"**Another client's lock** shows the expiry the server **last announced**,\nfor example `last announced expiry in 9 s`. The holder also renews every\n5 s, but this client learns the new expiry only if the server announces\nthe lock state again after each renewal. That re-announcement is the\nclient's proposal in change request 0008, not yet part of the protocol\ncontract. When the announced time has passed, the card shows\n`expiry passed as last announced; the server may have renewed it`: the\nlock may still be held, and the lock line changes only when the server\nannounces it."},"1048":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-43","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"**Calibration rows** are highlighted when a kind has `failed`, or when\n`camera-pose` or `depth-quantization` is not `valid` (and not\n`running`): the server cannot stream until those two are valid. The\n`network` kind is per client and never blocks streaming."},"1049":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-44","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"**Bundle rows**, for example\n`bundle-cam0: 1 camera, available; ready, drawing`:"},"1050":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-45","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"Availability: `available` or `unavailable`, then `, paused` if the\nserver paused the bundle, then the server's reason, if any. Before the\nserver has announced it: `availability not announced`."},"1051":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-46","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"Render status:"},"1052":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-47","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"`ready, drawing`"},"1053":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-48","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"`ready, no frame yet`"},"1054":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-49","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"`rendering incompatible (…): …`"},"1055":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-50","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"`metadata invalid (…): …`"},"1056":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-51","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"`upload error: …`"},"1057":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-52","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"`no render status yet`"},"1058":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-53","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"The row is highlighted when the bundle is unavailable or paused, or its\nrender status is a problem."},"1059":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-54","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"**Counts** belong to the current session, from its handshake on:"},"1060":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-55","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"\"decoded pairs\" counts matched colour and depth frames."},"1061":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-56","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"\"uploaded\" counts pairs sent to the GPU."},"1062":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-57","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"\"dropped\" counts pairs decoded but not drawn."},"1063":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-58","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"\"streams\" counts the media streams open now."},"1064":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-59","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"Decoded pairs equal uploaded plus dropped, give or take the pairs still\non their way to the GPU. After a disconnect the card keeps the last\nsession's counts. A reconnect starts them from zero, and they stay at 0\nuntil the new session's first frames arrive. The bundle row shows\n`ready, no frame yet` until then."},"1065":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-60","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"**Network budget:** `no budget yet` until the server sends one. After\nthat it reads, for example,\n`active 40.0 Mbit/s, server maximum 100.0 Mbit/s, safe for this client 35.0 Mbit/s, network compatible`:"},"1066":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-61","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"\"active\" is the budget the server currently applies;"},"1067":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-62","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"\"server maximum\" is the server's own limit;"},"1068":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-63","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"\"safe for this client\" is 70 % of the throughput measured for this\nclient;"},"1069":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-64","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"`not network compatible (below the useful budget)`, highlighted, means\nthis client is too slow to be counted in the budget."},"1070":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-65","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"**Shared updates.** Calibration results and placement changes are\n*shared updates*: the server sends them to every client that asked for\nthem."},"1071":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-66","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"The checkbox **Receive shared updates (calibration results, placement)**\nis on by default."},"1072":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-67","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"Turning it off stops them at once. Turning it on takes effect when the\nserver accepts."},"1073":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-68","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"While disconnected, the choice is stored and sent when the client next\nconnects."},"1074":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-69","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"With it off, the server still tells this client that something changed.\nThe card then shows\n`Metadata is stale: a shared update was withheld.` and a\n**Refresh stale metadata** button, which fetches the server's full state."},"1075":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-70","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#fields","content":"When the change also restarts the server's streams, as a placement\nchange or a committed calibration does, the client fetches the full\nstate by itself, so the card does not stay stale."},"1076":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-71","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#actions","content":"Every action is a button. When an action is not possible, its button\nstays focusable and the reason is written under it. The result of the\nlast action appears in a line at the bottom of the card; screen readers\nannounce it."},"1077":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-72","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#actions","content":"Action"},"1078":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-73","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#actions","content":"What it does"},"1079":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-74","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#actions","content":"Not possible when (reason shown)"},"1080":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-75","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#actions","content":"**Set up**"},"1081":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-76","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#actions","content":"Opens the setup workspace for this server in place of the server list, and takes its setup lock."},"1082":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-77","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#actions","content":"`not connected`; `no connection`; `the source is invalid`; `the setup workspace is open for this server`; `the setup workspace is open for <name>; leave it first`"},"1083":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-78","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#actions","content":"**Acquire lock**"},"1084":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-79","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#actions","content":"Asks the server for its setup lock. The lock line changes once the server announces the new owner."},"1085":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-80","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#actions","content":"`not connected`; `this client already holds the lock`; `the lock is held by <name>`"},"1086":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-81","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#actions","content":"**Release lock**"},"1087":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-82","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#actions","content":"Gives the lock back."},"1088":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-83","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#actions","content":"`not connected`; `this client does not hold the lock`"},"1089":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-84","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#actions","content":"**Refresh**"},"1090":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-85","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#actions","content":"Fetches the server's full state (a snapshot)."},"1091":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-86","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#actions","content":"`not connected`; `a snapshot is already being requested`"},"1092":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-87","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#actions","content":"**Reconnect**"},"1093":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-88","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#actions","content":"Starts a new session at once, without waiting for the automatic retry. After a conflict it tries again: if another card still shows the same server, it fails with the conflict (`Reconnect failed: closed locally: server <id> is already connected through <entry>`) and the card stays `disconnected`."},"1094":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-89","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#actions","content":"`already connecting`; `already connected`"},"1095":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-90","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#actions","content":"**Remove**"},"1096":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-91","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#actions","content":"Disconnects and removes the card and the server's point clouds. Always possible."},"1097":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-92","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#actions","content":"A browser that cannot decode HEVC can still take the lock. The lock is a\nsetup tool, not a viewing one."},"1098":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-93","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#actions","content":"For a recording whose files were rejected, every action except\n**Remove**, and the **Receive shared updates** checkbox, is unavailable,\nwith the reason `the source is invalid`."},"1099":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-94","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#actions","content":"Every control's accessible name includes the card's title, for example\n\"Acquire lock, Rig A\", so screen readers can tell cards apart. When two\ncards have the same title (as in a conflict), the name adds the server\nid and the entry id."},"1100":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-95","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#actions","content":"Results in the bottom line:"},"1101":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-96","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#actions","content":"`Acquire lock: accepted; waiting for the server's lock state`"},"1102":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-97","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#actions","content":"`Release lock: released`"},"1103":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-98","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#actions","content":"`Refresh: snapshot received`"},"1104":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-99","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#actions","content":"`Shared updates off: accepted by the server`, or\n`Shared updates off: stored; sent with the next hello` while\ndisconnected"},"1105":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-100","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#actions","content":"`Reconnect: connected (session 2)`"},"1106":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-101","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#actions","content":"`<action> rejected (<code>): <message>`: the server refused it. The code\nand message are the server's own; the protocol does not fix them. For\nexample, from the mock server:\n`Acquire lock rejected (lock-held): setup lock held by Client A`."},"1107":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-102","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#actions","content":"`<action> server error <code>: <message>`: the server answered with an\nerror; again the code is the server's own."},"1108":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-103","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#actions","content":"`<action> failed (<reason>): <message>`, for example `failed (timeout)`\nwhen the server did not answer in time"},"1109":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-104","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#actions","content":"`Reconnect failed: <why the session ended>`"},"1110":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-105","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#status-labels","content":"Label"},"1111":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-106","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#status-labels","content":"Meaning"},"1112":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-107","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#status-labels","content":"`connecting`"},"1113":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-108","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#status-labels","content":"Opening the session or waiting for the server's hello"},"1114":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-109","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#status-labels","content":"`disconnected`"},"1115":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-110","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#status-labels","content":"No session, for example after a conflict or a close by the server. After a server close the client retries, so the label cycles back to `connecting`"},"1116":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-111","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#status-labels","content":"`error`"},"1117":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-112","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#status-labels","content":"The last session failed (a reconnect is scheduled unless it was a version mismatch), or the source was invalid"},"1118":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-113","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#status-labels","content":"`needs-setup`"},"1119":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-114","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#status-labels","content":"Connected; the server needs setup before it can stream"},"1120":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-115","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#status-labels","content":"`locked-by-me`"},"1121":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-116","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#status-labels","content":"Connected; this client holds the server's setup lock"},"1122":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-117","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#status-labels","content":"`locked-by-other`"},"1123":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-118","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#status-labels","content":"Connected; another client holds the setup lock"},"1124":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-119","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#status-labels","content":"`paused-for-setup`"},"1125":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-120","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#status-labels","content":"Connected; streaming is paused for setup"},"1126":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-121","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#status-labels","content":"`ready`"},"1127":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-122","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#status-labels","content":"Connected and ready, not streaming"},"1128":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-123","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#status-labels","content":"`streaming`"},"1129":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-124","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#status-labels","content":"Connected and streaming"},"1130":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-125","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#status-labels","content":"The lock comes before readiness and streaming: a server that is\nstreaming while another client holds its lock shows `locked-by-other`."},"1131":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-126","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#expected-result","content":"A new card appears at once with `connecting`, then the server's name,\nits id and a live status (`ready`, `streaming` or `needs-setup`)."},"1132":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-127","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#expected-result","content":"The lock line reads `unlocked`, the calibration rows list three kinds,\nand the layout lists the server's bundles."},"1133":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-128","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#expected-result","content":"**Acquire lock** turns the label into `locked-by-me`, and the lock line\ncounts down from 15 s, restarting every 5 s. Other clients show\n`locked-by-other` and the name of this client."},"1134":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-129","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#expected-result","content":"**Release lock** returns every client to `unlocked`."},"1135":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-130","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#expected-result","content":"**Set up** replaces the server list with the setup workspace for this\nserver and takes the lock; leaving the workspace brings the cards back.\nSee Setup workspace."},"1136":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-131","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#expected-result","content":"**Acquire lock** on the card only holds the lock. To run calibrations, use\n**Set up**; it adopts a lock this client already holds."},"1137":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-132","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#troubleshooting","content":"**Acquire lock is refused:**"},"1138":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-133","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#troubleshooting","content":"`the lock is held by <name>` under the button, or\n`Acquire lock rejected (<code>): <message>` (from the mock server:\n`Acquire lock rejected (lock-held): …`): another client holds it. Ask\nthat operator to release it. A lock whose holder disappeared expires\n15 s after its last renewal."},"1139":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-134","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#troubleshooting","content":"`not connected`: the session is not up. Wait for it, or use\n**Reconnect**."},"1140":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-135","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#troubleshooting","content":"**The lock is gone after a reconnect:** expected. A lock never survives\na reconnect. Acquire it again."},"1141":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-136","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#troubleshooting","content":"**`Release lock failed (no-lease)`:** this client does not hold the lock\nany more, for example because it expired. Nothing needs releasing."},"1142":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-137","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#troubleshooting","content":"**`Metadata is stale: a shared update was withheld.`:** shared updates\nare off, and another client changed something. Select\n**Refresh stale metadata**, or turn shared updates back on and then\nrefresh."},"1143":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-138","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#troubleshooting","content":"**`Refresh server error <code>: <message>`:** the server could not\nanswer the refresh (from the mock server: `Refresh server error busy: …`).\nTry again."},"1144":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-139","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#troubleshooting","content":"**The lock shows `expires at server time …`:** clock sync has not\nfinished. It needs a few round trips after connecting; the countdown\nappears by itself."},"1145":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-140","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#troubleshooting","content":"**`budget: no budget yet`:** the server has not sent a network budget\nto this client."},"1146":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-141","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#troubleshooting","content":"**The card stays `error` with `reconnect scheduled`:** the client\nretries after 1 s, doubling the wait up to 30 s. Select **Reconnect** to\ntry at once. If it keeps failing, read the **last close** line and see\nAdd a server."},"1147":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-142","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#troubleshooting","content":"**Counts at 0 and `ready, no frame yet` right after a reconnect:**\nexpected for a moment. The new session starts its counts from zero and\nwaits for its first frames. If they stay at 0, check that the server is\nstreaming and that no compatibility line is shown."},"1148":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-143","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#troubleshooting","content":"**`Reconnect failed: …`:** the new session could not be opened. The\ntext after the colon is the reason, as in the **last close** line.\n`closed locally: server <id> is already connected through <entry>`\nmeans another card still shows that server: remove one of the two."},"1149":{"id":"/docs/client/server-card-144","page_id":"/docs/client/server-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/server-card#troubleshooting","content":"**To replay a recording:** **Reconnect** is unavailable while the card\nis connected. Select **Remove**, then open the recording again."},"1150":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","type":"page","content":"Setup workspace","breadcrumbs":["HSLU OrbbecStreamer","Client"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace"},"1151":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-0","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","content":"Open the focused setup workspace for one server, hold its setup lock, and leave it again; what each line means and what to do when you are refused or forced out."},"1152":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-1","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#what-it-is","content":"What it is"},"1153":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-2","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#how-to-use-it","content":"How to use it"},"1154":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-3","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#open-it","content":"Open it"},"1155":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-4","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#what-it-shows","content":"What it shows"},"1156":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-5","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#leave-it","content":"Leave it"},"1157":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-6","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#when-the-session-ends-without-you","content":"When the session ends without you"},"1158":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-7","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#expected-result","content":"Expected result"},"1159":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-8","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"1160":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-9","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#what-it-is","content":"The setup workspace is a focused view for **one server at a time**. You\nopen it from that server's card with **Set up**. It then replaces the side\npanel's content; the 3D view stays usable."},"1161":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-10","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#what-it-is","content":"Opening it takes the server's setup lock. While you hold the lock, the\nworkspace lets you run and commit the server's calibrations. See\nCalibration for the calibration sections."},"1162":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-11","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#what-it-is","content":"The workspace never commits anything by itself. A calibration result comes\ninto force only when you select **Commit**. When you leave, or the lock or\nthe connection is lost, the client discards its own copy of an\nuncommitted result. What the server does with it is not defined by the\nprotocol contract yet (change request 0012 is open); the mock server\ndrops it."},"1163":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-12","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#what-it-is","content":"The workspace also has a **Placement** section, where you edit the\nserver's placement as a local draft and commit it; see\nPlacement editing. A placement draft is\nkept in memory when you leave the workspace (a reload loses it), and is\nonly sent when you select **Commit placement**."},"1164":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-13","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#open-it","content":"Connect a server (see Add a server) and\nwait until its card shows a live status such as `ready` or\n`streaming`."},"1165":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-14","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#open-it","content":"On the card, select **Set up**."},"1166":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-15","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#open-it","content":"The workspace opens and asks the server for the setup lock at once."},"1167":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-16","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#open-it","content":"**Set up** is unavailable, with the reason under the button, when:"},"1168":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-17","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#open-it","content":"`not connected`: the card has no live session;"},"1169":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-18","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#open-it","content":"`the source is invalid`: a recording whose files were rejected;"},"1170":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-19","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#open-it","content":"`no connection`: the entry has no connection object at all;"},"1171":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-20","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#open-it","content":"`the setup workspace is open for this server`, or\n`the setup workspace is open for <name>; leave it first`: a workspace is\nalready open. Only one can be open at a time."},"1172":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-21","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#open-it","content":"**Set up** is available while another client holds the lock. Opening the\nworkspace then shows the refusal; see Troubleshooting."},"1173":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-22","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#what-it-shows","content":"From the top:"},"1174":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-23","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#what-it-shows","content":"**Status label and title:** `Set up: <server name>`, with the card's\nstatus label (`locked-by-me` while you hold the lock)."},"1175":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-24","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#what-it-shows","content":"**Controls:**"},"1176":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-25","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#what-it-shows","content":"**Leave setup (release lock)** while the session is active or\nacquiring the lock;"},"1177":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-26","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#what-it-shows","content":"**Back to servers** once the session has ended;"},"1178":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-27","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#what-it-shows","content":"**Enter setup again** once the session has ended and the server is\nstill connected."},"1179":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-28","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#what-it-shows","content":"**session:** where the session is:"},"1180":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-29","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#what-it-shows","content":"`acquiring the setup lock…`"},"1181":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-30","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#what-it-shows","content":"`active: this client holds the setup lock`"},"1182":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-31","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#what-it-shows","content":"`leaving: cancelling runs and releasing the lock…`"},"1183":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-32","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#what-it-shows","content":"`ended`"},"1184":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-33","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#what-it-shows","content":"**lock:** `held by this client, expires in 14 s`, as on the server card.\nThe client renews the lock every 5 s, so the countdown restarts from\n15 s. Until clock sync has a result it shows the server time instead,\nfor example `expires at server time 16.000 s (clock offset not known yet)`.\nWhile asking for the lock: `requested, not held yet`. After the session\nended: `not held by this client`."},"1185":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-34","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#what-it-shows","content":"A **hint** when the server waits for its camera-pose calibration:\n`The server waits for a camera-pose calibration, which it accepts without other setup.`"},"1186":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-35","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#what-it-shows","content":"An **exit box** when the session has ended (see below)."},"1187":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-36","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#what-it-shows","content":"Three **calibration sections**: Camera pose, Depth quantization and\nNetwork. See Calibration."},"1188":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-37","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#what-it-shows","content":"The **Placement** section: the server's placement (anchor, revision,\ntranslation, yaw / pitch / roll) and the draft editor. See\nPlacement editing."},"1189":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-38","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#what-it-shows","content":"Every button stays focusable when it is unavailable, and its reason is\nwritten under it; while its request is waiting for an answer it shows\n`in progress`. Accessible names include the server name, for example\n\"Leave setup (release lock), Rig A\"."},"1190":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-39","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#what-it-shows","content":"Keyboard focus and screen readers:"},"1191":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-40","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#what-it-shows","content":"Opening the workspace moves focus to its heading."},"1192":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-41","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#what-it-shows","content":"**Enter setup again** moves focus to the heading too, since the button\ndisappears while the lock is requested."},"1193":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-42","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#what-it-shows","content":"When the workspace closes (**Back to servers**, or a clean leave), focus\nreturns to that server's **Set up** button, and the side panel\nannounces how the session ended, followed by\n`Setup workspace closed.`"},"1194":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-43","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#what-it-shows","content":"Results and exits are announced as they happen. A progress summary is\nannounced at most every 5 s, and the latest one at the end of each\n5 s window. The same result after a new action is announced again."},"1195":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-44","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#leave-it","content":"Select **Leave setup (release lock)**. The client first cancels any\ncalibration that is still running, then releases the lock. When the\nrelease succeeds, the workspace closes and the server cards come back."},"1196":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-45","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#leave-it","content":"Nothing is committed on the way out. The client discards its copy of a\ncalibration result you did not commit. A placement draft is kept, but no\nlonger drawn in the 3D view, until you open the workspace again, discard\nit, or remove the server."},"1197":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-46","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#leave-it","content":"If the release fails, the workspace stays open with\n`Could not release the setup lock (<reason>): <message>. The session stays active; try Leave again.`"},"1198":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-47","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#when-the-session-ends-without-you","content":"The exit box explains why. For a forced exit it always adds\n`Nothing was committed.`"},"1199":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-48","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#when-the-session-ends-without-you","content":"Exit box"},"1200":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-49","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#when-the-session-ends-without-you","content":"Meaning"},"1201":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-50","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#when-the-session-ends-without-you","content":"`Could not enter setup. The setup lock is held by <name>.`"},"1202":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-51","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#when-the-session-ends-without-you","content":"Another client holds the lock."},"1203":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-52","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#when-the-session-ends-without-you","content":"`Could not enter setup. Could not acquire the setup lock: <message>.`"},"1204":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-53","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#when-the-session-ends-without-you","content":"The server refused the lock for another reason."},"1205":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-54","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#when-the-session-ends-without-you","content":"`Could not enter setup. Not connected to the server.`"},"1206":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-55","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#when-the-session-ends-without-you","content":"The session was not live when you opened the workspace."},"1207":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-56","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#when-the-session-ends-without-you","content":"`Forced out of setup. The setup lease expired.`"},"1208":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-57","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#when-the-session-ends-without-you","content":"This client's lock ran out, for example because renewals did not reach the server."},"1209":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-58","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#when-the-session-ends-without-you","content":"`Forced out of setup. The setup lease was lost: <message>.`"},"1210":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-59","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#when-the-session-ends-without-you","content":"The server rejected a renewal."},"1211":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-60","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#when-the-session-ends-without-you","content":"`Forced out of setup. The server ended the setup lease.`"},"1212":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-61","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#when-the-session-ends-without-you","content":"The server announced the lock free without a release from you."},"1213":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-62","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#when-the-session-ends-without-you","content":"`Forced out of setup. The setup lock is held by <name>.`"},"1214":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-63","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#when-the-session-ends-without-you","content":"Another client took over the lock."},"1215":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-64","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#when-the-session-ends-without-you","content":"`Forced out of setup. The connection closed: <reason>.`"},"1216":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-65","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#when-the-session-ends-without-you","content":"The session to the server ended. A lock never survives a reconnect."},"1217":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-66","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#when-the-session-ends-without-you","content":"When a result was waiting for **Commit**, the box also says\n`The client discarded the uncommitted depth quantization result.`"},"1218":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-67","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#when-the-session-ends-without-you","content":"Select **Enter setup again** to ask for the lock again, or\n**Back to servers** to close the workspace."},"1219":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-68","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#expected-result","content":"**Set up** opens the workspace. Within a moment the session line reads\n`active: this client holds the setup lock`, the lock line counts down\nfrom 15 s, and the status label is `locked-by-me`. Other clients show\n`locked-by-other` with this client's name."},"1220":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-69","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#expected-result","content":"**Leave setup (release lock)** closes the workspace, and every client\nshows the server `unlocked` again."},"1221":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-70","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#expected-result","content":"While the workspace is open, the server cards and the World anchors\nsection are hidden; the 3D view keeps drawing every server, and draws\nthis server at your placement draft while you have one."},"1222":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-71","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#expected-result","content":"The workspace does not move the 3D camera to the server's point cloud yet."},"1223":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-72","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#troubleshooting","content":"**`Could not enter setup. The setup lock is held by <name>.`:** another\noperator is setting up this server. Ask them to leave setup, or wait:\na lock whose holder disappeared expires 15 s after its last renewal.\nThen select **Enter setup again**."},"1224":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-73","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#troubleshooting","content":"**`Forced out of setup. The setup lease expired.` in the middle of a\nrun:** the lock ran out. The client committed nothing. What the server\ndoes with a run whose lock ends is not defined by the protocol contract\nyet (change request 0012 is open); the mock server cancels it. Check\nthe connection (the card's network line and last close), then select\n**Enter setup again**. If the state line still shows `running`, the run\ncontinued on the server; otherwise start it again."},"1225":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-74","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#troubleshooting","content":"**`Forced out of setup. The connection closed: …`:** the session ended.\nSelect **Back to servers**, wait until the card is live again (the\nclient reconnects by itself), then select **Set up** again."},"1226":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-75","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#troubleshooting","content":"**A result was never committed:** a result comes into force only with\n**Commit**. When you leave or lose the lock, the client discards its\ncopy. Run the calibration again and commit it before leaving."},"1227":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-76","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#troubleshooting","content":"**`Could not release the setup lock …`:** the server did not accept the\nrelease. Select **Leave setup (release lock)** again. If the connection\nis gone, the lock ends on the server 15 s after its last renewal."},"1228":{"id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace-77","page_id":"/docs/client/setup-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/setup-workspace#troubleshooting","content":"**Set up says `the setup workspace is open for <name>; leave it first`:**\nonly one workspace can be open. Leave that one first."},"1229":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","type":"page","content":"The 3D viewer","breadcrumbs":["HSLU OrbbecStreamer","Client"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/viewer"},"1230":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-0","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer","content":"What the client's 3D view shows, how to move around in it, which graphics backend it uses, and what to do when nothing is drawn."},"1231":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-1","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/viewer#what-it-is","content":"What it is"},"1232":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-2","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/viewer#how-to-use-it","content":"How to use it"},"1233":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-3","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/viewer#camera-controls","content":"Camera controls"},"1234":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-4","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/viewer#which-graphics-backend-is-in-use","content":"Which graphics backend is in use"},"1235":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-5","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/viewer#where-each-server-appears-world-anchors","content":"Where each server appears: world anchors"},"1236":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-6","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/viewer#not-available-yet","content":"Not available yet"},"1237":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-7","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/viewer#expected-result","content":"Expected result"},"1238":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-8","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"1239":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-9","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#what-it-is","content":"The large area to the left of the client's side panel is the 3D viewer. It\ndraws one live, coloured point cloud per camera bundle, for every connected\nserver and every open recording, all in one shared scene. The client\nrebuilds each point on the GPU from the depth stream, using the server's\ncamera calibration and placement, and colours it from the colour stream."},"1240":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-10","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#what-it-is","content":"What you see:"},"1241":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-11","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#what-it-is","content":"**One point per depth pixel.** Each point takes the colour of the same\npixel in the colour stream (the server aligns colour to depth before\nsending)."},"1242":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-12","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#what-it-is","content":"**Only valid depth is drawn.** The server marks every depth pixel with a\ncode. The viewer hides:"},"1243":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-13","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#what-it-is","content":"pixels marked invalid (outside the foreground mask, or no reading);"},"1244":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-14","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#what-it-is","content":"pixels marked closer than the server's minimum depth;"},"1245":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-15","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#what-it-is","content":"pixels marked farther than the server's maximum depth."},"1246":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-16","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#what-it-is","content":"A hidden pixel leaves a gap; it is never drawn as a wall at the near or\nfar limit."},"1247":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-17","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#what-it-is","content":"**Every server in one scene.** Each server's cloud is placed with that\nserver's placement (where the server sits relative to its anchor). Two\nservers never mix, even if they use the same bundle names."},"1248":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-18","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#what-it-is","content":"**Point size.** Points are 2 pixels wide on WebGL2 and 1 pixel wide on\nWebGPU. WebGPU has no adjustable point size yet."},"1249":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-19","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#how-to-use-it","content":"Open the client in a desktop browser."},"1250":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-20","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#how-to-use-it","content":"In the side panel, connect to a server under **Add server**, or play a\nrecording under **Open recording**. The viewer shows the clouds as soon\nas frames arrive; there is nothing to switch on."},"1251":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-21","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#how-to-use-it","content":"Move around with the camera controls below. Click the viewer once first\nso that it has keyboard focus."},"1252":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-22","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#camera-controls","content":"The viewer uses an orbit camera. It turns around a target point that\nstarts 2 m in front of the scene origin. At start the camera sits 3 m from\nthe target, slightly above it, looking forward along +Z."},"1253":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-23","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#camera-controls","content":"Action"},"1254":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-24","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#camera-controls","content":"Mouse"},"1255":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-25","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#camera-controls","content":"Touch"},"1256":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-26","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#camera-controls","content":"Keyboard"},"1257":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-27","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#camera-controls","content":"Orbit around the target"},"1258":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-28","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#camera-controls","content":"Drag with the left button"},"1259":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-29","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#camera-controls","content":"Drag with one finger"},"1260":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-30","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#camera-controls","content":"Arrow keys"},"1261":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-31","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#camera-controls","content":"Pan (move the target)"},"1262":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-32","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#camera-controls","content":"Drag with the right button, or Ctrl + left-drag"},"1263":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-33","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#camera-controls","content":"Drag with two fingers"},"1264":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-34","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#camera-controls","content":"Ctrl + arrow keys"},"1265":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-35","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#camera-controls","content":"Zoom in and out"},"1266":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-36","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#camera-controls","content":"Mouse wheel"},"1267":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-37","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#camera-controls","content":"Pinch"},"1268":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-38","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#camera-controls","content":"Alt + Up / Alt + Down"},"1269":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-39","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#camera-controls","content":"Mouse-wheel zoom moves roughly 2% of the current distance per wheel step (the exact amount depends on the browser's wheel delta), so it is\nfine up close and fast far away. Points closer than 1 cm or farther than\n100 m from the camera are not drawn. There is no \"reset view\" control; to\nget back to the start view, navigate back manually."},"1270":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-40","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#which-graphics-backend-is-in-use","content":"The client uses WebGPU when the browser offers it. Otherwise it falls back\nto WebGL2. The `renderer:` line at the top of the side panel, under the\nprotocol version, tells you which one is active:"},"1271":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-41","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#which-graphics-backend-is-in-use","content":"Panel shows"},"1272":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-42","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#which-graphics-backend-is-in-use","content":"Meaning"},"1273":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-43","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#which-graphics-backend-is-in-use","content":"`renderer: webgpu`"},"1274":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-44","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#which-graphics-backend-is-in-use","content":"WebGPU is in use."},"1275":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-45","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#which-graphics-backend-is-in-use","content":"`renderer: webgl2`"},"1276":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-46","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#which-graphics-backend-is-in-use","content":"WebGL2 is in use (WebGPU is missing or failed to start)."},"1277":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-47","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#which-graphics-backend-is-in-use","content":"`renderer: rendering-incompatible. Rendering incompatible: …`"},"1278":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-48","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#which-graphics-backend-is-in-use","content":"Neither backend is available. No point clouds are drawn, and the viewer area stays empty."},"1279":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-49","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#which-graphics-backend-is-in-use","content":"The collapsible **renderer notes (N)** line, when present, tells you why the client chose that\nbackend. Examples are `WebGPU not supported`, or\n`WebGPU initialisation failed: …` followed by `fresh canvas for the WebGL2\nfallback`."},"1280":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-50","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#which-graphics-backend-is-in-use","content":"A browser without a rendering backend can still connect to a server for\ncontrol and setup."},"1281":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-51","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#where-each-server-appears-world-anchors","content":"A server's placement says where the server sits relative to a named anchor\n(for example, a marker or a corner of the room). The client then decides\nwhere that anchor sits in its shared scene. That anchor pose is\n**client-local**: it is stored only in this browser tab, it is never sent\nto a server, and it never changes a server's placement. To change a\nserver's placement itself, see Placement editing."},"1282":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-52","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#where-each-server-appears-world-anchors","content":"The side panel's **World anchors** section, below the server cards, lists\nevery anchor that a connected server's placement names. It needs no setup\nlock. For each anchor it shows:"},"1283":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-53","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#where-each-server-appears-world-anchors","content":"**used by:** the servers whose placement names it;"},"1284":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-54","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#where-each-server-appears-world-anchors","content":"whether a pose was set in this browser, or `no pose set: at the scene\norigin`, and the pose, for example `at the scene origin (identity)`;"},"1285":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-55","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#where-each-server-appears-world-anchors","content":"six fields: **x (m)**, **y (m)**, **z (m)**, **yaw (°)**, **pitch (°)**\nand **roll (°)**;"},"1286":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-56","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#where-each-server-appears-world-anchors","content":"**Reset to identity**, which puts the anchor back at the scene origin."},"1287":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-57","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#where-each-server-appears-world-anchors","content":"To move an anchor:"},"1288":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-58","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#where-each-server-appears-world-anchors","content":"Type in its fields. A valid value applies at once, and every server\nthat uses the anchor moves with it in your 3D view. **Arrow Up** and\n**Arrow Down** step by 0.01 m or 1° (**Shift**: ten times that)."},"1289":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-59","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#where-each-server-appears-world-anchors","content":"To undo, select **Reset to identity**."},"1290":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-60","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#where-each-server-appears-world-anchors","content":"The fields work as in Placement editing,\nwith the same rotation order. Only rigid poses are accepted; a refused pose\nshows `Not applied (not a rigid transform): …` and changes nothing."},"1291":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-61","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#where-each-server-appears-world-anchors","content":"Anchor poses are not saved: reloading the page puts every anchor back at\nthe scene origin."},"1292":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-62","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#not-available-yet","content":"**Coming soon**, tracked in `client/docs/development/ROADMAP.md` (Phase 2):"},"1293":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-63","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#not-available-yet","content":"**Point-size and splat settings**, and larger points on WebGPU."},"1294":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-64","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#not-available-yet","content":"**Blending of overlapping cameras.** Where two cameras see the same\nsurface, both sets of points are drawn."},"1295":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-65","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#not-available-yet","content":"**WebXR (headset) viewing.**"},"1296":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-66","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#not-available-yet","content":"**Not available, and not on the roadmap yet:**"},"1297":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-67","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#not-available-yet","content":"**View toggles.** There are no switches for colour only, depth only or\nthe foreground mask. The viewer always shows coloured points."},"1298":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-68","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#not-available-yet","content":"**Hidden-pixel debug view.** The renderer can show pixels closer or\nfarther than the depth range in blue and red. The client has no switch\nfor it."},"1299":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-69","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#expected-result","content":"The side panel shows `renderer: webgpu` or `renderer: webgl2`."},"1300":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-70","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#expected-result","content":"For each connected server or open recording, the server card's layout\nshows `ready, drawing` for each bundle, and the **uploaded** counter goes\nup."},"1301":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-71","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#expected-result","content":"The viewer shows a coloured point cloud on a dark background. Gaps appear\nwhere the depth was invalid or out of range."},"1302":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-72","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#expected-result","content":"Dragging, the wheel and the arrow keys move the view smoothly."},"1303":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-73","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"Symptom"},"1304":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-74","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"Likely cause"},"1305":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-75","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"What to do"},"1306":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-76","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"Panel shows `renderer: rendering-incompatible`"},"1307":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-77","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"The browser has neither WebGPU nor WebGL2, or hardware acceleration is off."},"1308":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-78","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"Enable hardware acceleration in the browser settings, or try another browser with WebGPU or WebGL2. No browser has been verified end to end yet."},"1309":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-79","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"Server card shows `Setup and control only: this browser lacks HEVC colour decoding` or `… HEVC Main10 depth decoding`"},"1310":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-80","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"The browser cannot decode the streams, so there are no frames to draw."},"1311":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-81","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"Use a browser and GPU with HEVC (Main and Main10) decoding. No browser has been verified for this yet."},"1312":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-82","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"Panel shows `decoders: WebCodecs VideoDecoder is unavailable: …`"},"1313":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-83","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"The browser has no WebCodecs video decoding."},"1314":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-84","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"Use a browser with WebCodecs video decoding."},"1315":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-85","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"A bundle row stays `ready, no frame yet`, and **decoded pairs** stays at 0"},"1316":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-86","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"No colour and depth frames are reaching the client yet."},"1317":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-87","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"Check that the server is streaming. The card's status and **last close** line say whether the connection is up."},"1318":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-88","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"**decoded pairs** goes up, but **uploaded** does not and **dropped** does"},"1319":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-89","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"Frames are arriving but are not drawn, for example because they belong to a newer server setup than the one the client holds."},"1320":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-90","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"After a change on the server (calibration, depth range, placement), the client fetches the new setup and resumes on its own. If it does not, select **Remove** on the card and add the server again."},"1321":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-91","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"The cloud freezes, or disappears for a moment, right after a calibration or placement change on the server"},"1322":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-92","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"The client never draws a frame with the setup of a different revision. It waits for the new setup."},"1323":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-93","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"Wait a moment; drawing resumes once the new setup has arrived."},"1324":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-94","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"A bundle row shows `upload error: …`"},"1325":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-95","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"The GPU rejected a frame. The bundle stays hidden until the next good frame."},"1326":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-96","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"Usually clears by itself. If it keeps happening, reload the page."},"1327":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-97","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"A bundle row shows `rendering incompatible (too-many-tiles): …`"},"1328":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-98","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"The bundle packs more than 16 cameras into one stream, which the viewer cannot draw."},"1329":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-99","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"Use a server stream layout with 16 cameras or fewer per bundle (for example, one bundle per camera)."},"1330":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-100","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"A bundle row shows `metadata invalid (…)`"},"1331":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-101","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"The server's setup for this bundle is not consistent."},"1332":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-102","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"The client keeps showing the last good frame. Check the server's calibration and placement."},"1333":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-103","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"A card shows `conflict: server … is already rendered by …`"},"1334":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-104","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"The same server was added twice. Only one card per server is drawn."},"1335":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-105","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"Remove the duplicate card."},"1336":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-106","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"The cloud looks mirrored (left and right, or up and down, swapped)"},"1337":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-107","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"The coordinate convention between server and client is still being settled in change request 0011. The client assumes one reading of it."},"1338":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-108","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"Known limitation until change request 0011 is decided. Report it with the server's calibration so the teams can check the convention."},"1339":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-109","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"Two servers' clouds overlap"},"1340":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-110","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"Their placements put them in the same place, or they use different anchors that both sit at the scene origin in this browser."},"1341":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-111","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"Move one server with Placement editing, or move its anchor under **World anchors** (this browser only)."},"1342":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-112","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"A server's cloud moved in my view but not for other operators"},"1343":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-113","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"You moved its anchor under **World anchors**, or you have an uncommitted placement draft open in the setup workspace. Both are local to this browser."},"1344":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-114","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"Commit the placement if it is right (see Placement editing); otherwise **Reset to identity** or **Discard draft**."},"1345":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-115","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"The picture tears on WebGL2 (parts of two frames at once)"},"1346":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-116","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"WebGL2 uses a low-latency canvas where the browser allows it. This can tear."},"1347":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-117","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"Expected; it trades tearing for lower latency."},"1348":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-118","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"The view is slow or jerky"},"1349":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-119","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"Many points: roughly one per depth pixel per camera."},"1350":{"id":"/docs/client/viewer-120","page_id":"/docs/client/viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/client/viewer#troubleshooting","content":"Close other GPU-heavy tabs, and connect only the servers you need: each adds its full point count."},"1351":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream","type":"page","content":"First stream","breadcrumbs":["HSLU OrbbecStreamer","Getting Started"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream"},"1352":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream-0","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream","content":"Capture your own camera through the full server pipeline today; stream it to a browser once serving lands."},"1353":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream-1","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream#adapt-the-config-to-your-rig","content":"Adapt the config to your rig"},"1354":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream-2","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream#run-it","content":"Run it"},"1355":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream-3","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream#watch-it-work","content":"Watch it work"},"1356":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream-4","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream#watch-your-own-capture","content":"Watch your own capture"},"1357":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream-5","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream#optional-preview-it-in-the-client","content":"Optional: preview it in the client"},"1358":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream-6","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"1359":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream-7","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream","content":"Browsers cannot get a live stream from a real server yet: WebTransport\nserving is not implemented (see Serve to browsers).\nA working first stream today runs entirely on the server, verified by its\nown telemetry and debug recordings."},"1360":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream-8","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream","content":"This needs a built server and at\nleast one attached Orbbec camera."},"1361":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream-9","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream#adapt-the-config-to-your-rig","content":"`config/dev/live.yaml` describes the development rig, not yours. Copy it and\nedit the camera serial numbers, sync settings and mask backend for your own\ncameras. Full steps:\nAdapt the config to your rig."},"1362":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream-10","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream#adapt-the-config-to-your-rig","content":"The short version, from `server/`:"},"1363":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream-11","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream#adapt-the-config-to-your-rig","content":"Then edit `config/local/live.yaml`: set each camera's `serial_number`, and\neither build the RVM engine or set `mask.backend: fill_all` to run without\nsegmentation."},"1364":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream-12","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream#watch-it-work","content":"The terminal redraws a rate table roughly every 5 seconds. After the\nwarm-up, every stage should reach your configured frame rate with 0 drops.\nSee Read the telemetry for what each line means,\nand Run the server for a full\nworked log."},"1365":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream-13","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream#watch-it-work","content":"Stop it with `Ctrl+C` when you're done; it shuts down cleanly."},"1366":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream-14","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream#watch-your-own-capture","content":"With `debug_recording.record_gpu_outputs: true` and\n`locally_decode_gpu_outputs: true` in the config, open\n`debug/live/<camera>/gpu-output-depth-inferno.mkv` in any video player to\nsee your own depth stream, colourised. See\nRun the server for the full\nfile list."},"1367":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream-15","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream#optional-preview-it-in-the-client","content":"The browser client can play back a recorded `.hevc` colour and depth pair\ntoday, without a server. Bridging your server's debug output into the\nclient's recording format is manual: you write a manifest by hand (camera\nintrinsics, depth range and lookup table) alongside the raw `.hevc` files.\nSee Play back .hevc recordings for the file\nrequirements and the manifest format. Real HEVC decoding has not been\nverified in a desktop browser yet either; see\nBrowser requirements."},"1368":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream-16","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/first-stream#troubleshooting","content":"Every start-up failure and its fix are in\nRun the server and\nConfiguration. For calibrating\ndepth quantization or camera pose next, see\nCalibration."},"1369":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/install-server","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/install-server","type":"page","content":"Install the server","breadcrumbs":["HSLU OrbbecStreamer","Getting Started"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/install-server"},"1370":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/install-server-0","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/install-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/install-server","content":"The shortest path to a built server, linking out to the full server documentation for every detail."},"1371":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/install-server-1","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/install-server","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/install-server#check-your-machine","content":"Check your machine"},"1372":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/install-server-2","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/install-server","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/install-server#clone-the-repository","content":"Clone the repository"},"1373":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/install-server-3","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/install-server","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/install-server#install-the-system-packages-and-sdks","content":"Install the system packages and SDKs"},"1374":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/install-server-4","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/install-server","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/install-server#configure-and-build","content":"Configure and build"},"1375":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/install-server-5","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/install-server","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/install-server#verify","content":"Verify"},"1376":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/install-server-6","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/install-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/install-server","content":"This is the minimal path. The Server section has the full\ndetail for every step, including every package, every troubleshooting\nmessage, and how to build for a GPU other than the tested one."},"1377":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/install-server-7","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/install-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/install-server#check-your-machine","content":"The tested machine is Ubuntu 26.04 with an NVIDIA RTX 4090 (compute\ncapability 8.9), CUDA 13, TensorRT 11 and Orbbec cameras on USB 3. See\nRequirements for the full list and a check\ncommand for each item, including what to do on an older GPU."},"1378":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/install-server-8","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/install-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/install-server#clone-the-repository","content":"Without a GitHub SSH key, see Install\nfor the HTTPS form."},"1379":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/install-server-9","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/install-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/install-server#install-the-system-packages-and-sdks","content":"Follow Install start to finish: system packages,\nCUDA, TensorRT, the Orbbec SDK and vcpkg. The RVM segmentation engine near\nthe end is optional; skip it for now."},"1380":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/install-server-10","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/install-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/install-server#configure-and-build","content":"The first configure builds every vcpkg dependency from source and can take\na long time. See Build and test for the Makefile\nshortcuts, the CTest labels, CLion setup, and how to build for a GPU below\ncompute capability 8.9."},"1381":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/install-server-11","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/install-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/install-server#verify","content":"**Expected result:** `--cuda-test` reports your GPU and ends\n`CUDA smoke test OK`; `--nvenc-test` reports `main10=true` and ends\n`NVENC capability test passed`. See\nBuild and test for the full output on\nthe reference machine, and its\nTroubleshooting table for every\nfailure message."},"1382":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/install-server-12","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/install-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/install-server#verify","content":"Every environment variable the build and the runtime read is listed in\nGetting started notes."},"1383":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/install-server-13","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/install-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/install-server#verify","content":"Next: First stream. Want the browser\nclient too? See Run the dev build."},"1384":{"id":"/docs/guides/calibration","page_id":"/docs/guides/calibration","type":"page","content":"Calibration","breadcrumbs":["HSLU OrbbecStreamer","Guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/calibration"},"1385":{"id":"/docs/guides/calibration-0","page_id":"/docs/guides/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/calibration","content":"What each calibration kind does, what works today on the server and the client, and why they can't yet be chained into one flow."},"1386":{"id":"/docs/guides/calibration-1","page_id":"/docs/guides/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/calibration","content":"There are three calibration kinds. Each one is a server-side state with an\noptional client-side workspace to run it from. Today the server and client\ncannot talk to each other at all (see Serve to browsers),\nso every client-side calibration in this table works only against the\nclient's own built-in mock server, not against a real `orbbec_streamer`."},"1387":{"id":"/docs/guides/calibration-2","page_id":"/docs/guides/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/calibration","content":"Kind"},"1388":{"id":"/docs/guides/calibration-3","page_id":"/docs/guides/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/calibration","content":"Server"},"1389":{"id":"/docs/guides/calibration-4","page_id":"/docs/guides/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/calibration","content":"Client"},"1390":{"id":"/docs/guides/calibration-5","page_id":"/docs/guides/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/calibration","content":"Camera pose"},"1391":{"id":"/docs/guides/calibration-6","page_id":"/docs/guides/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/calibration","content":"Works, from the local console. Camera pose calibration."},"1392":{"id":"/docs/guides/calibration-7","page_id":"/docs/guides/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/calibration","content":"Placeholder screen only; no controls. Calibration."},"1393":{"id":"/docs/guides/calibration-8","page_id":"/docs/guides/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/calibration","content":"Depth quantization"},"1394":{"id":"/docs/guides/calibration-9","page_id":"/docs/guides/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/calibration","content":"Works, from a CLI tool. Depth quantization calibrator."},"1395":{"id":"/docs/guides/calibration-10","page_id":"/docs/guides/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/calibration","content":"Start, watch, cancel and commit a run against the mock server. Calibration, Mock server."},"1396":{"id":"/docs/guides/calibration-11","page_id":"/docs/guides/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/calibration","content":"Network"},"1397":{"id":"/docs/guides/calibration-12","page_id":"/docs/guides/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/calibration","content":"Not available. A stream is reserved in the wire format (§1); no calibration procedure exists yet."},"1398":{"id":"/docs/guides/calibration-13","page_id":"/docs/guides/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/calibration","content":"Not available: waits for change request 0018."},"1399":{"id":"/docs/guides/calibration-14","page_id":"/docs/guides/calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/calibration","content":"Once WebTransport serving exists, the client's depth-quantization workspace\nis expected to work the same way against a real server. Until then, run\ncamera pose and depth quantization calibration on the server console: see\nFirst stream for a config already set\nup for your cameras."},"1400":{"id":"/docs/guides/placement","page_id":"/docs/guides/placement","type":"page","content":"Placement","breadcrumbs":["HSLU OrbbecStreamer","Guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/placement"},"1401":{"id":"/docs/guides/placement-0","page_id":"/docs/guides/placement","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/placement","content":"Placing each server's point cloud in the shared scene. Not available on either side yet."},"1402":{"id":"/docs/guides/placement-1","page_id":"/docs/guides/placement","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/placement","content":"Placement fixes where each server's point cloud sits in a scene shared by\nseveral servers. Nothing here is available to a user yet."},"1403":{"id":"/docs/guides/placement-2","page_id":"/docs/guides/placement","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/placement","content":"Side"},"1404":{"id":"/docs/guides/placement-3","page_id":"/docs/guides/placement","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/placement","content":"Status"},"1405":{"id":"/docs/guides/placement-4","page_id":"/docs/guides/placement","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/placement","content":"Server"},"1406":{"id":"/docs/guides/placement-5","page_id":"/docs/guides/placement","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/placement","content":"Accepts a revisioned placement commit over the control protocol, but nothing sends one yet."},"1407":{"id":"/docs/guides/placement-6","page_id":"/docs/guides/placement","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/placement","content":"Client"},"1408":{"id":"/docs/guides/placement-7","page_id":"/docs/guides/placement","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/placement","content":"No placement editor. Every server is drawn where its own stored placement puts it. Placement editing."},"1409":{"id":"/docs/guides/placement-8","page_id":"/docs/guides/placement","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/placement","content":"Once the client ships a placement editor, it will commit through the path\nthe server already accepts."},"1410":{"id":"/docs","page_id":"/docs","type":"page","content":"Introduction","breadcrumbs":["HSLU OrbbecStreamer"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs"},"1411":{"id":"/docs-0","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"Stream live RGB-D from Orbbec cameras to the browser, GPU-encoded end to end."},"1412":{"id":"/docs-1","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"OrbbecStreamer captures colour and depth from Orbbec cameras, processes and\nHEVC-encodes them on an NVIDIA GPU, and will stream them over WebTransport to\na browser client."},"1413":{"id":"/docs-2","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"The server and client each work well on their own today, but they cannot yet\ntalk to each other: WebTransport serving is not implemented (see\nServe to browsers). A working first stream today\nmeans running the server against your own camera and watching it capture,\nprocess and encode in real time: see First stream\nbelow."},"1414":{"id":"/docs-3","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"<Card title=\"Getting Started\" href=\"/docs/getting-started/install-server\" description=\"Install the server, and reach a first stream.\" />"},"1415":{"id":"/docs-4","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"<Card title=\"Guides\" href=\"/docs/guides/calibration\" description=\"Calibration and placement, across the server and the client.\" />"},"1416":{"id":"/docs-5","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"<Card title=\"Server\" href=\"/docs/server\" description=\"Install, configure and run the capture and streaming server.\" />"},"1417":{"id":"/docs-6","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"<Card title=\"Client\" href=\"/docs/client\" description=\"Connect to a server, play back recordings and view point clouds.\" />"},"1418":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","type":"page","content":"How the server works","breadcrumbs":["HSLU OrbbecStreamer","Server","How it works"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/architecture"},"1419":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-0","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/architecture","content":"The live pipeline from the cameras to the encoded bundles, which thread owns each stage, the bounded queues, the clock domains and what leaves the server today."},"1420":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-1","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/architecture#the-pipeline","content":"The pipeline"},"1421":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-2","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/architecture#threads-and-ownership","content":"Threads and ownership"},"1422":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-3","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/architecture#bounded-queues","content":"Bounded queues"},"1423":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-4","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/architecture#side-paths","content":"Side paths"},"1424":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-5","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/architecture#clock-domains","content":"Clock domains"},"1425":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-6","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/architecture#what-leaves-the-server","content":"What leaves the server"},"1426":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-7","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/architecture#related-pages","content":"Related pages"},"1427":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-8","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/architecture","content":"`orbbec_streamer --live` runs one pipeline: it captures synchronised colour\nand depth from every camera, groups them into multi-camera batches, copies\nthem to the GPU, masks and filters them, encodes colour and depth with\nNVENC and hands each encoded bundle to its consumer. This page shows how\nthe parts fit together. The details are on\nCapture and synchronisation,\nGPU processing and Stream layout.\nThe code is in `server/src/app/live/LiveApp.cpp`."},"1428":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-9","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/architecture#the-pipeline","content":"The batcher has no thread of its own: it runs on the capture thread whose\nframe set completes a batch, and that thread also pushes the batch into the\nupload queue."},"1429":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-10","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/architecture#the-pipeline","content":"**Capture.** Each camera has one capture thread. It takes a colour +\ndepth frame set from the Orbbec SDK, aligns colour to depth (in the SDK,\non the CPU) and passes the frame set to the batcher."},"1430":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-11","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/architecture#the-pipeline","content":"**Batching.** The frame batcher waits until every camera has a frame set\nwhose capture timestamps lie within `sync.timestamp_tolerance_us`, then\nemits one batch. The batch always holds one frame set per camera, in\nconfig order."},"1431":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-12","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/architecture#the-pipeline","content":"**Upload.** The upload thread copies each frame into pinned host memory\nand starts an asynchronous copy to the GPU."},"1432":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-13","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/architecture#the-pipeline","content":"**GPU processing.** The processing thread computes the foreground mask\nand filters depth, then hands the batch to the encoder."},"1433":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-14","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/architecture#the-pipeline","content":"**Encoding.** The encode thread converts colour to NV12 and depth to\n10-bit codes, encodes both with NVENC and builds an encoded bundle: one\nper batch in `concatenated_batch` mode, one per camera in `per_camera`\nmode (Stream layout)."},"1434":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-15","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/architecture#the-pipeline","content":"**Hand-off.** The bundle is recorded for the latency telemetry and passed\nto the debug recorder when output recording is on. This is where the\nnetwork server will take it."},"1435":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-16","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/architecture#threads-and-ownership","content":"Thread"},"1436":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-17","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/architecture#threads-and-ownership","content":"Owns"},"1437":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-18","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/architecture#threads-and-ownership","content":"Never waits for"},"1438":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-19","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/architecture#threads-and-ownership","content":"Capture, one per camera"},"1439":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-20","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/architecture#threads-and-ownership","content":"The camera's SDK pipeline, CPU alignment, the frame batcher (shared, behind a lock)"},"1440":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-21","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/architecture#threads-and-ownership","content":"Upload: it only pushes into the upload queue"},"1441":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-22","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/architecture#threads-and-ownership","content":"Upload"},"1442":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-23","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/architecture#threads-and-ownership","content":"Pinned staging buffers and the upload CUDA stream"},"1443":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-24","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/architecture#threads-and-ownership","content":"Processing"},"1444":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-25","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/architecture#threads-and-ownership","content":"Processing"},"1445":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-26","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/architecture#threads-and-ownership","content":"The processing CUDA stream, the RVM TensorRT engine, masks and filtered depth"},"1446":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-27","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/architecture#threads-and-ownership","content":"Encoding, preview, debug recording"},"1447":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-28","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/architecture#threads-and-ownership","content":"Encode"},"1448":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-29","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/architecture#threads-and-ownership","content":"The NVENC sessions (2, or 2 per camera) and their CUDA stream"},"1449":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-30","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/architecture#threads-and-ownership","content":"Its consumers"},"1450":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-31","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/architecture#threads-and-ownership","content":"Preview (with `run.preview`)"},"1451":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-32","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/architecture#threads-and-ownership","content":"The OpenCV window"},"1452":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-33","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/architecture#threads-and-ownership","content":"Nothing upstream waits for it"},"1453":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-34","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/architecture#threads-and-ownership","content":"Debug recorder, two workers (with recording on)"},"1454":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-35","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/architecture#threads-and-ownership","content":"FFV1 writers, local HEVC decoders, disk"},"1455":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-36","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/architecture#threads-and-ownership","content":"Nothing upstream waits for it"},"1456":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-37","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/architecture#threads-and-ownership","content":"Camera-pose calibration worker"},"1457":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-38","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/architecture#threads-and-ownership","content":"ChArUco detection and the pose solver"},"1458":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-39","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/architecture#threads-and-ownership","content":"Capture hands it references only while a run is active"},"1459":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-40","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/architecture#threads-and-ownership","content":"Main"},"1460":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-41","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/architecture#threads-and-ownership","content":"Start-up, stop, the 1 s telemetry loop, setup-lease expiry"},"1461":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-42","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/architecture#threads-and-ownership","content":"-"},"1462":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-43","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/architecture#threads-and-ownership","content":"An error in the upload, processing, encode or preview thread (for example a\nCUDA or NVENC failure) stops the whole server: the main loop sees it within\na second, stops capture and every stage, and exits with\n`orbbec-streamer failed: <reason>`. See\nRun the server. A debug-recorder error only\ndisables the recorder (`worker=failed` in the telemetry). A camera error\nends that camera's capture thread without stopping the server; see\nCapture and synchronisation."},"1463":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-44","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/architecture#bounded-queues","content":"Every hand-off between threads goes through a short queue with a fixed\ncapacity. None of them can grow:"},"1464":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-45","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/architecture#bounded-queues","content":"Queue"},"1465":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-46","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/architecture#bounded-queues","content":"Capacity"},"1466":{"id":"/docs/server/architecture-47","page_id":"/docs/server/architecture","tags":[],"type":