,"1668":{"id":"/docs/server/build-129","page_id":"/docs/server/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/build#clion","content":"CLion reads `CMakePresets.json`. In **Settings → Build, Execution, Deployment →\nCMake**, enable the `dev-debug` profile and turn off the default `Debug`\nprofile. The default profile builds in `cmake-build-debug` without the vcpkg\ntoolchain and the compiler settings of the presets. Set the program arguments of the\n`orbbec_streamer` run configuration to one of the smoke flags, or to\n`--live config/dev/live.yaml`, and set its working directory to `server/`."},"1669":{"id":"/docs/server/build-130","page_id":"/docs/server/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/build#expected-result","content":"Configure ends with:"},"1670":{"id":"/docs/server/build-131","page_id":"/docs/server/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/build#expected-result","content":"`check_unit` ends with:"},"1671":{"id":"/docs/server/build-132","page_id":"/docs/server/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/build#expected-result","content":"The CTest command without cameras or the RVM engine ends with:"},"1672":{"id":"/docs/server/build-133","page_id":"/docs/server/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/build#expected-result","content":"`--cuda-test` and `--nvenc-test` print, on the reference machine:"},"1673":{"id":"/docs/server/build-134","page_id":"/docs/server/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/build#expected-result","content":"`--orbbec-test` with two Femto Bolts prints one block per camera and ends with:"},"1674":{"id":"/docs/server/build-135","page_id":"/docs/server/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/build#troubleshooting","content":"Symptom"},"1675":{"id":"/docs/server/build-136","page_id":"/docs/server/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/build#troubleshooting","content":"Cause and fix"},"1676":{"id":"/docs/server/build-137","page_id":"/docs/server/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/build#troubleshooting","content":"`C++ and CUDA host compilers must use the same major toolchain`"},"1677":{"id":"/docs/server/build-138","page_id":"/docs/server/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/build#troubleshooting","content":"CMake cached different compilers for C++ and CUDA, usually from a configure outside the presets. Run `cmake --preset dev-debug --fresh` to discard the CMake cache. The presets set `CC`, `CXX` and `CUDAHOSTCXX` for you."},"1678":{"id":"/docs/server/build-139","page_id":"/docs/server/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/build#troubleshooting","content":"`CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER ... /usr/bin/g++-15 is not a full path to an existing compiler`"},"1679":{"id":"/docs/server/build-140","page_id":"/docs/server/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/build#troubleshooting","content":"Install `g++-15` (see Install)."},"1680":{"id":"/docs/server/build-141","page_id":"/docs/server/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/build#troubleshooting","content":"`No CMAKE_CUDA_COMPILER could be found` or `/usr/local/cuda/bin/nvcc` missing"},"1681":{"id":"/docs/server/build-142","page_id":"/docs/server/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/build#troubleshooting","content":"The CUDA toolkit is not installed at `/usr/local/cuda`. See Install."},"1682":{"id":"/docs/server/build-143","page_id":"/docs/server/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/build#troubleshooting","content":"vcpkg fails while building `at-spi2-core`, `gtk3` or another OpenCV dependency"},"1683":{"id":"/docs/server/build-144","page_id":"/docs/server/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/build#troubleshooting","content":"A system build tool or X11 header is missing. Install the packages in Install and configure again. The vcpkg log path is in the error message."},"1684":{"id":"/docs/server/build-145","page_id":"/docs/server/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/build#troubleshooting","content":"A CUDA test fails with `no kernel image is available for execution on the device`"},"1685":{"id":"/docs/server/build-146","page_id":"/docs/server/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/build#troubleshooting","content":"The GPU is older than compute capability 8.9, which the presets build for. See Build for a different GPU."},"1686":{"id":"/docs/server/build-147","page_id":"/docs/server/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/build#troubleshooting","content":"`smoke_rvm_engine_b1` and `smoke_rvm_engine_b2` are `Not Run`"},"1687":{"id":"/docs/server/build-148","page_id":"/docs/server/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/build#troubleshooting","content":"The RVM engines are not built. Build them, or exclude them with `-LE rvm`."},"1688":{"id":"/docs/server/build-149","page_id":"/docs/server/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/build#troubleshooting","content":"`protocol_conformance_tests` fails after you update from `main`"},"1689":{"id":"/docs/server/build-150","page_id":"/docs/server/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/build#troubleshooting","content":"The protocol contract changed and the server does not conform yet. This is expected: it is how the server team learns of a contract change."},"1690":{"id":"/docs/server/build-151","page_id":"/docs/server/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/build#troubleshooting","content":"`orbbec_live_sync_integration_test` fails with `Request failed, device response with unknown error! propertyId: 1038`"},"1691":{"id":"/docs/server/build-152","page_id":"/docs/server/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/build#troubleshooting","content":"A camera rejected the multi-device sync settings (property 1038 is `OB_STRUCT_MULTI_DEVICE_SYNC_CONFIG`). Possible causes are a missing or loose sync cable, wrong `primary` and `secondary` roles in the config, or a camera left in a bad state by an earlier run. Check the cabling and the roles, then power-cycle the cameras. This fix is not yet confirmed. The Orbbec SDK log is in `Log/OrbbecSDK.log.txt` in the working directory."},"1692":{"id":"/docs/server/build-153","page_id":"/docs/server/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/build#troubleshooting","content":"An NVENC test fails with `NvEncOpenEncodeSessionEx failed with NVENC status 21`"},"1693":{"id":"/docs/server/build-154","page_id":"/docs/server/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/build#troubleshooting","content":"Too many NVENC sessions at once: GeForce drivers limit concurrent encoder sessions and report status 21 (`NV_ENC_ERR_INCOMPATIBLE_CLIENT_KEY`). `ctest` runs the NVENC tests one at a time (they share the `nvenc` resource lock), so this appears only when another program is encoding at the same time, such as a running server, OBS or a second `ctest`. Stop it and rerun."},"1694":{"id":"/docs/server/build-155","page_id":"/docs/server/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/build#troubleshooting","content":"`--orbbec-capture-test` prints `Orbbec SDK error: ...` but exits with code 0, and CTest reports `smoke_orbbec_capture` as passed"},"1695":{"id":"/docs/server/build-156","page_id":"/docs/server/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/build#troubleshooting","content":"The capture smoke test catches SDK errors and does not fail on them. Read its output: it passed only if the last line ends in `smoke test OK`."},"1696":{"id":"/docs/server/build-157","page_id":"/docs/server/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/build#troubleshooting","content":"A hardware test cannot find a camera"},"1697":{"id":"/docs/server/build-158","page_id":"/docs/server/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/build#troubleshooting","content":"Check that the serial numbers in `config/dev/live.yaml` match `--orbbec-test`, and that no other program, such as `OrbbecViewer` or a running server, has the cameras open."},"1698":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","type":"page","content":"Camera pose calibration","breadcrumbs":["HSLU OrbbecStreamer","Server","Operate"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration"},"1699":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-0","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","content":"Print the ChArUco board, calibrate where each depth camera sits, and read the calibration state at startup."},"1700":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-1","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#what-works-today","content":"What works today"},"1701":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-2","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#configuration","content":"Configuration"},"1702":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-3","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#print-the-board","content":"Print the board"},"1703":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-4","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#run-a-calibration","content":"Run a calibration"},"1704":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-5","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#expected-result","content":"Expected result"},"1705":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-6","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#startup-states","content":"Startup states"},"1706":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-7","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#what-autocalibrate-changes","content":"What `autocalibrate` changes"},"1707":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-8","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#recalibrating-a-valid-setup","content":"Recalibrating a valid setup"},"1708":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-9","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"1709":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-10","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","content":"Camera pose calibration finds where every camera sits relative to the others,\nso clients can merge all views into one 3D scene. The result is one rigid 4×4\ntransform per camera, `serverFromDepthCamera`: the pose of that camera's\n**depth sensor** in the server frame. The server frame is the depth frame of\nthe reference camera (the first camera in the rig), whose pose is the\nidentity."},"1710":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-11","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","content":"You show a printed ChArUco board to the cameras. The server detects it in each\ncamera's colour image, which is already aligned into the depth image, and\nsolves the board pose with the depth intrinsics. Because of that alignment the\nresult is the depth-sensor pose directly; no colour-to-depth correction is\napplied. This requires `streams.alignment: color_to_depth`."},"1711":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-12","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","content":"The server needs a valid camera pose before it is ready to serve clients."},"1712":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-13","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#what-works-today","content":"Feature"},"1713":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-14","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#what-works-today","content":"Status"},"1714":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-15","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#what-works-today","content":"Print the board (`--print-charuco-board`)"},"1715":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-16","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#what-works-today","content":"Available"},"1716":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-17","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#what-works-today","content":"Calibrate from the server console (`--live ... --calibrate-camera-pose`)"},"1717":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-18","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#what-works-today","content":"Available. Tested with synthetic cameras; not yet validated with a printed board on hardware."},"1718":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-19","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#what-works-today","content":"Load and check the saved calibration at startup"},"1719":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-20","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#what-works-today","content":"Available"},"1720":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-21","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#what-works-today","content":"Atomic save with a revision number"},"1721":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-22","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#what-works-today","content":"Available"},"1722":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-23","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#what-works-today","content":"Start, follow and commit a calibration from a browser client"},"1723":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-24","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#what-works-today","content":"Not yet available. The server-side state machine exists, but the WebTransport listener that carries client commands is not implemented."},"1724":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-25","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#what-works-today","content":"`calibration.autocalibrate: true`"},"1725":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-26","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#what-works-today","content":"Parsed and reported, but has no practical effect until clients can connect. Keep it `false`."},"1726":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-27","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#what-works-today","content":"The local pipeline (capture, GPU processing, encoding, debug recording) runs\nwhether or not the pose is calibrated. The calibration state only decides\nwhat the server will offer to clients."},"1727":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-28","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#configuration","content":"All keys are in the `calibration` section of the live config\n(`config/dev/live.yaml`)."},"1728":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-29","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#configuration","content":"Key"},"1729":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-30","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#configuration","content":"Default"},"1730":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-31","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#configuration","content":"Meaning"},"1731":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-32","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#configuration","content":"`camera_pose_path`"},"1732":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-33","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#configuration","content":"`config/dev/camera-pose.json`"},"1733":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-34","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#configuration","content":"Saved calibration. Relative to the working directory. A missing file is not an error."},"1734":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-35","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#configuration","content":"`autocalibrate`"},"1735":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-36","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#configuration","content":"`false`"},"1736":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-37","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#configuration","content":"When the pose is missing or stale: `true` lets a client with the setup lock start calibration on its own; `false` needs an operator. See Startup states."},"1737":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-38","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#configuration","content":"`board.squares_x`"},"1738":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-39","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#configuration","content":"`7`"},"1739":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-40","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#configuration","content":"Squares across. At least 2."},"1740":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-41","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#configuration","content":"`board.squares_y`"},"1741":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-42","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#configuration","content":"`5`"},"1742":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-43","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#configuration","content":"Squares down. At least 2."},"1743":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-44","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#configuration","content":"`board.square_length_m`"},"1744":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-45","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#configuration","content":"`0.08`"},"1745":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-46","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#configuration","content":"Printed square size in metres."},"1746":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-47","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#configuration","content":"`board.marker_length_m`"},"1747":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-48","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#configuration","content":"`0.06`"},"1748":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-49","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#configuration","content":"Printed marker size in metres; smaller than the square."},"1749":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-50","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#configuration","content":"`board.dictionary`"},"1750":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-51","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#configuration","content":"`DICT_5X5_100`"},"1751":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-52","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#configuration","content":"OpenCV ArUco dictionary name."},"1752":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-53","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#configuration","content":"`streams.alignment` must be `color_to_depth`."},"1753":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-54","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#print-the-board","content":"Write the board as a PNG, using the board from your config. Run from\n`server/`:"},"1754":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-55","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#print-the-board","content":"Without `--live`, the built-in defaults (the same 7 × 5, 80 mm board) are\nused. This command does not open the cameras."},"1755":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-56","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#print-the-board","content":"The log tells you the physical size:"},"1756":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-57","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#print-the-board","content":"The image is drawn at 300 dpi with one white square of margin on every\nside, so the default image is 720 × 560 mm (8504 × 6614 pixels). The\nwhole image needs A1 paper (841 × 594 mm). A2 (594 × 420 mm) fits only the\n560 × 400 mm board without the margin, so crop the margin or print the\nboard edge to edge. The PNG carries no DPI information, so set the print\nsize yourself: the black-and-white board, without the margin, must measure\nthe size in the log."},"1757":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-58","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#print-the-board","content":"For a smaller printer, shrink the squares in the config and print again.\nFor example `square_length_m: 0.04` and `marker_length_m: 0.03` give a\n280 × 200 mm board (360 × 280 mm with margin), which fits A3 landscape.\nSmaller boards are harder to detect at 640 × 576 depth resolution, so hold\nthem closer."},"1758":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-59","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#print-the-board","content":"Measure one printed square with a ruler. Put the measured size into\n`square_length_m`, and scale `marker_length_m` by the same factor. A wrong\nsize does not stop detection, but every camera distance comes out scaled."},"1759":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-60","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#print-the-board","content":"Mount the print on something flat and rigid. A bent board makes the views\ndisagree."},"1760":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-61","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#run-a-calibration","content":"Build the server, then stop any other process that uses the cameras."},"1761":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-62","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#run-a-calibration","content":"Start the live pipeline with the calibration flag, from `server/`:"},"1762":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-63","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#run-a-calibration","content":"The server takes the setup lock as the local operator and starts a\ncalibration run. This works with `autocalibrate: false`, and it also\nrecalibrates an existing valid pose."},"1763":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-64","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#run-a-calibration","content":"Walk the board through the capture area:"},"1764":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-65","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#run-a-calibration","content":"At least two cameras must see the board at the same moment."},"1765":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-66","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#run-a-calibration","content":"Move or tilt it between views: a view is used only if the board moved\nat least 2 cm or turned at least 3° since the last accepted view."},"1766":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-67","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#run-a-calibration","content":"Tilt it rather than holding it square to a camera; views where the pose\nis ambiguous are rejected."},"1767":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-68","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#run-a-calibration","content":"Every camera needs at least 5 consistent shared views with a camera that\nis already placed. Cameras that never see the board together with the\nreference camera are chained through other cameras."},"1768":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-69","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#run-a-calibration","content":"The run needs 20 accepted views and gives up after 120 seconds."},"1769":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-70","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#run-a-calibration","content":"When the poses are solved the server saves them, raises the revision by\none and releases the lock. The live pipeline keeps running; stop it with\nCtrl+C. If you press Ctrl+C before the result is saved, the previous\ncalibration file is left untouched."},"1770":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-71","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#expected-result","content":"While the run is going, a progress line appears every 5 seconds:"},"1771":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-72","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#expected-result","content":"`cam1=no board` means that camera does not see the board in the current frame."},"1772":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-73","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#expected-result","content":"A successful run ends like this (numbers from a synthetic test rig):"},"1773":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-74","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#expected-result","content":"Check the translations against the real rig: they are the positions of each\ndepth sensor, in metres, relative to the reference camera."},"1774":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-75","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#expected-result","content":"The saved file (`calibration.camera_pose_path`) looks like this. The matrix\nis column-major, in metres, so the last column (entries 12–14) is the\ntranslation:"},"1775":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-76","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#expected-result","content":"The file is replaced atomically (temporary file, fsync, rename), so a crash\nleaves either the old or the new calibration. The server only writes a result\nthat covers every active camera with a valid rigid pose. Do not edit the file\nby hand: the loader is strict, and an unknown key or a non-rigid matrix makes\nthe whole calibration stale."},"1776":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-77","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#startup-states","content":"At every start, after the cameras are open, the server loads\n`calibration.camera_pose_path` and checks it against the running rig. It logs\none line:"},"1777":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-78","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#startup-states","content":"Calibration state"},"1778":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-79","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#startup-states","content":"When"},"1779":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-80","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#startup-states","content":"Phase in the log"},"1780":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-81","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#startup-states","content":"`valid`"},"1781":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-82","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#startup-states","content":"The file covers every active camera with the same serial number and depth resolution."},"1782":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-83","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#startup-states","content":"`READY` (or `STREAMING` once media is requested)"},"1783":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-84","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#startup-states","content":"`missing`"},"1784":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-85","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#startup-states","content":"No file."},"1785":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-86","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#startup-states","content":"`NEEDS_SETUP`, or `WAITING_FOR_CALIBRATION` with `autocalibrate: true`"},"1786":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-87","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#startup-states","content":"`stale`"},"1787":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-88","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#startup-states","content":"The file is unreadable or invalid, or a camera is not in it, has a different serial number (hardware swapped) or a different depth resolution. The reason is in the log line."},"1788":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-89","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#startup-states","content":"Same as `missing`"},"1789":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-90","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#startup-states","content":"`running`"},"1790":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-91","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#startup-states","content":"A calibration run is in progress."},"1791":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-92","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#startup-states","content":"`CALIBRATING`"},"1792":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-93","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#startup-states","content":"`failed`"},"1793":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-94","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#startup-states","content":"The last run failed and there was no valid calibration before."},"1794":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-95","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#startup-states","content":"Same as `missing`"},"1795":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-96","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#startup-states","content":"Removing a camera from the config does not invalidate the others: entries\nfor cameras that are not running are ignored. A missing or stale calibration\nnever stops the server; it starts and waits for setup."},"1796":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-97","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#startup-states","content":"`WAITING_FOR_CALIBRATION` and `CALIBRATING` are internal names. Clients see\n`readiness=needs-setup` with the snapshot flag `autocalibrate=true`, and a\nlock owner with the camera-pose calibration `running` (see\n`protocol/wire-format.md` §10 and §11)."},"1797":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-98","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#what-autocalibrate-changes","content":"`false` (dev default): with a missing or stale pose, a client may not start\na calibration; an operator runs `--calibrate-camera-pose` on the server."},"1798":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-99","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#what-autocalibrate-changes","content":"`true`: a client that holds the setup lock may start the calibration\nitself, and the server holds normal media until the result is committed.\nUntil the network layer exists no client can connect, so the only visible\ndifference today is `WAITING_FOR_CALIBRATION` instead of `NEEDS_SETUP` in\nthe log."},"1799":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-100","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#what-autocalibrate-changes","content":"In both modes, recalibrating a valid pose is allowed, only one client (or the\nconsole) can hold the setup lock at a time, and other clients keep their\nnormal control connection."},"1800":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-101","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#recalibrating-a-valid-setup","content":"While a new run is in progress the committed poses stay in use and the server\nstays ready (media is paused for setup). If the run fails, the old poses stay\nvalid and the state carries the message\n`last calibration attempt failed: ...`. A cancelled or interrupted run leaves\nthe previous calibration and its revision unchanged."},"1801":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-102","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#troubleshooting","content":"Message or symptom"},"1802":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-103","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#troubleshooting","content":"Cause and fix"},"1803":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-104","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#troubleshooting","content":"`--calibrate-camera-pose requires --live <config.yaml>`"},"1804":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-105","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#troubleshooting","content":"Add `--live config/dev/live.yaml`."},"1805":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-106","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#troubleshooting","content":"`--print-charuco-board only writes the board; run --calibrate-camera-pose separately`"},"1806":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-107","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#troubleshooting","content":"Run the two commands one after the other."},"1807":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-108","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#troubleshooting","content":"`calibration.board needs squares_x, squares_y >= 2, 0 < marker_length_m < square_length_m (metres) and a dictionary name`"},"1808":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-109","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#troubleshooting","content":"Fix the `calibration.board` values."},"1809":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-110","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#troubleshooting","content":"`--calibrate-camera-pose requires streams.alignment: color_to_depth`"},"1810":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-111","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#troubleshooting","content":"Set `streams.alignment: color_to_depth`. Other alignments give no depth-camera pose."},"1811":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-112","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#troubleshooting","content":"`setup state not built: client-facing setup requires streams.alignment=color_to_depth`"},"1812":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-113","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#troubleshooting","content":"Same cause, on a normal `--live` run: no calibration state is built."},"1813":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-114","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#troubleshooting","content":"Progress shows `camX=no board`"},"1814":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-115","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#troubleshooting","content":"The board is too small or far away, there is glare, the light is too low, or `board.dictionary` or the square counts do not match the print. Move closer, avoid reflections, check the config."},"1815":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-116","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#troubleshooting","content":"Corners detected but observations do not increase"},"1816":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-117","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#troubleshooting","content":"Views are rejected when fewer than 8 corners are found, when the fitted pose has more than 2 px RMS reprojection error, or when the pose is ambiguous (small, distant or face-on board). Hold the board closer and tilted, keep it still for a moment to avoid motion blur, and make sure it is flat. Views also need two cameras at once and at least 2 cm or 3° of movement since the last one."},"1817":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-118","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#troubleshooting","content":"`camera-pose calibration timed out after 120000 ms: accepted N of 20 observations`"},"1818":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-119","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#troubleshooting","content":"Not enough usable views in two minutes. Restart the command and keep the board in two cameras' views while moving it."},"1819":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-120","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#troubleshooting","content":"`... cameras cam1 did not see the board together with a calibrated camera in at least 5 consistent observations; inconsistent pairs: cam0-cam1 (... mm RMS)`"},"1820":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-121","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#troubleshooting","content":"The shared views of that pair disagree by more than 15 mm RMS. Common causes: a bent board, a board moving during capture, or cameras that are not in hardware sync. Check `sync` in the config and hold the board still in each position."},"1821":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-122","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#troubleshooting","content":"A failed run in console mode"},"1822":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-123","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#troubleshooting","content":"The server logs `camera-pose calibration run 1 failed: ...` and keeps running without a new calibration. Stop it with Ctrl+C and start the command again."},"1823":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-124","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#troubleshooting","content":"`camera_pose_calibration=stale (... serial changed from A to B)`"},"1824":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-125","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#troubleshooting","content":"A camera was swapped. Recalibrate."},"1825":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-126","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#troubleshooting","content":"`camera_pose_calibration=stale (... depth geometry changed from 640x576 to ...)`"},"1826":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-127","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#troubleshooting","content":"`streams.depth` resolution changed. Recalibrate, or restore the resolution."},"1827":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-128","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#troubleshooting","content":"`camera_pose_calibration=stale (camera cam2 is not calibrated)`"},"1828":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-129","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#troubleshooting","content":"A camera was added, or a camera `id` was renamed. Recalibrate."},"1829":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-130","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#troubleshooting","content":"Distances between cameras are off by a constant factor"},"1830":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-131","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#troubleshooting","content":"`board.square_length_m` does not match the printed square. Measure it and recalibrate."},"1831":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-132","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#troubleshooting","content":"`config/dev/camera-pose.json` appears in `git status`"},"1832":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-133","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#troubleshooting","content":"`server/.gitignore` ignores `config/*/camera-pose.json`, so the file shows up only when it is already tracked because someone committed it. The file belongs to one physical rig. To stop tracking it, run `git rm --cached config/dev/camera-pose.json`. To commit a new version on purpose, use `git add -f config/dev/camera-pose.json`."},"1833":{"id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration-134","page_id":"/docs/server/camera-calibration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/camera-calibration#troubleshooting","content":"The depth-to-code table is calibrated separately; see\nDepth quantization calibrator."},"1834":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","type":"page","content":"Capture and synchronisation","breadcrumbs":["HSLU OrbbecStreamer","Server","How it works"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync"},"1835":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-0","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","content":"How the server opens the cameras, synchronises them in hardware and in time, aligns colour to depth and groups frames from all cameras into batches."},"1836":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-1","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#cameras-and-roles","content":"Cameras and roles"},"1837":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-2","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#hardware-sync-and-delays","content":"Hardware sync and delays"},"1838":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-3","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#time-sync","content":"Time sync"},"1839":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-4","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#colour-to-depth-alignment","content":"Colour-to-depth alignment"},"1840":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-5","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#frame-batching","content":"Frame batching"},"1841":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-6","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#frame-set-and-batch-numbers","content":"Frame-set and batch numbers"},"1842":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-7","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#capture-profiles","content":"Capture profiles"},"1843":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-8","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#latency-frame-rate-and-colour-timing","content":"Latency: frame rate and colour timing"},"1844":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-9","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#limits-and-guarantees","content":"Limits and guarantees"},"1845":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-10","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"1846":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-11","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#related-pages","content":"Related pages"},"1847":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-12","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","content":"The capture side turns several Orbbec cameras into one stream of\nsynchronised multi-camera batches: one colour + depth frame set per camera,\nall taken at the same moment. It uses the cameras' trigger cable for\nexposure sync, the Orbbec SDK's global timestamps for time sync, and a\nframe batcher that matches frame sets across cameras by timestamp. The code\nis in `server/src/camera/` (`OrbbecCameraProvider`, `CameraRig`,\n`FrameBatcher`)."},"1848":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-13","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#cameras-and-roles","content":"At start-up the server waits up to `run.camera_wait_timeout_ms` for the\ncameras listed in `cameras`, matched by `serial_number`. A missing camera is\nlogged and left out; the server runs with the ones it found (see\nConfiguration). Inside the server a camera is\ncalled `orbbec:<serial>`; logs, recordings and clients use your config `id`\ninstead."},"1849":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-14","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#cameras-and-roles","content":"`sync.enabled`"},"1850":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-15","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#cameras-and-roles","content":"Roles used"},"1851":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-16","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#cameras-and-roles","content":"`true`"},"1852":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-17","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#cameras-and-roles","content":"The camera with `role: primary` drives the trigger; every other camera is a secondary. Exactly one primary is required."},"1853":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-18","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#cameras-and-roles","content":"`false`"},"1854":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-19","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#cameras-and-roles","content":"Every camera runs free (standalone). `role` has no effect, but at most one camera may be `primary`."},"1855":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-20","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#cameras-and-roles","content":"The start-up order matters for hardware sync: the server writes the sync\nsettings to every camera first, starts the secondaries, and starts the\nprimary last, so every secondary is armed before the first trigger. Frames\nare passed on only after every camera is streaming and the clock sync below\nis enabled; earlier frames are discarded."},"1856":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-21","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#cameras-and-roles","content":"The server does not reassign the primary role. If the primary camera is\nmissing at start-up, the secondaries get no trigger."},"1857":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-22","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#hardware-sync-and-delays","content":"With `sync.enabled: true` the server programs each camera's multi-device sync\nsettings and reads the role back. A mismatch stops start-up with\n`Orbbec synchronization role readback mismatch for camera <id>`."},"1858":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-23","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#hardware-sync-and-delays","content":"Setting"},"1859":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-24","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#hardware-sync-and-delays","content":"Applied to"},"1860":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-25","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#hardware-sync-and-delays","content":"Default"},"1861":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-26","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#hardware-sync-and-delays","content":"Dev config"},"1862":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-27","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#hardware-sync-and-delays","content":"Depth delay"},"1863":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-28","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#hardware-sync-and-delays","content":"Secondary *n* (in config order): *n* × `secondary_depth_delay_step_us`; primary 0"},"1864":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-29","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#hardware-sync-and-delays","content":"150 µs step"},"1865":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-30","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#hardware-sync-and-delays","content":"160 µs step"},"1866":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-31","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#hardware-sync-and-delays","content":"`color_delay_us`"},"1867":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-32","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#hardware-sync-and-delays","content":"Every camera"},"1868":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-33","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#hardware-sync-and-delays","content":"0"},"1869":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-34","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#hardware-sync-and-delays","content":"0"},"1870":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-35","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#hardware-sync-and-delays","content":"`trigger_to_image_delay_us`"},"1871":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-36","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#hardware-sync-and-delays","content":"Every camera"},"1872":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-37","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#hardware-sync-and-delays","content":"0"},"1873":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-38","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#hardware-sync-and-delays","content":"0"},"1874":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-39","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#hardware-sync-and-delays","content":"`trigger_out_enable`, `trigger_out_delay_us`"},"1875":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-40","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#hardware-sync-and-delays","content":"Every camera"},"1876":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-41","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#hardware-sync-and-delays","content":"`true`, 0"},"1877":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-42","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#hardware-sync-and-delays","content":"`true`, 0"},"1878":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-43","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#hardware-sync-and-delays","content":"`frames_per_trigger`"},"1879":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-44","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#hardware-sync-and-delays","content":"Every camera"},"1880":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-45","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#hardware-sync-and-delays","content":"1"},"1881":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-46","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#hardware-sync-and-delays","content":"1"},"1882":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-47","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#hardware-sync-and-delays","content":"The depth delay staggers the time-of-flight exposures so the cameras' IR\nillumination does not interfere. The start-up log shows what each camera\naccepted:"},"1883":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-48","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#hardware-sync-and-delays","content":"`mode=4` is the primary and `mode=8` a secondary. The keys are in\nConfiguration."},"1884":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-49","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#time-sync","content":"Hardware sync makes the cameras expose together; the timestamps make that\nvisible to the server."},"1885":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-50","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#time-sync","content":"The server enables the SDK's **global timestamp** on every camera before\nit starts streaming. The SDK maps each camera's device clock to the host\nclock, so timestamps of different cameras are comparable. A camera\nwithout global-timestamp support stops start-up with\n`Orbbec global timestamps are required ...`."},"1886":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-51","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#time-sync","content":"After all cameras stream, the server enables the SDK's **device clock\nsync** once for all cameras, every 60 s (`interval_ms=60000` in the log)."},"1887":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-52","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#time-sync","content":"Frame sets whose timestamp is 0 (global timestamps not ready yet) are\ndropped."},"1888":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-53","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#time-sync","content":"A frame set's timestamp is its depth frame's global timestamp. See\nHow the server works for how it maps to the\nsteady clock and the wire."},"1889":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-54","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#colour-to-depth-alignment","content":"`streams.alignment` selects the SDK's alignment filter, which runs on each\ncamera's capture thread, on the CPU:"},"1890":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-55","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#colour-to-depth-alignment","content":"Value"},"1891":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-56","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#colour-to-depth-alignment","content":"Result"},"1892":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-57","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#colour-to-depth-alignment","content":"Use"},"1893":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-58","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#colour-to-depth-alignment","content":"`color_to_depth` (default)"},"1894":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-59","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#colour-to-depth-alignment","content":"Colour is resampled into the depth image; both are depth-sized (640 × 576 in the dev config)"},"1895":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-60","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#colour-to-depth-alignment","content":"Required for client-facing setup, RVM, camera-pose calibration and encoding with the dev profiles"},"1896":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-61","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#colour-to-depth-alignment","content":"`depth_to_color`"},"1897":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-62","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#colour-to-depth-alignment","content":"Depth is resampled into the colour image"},"1898":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-63","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#colour-to-depth-alignment","content":"Local experiments only; no client-facing setup state is built"},"1899":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-64","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#colour-to-depth-alignment","content":"`disabled` (`none`)"},"1900":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-65","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#colour-to-depth-alignment","content":"No alignment"},"1901":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-66","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#colour-to-depth-alignment","content":"Local experiments only; encoding fails unless colour and depth have the same size"},"1902":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-67","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#colour-to-depth-alignment","content":"Clients always get colour aligned to the depth camera and depth-camera\nintrinsics. Moving alignment and colour conversion to the GPU is planned\n(latency plan step 8)."},"1903":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-68","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#frame-batching","content":"The batcher turns per-camera frame sets into batches:"},"1904":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-69","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#frame-batching","content":"Each camera has a short list of frame sets waiting for partners, at most\n`sync.maximum_pending_frame_sets_per_camera` (default 4). When it is\nfull, the oldest one is dropped."},"1905":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-70","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#frame-batching","content":"Once every camera has a waiting frame set, the batcher compares the\noldest one of each camera. If their timestamps lie within\n`sync.timestamp_tolerance_us` (default 2000 µs, dev config 5000 µs), they\nbecome one batch."},"1906":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-71","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#frame-batching","content":"Otherwise the frame set with the earliest timestamp can never match and\nis dropped; the batcher tries again with the next one."},"1907":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-72","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#frame-batching","content":"Frame sets that repeat or go back in number are dropped."},"1908":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-73","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#frame-batching","content":"So a batch always has one frame set from **every** active camera, in config\norder. There are no partial batches: if one camera delivers nothing, no\nbatches are produced. Unmatched frame sets are dropped silently in `--live`;\nyou see them as `capture` below each camera's `frame_sets/s` in\nthe telemetry. `--orbbec-live-sync-test` reports\nthe measured skew (Run the server)."},"1909":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-74","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#frame-batching","content":"The batch's timestamp is the latest of its cameras' timestamps, and the\nspread between cameras is kept with it. In the 2026-09-26 baseline the\ncameras' frame sets reached the batcher 2.8–4.3 ms apart at p50 and\n15–16 ms at p99 (`arrival_skew`); that is the time the batcher waits for the\nslower camera."},"1910":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-75","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#frame-set-and-batch-numbers","content":"Number"},"1911":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-76","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#frame-set-and-batch-numbers","content":"Counts"},"1912":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-77","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#frame-set-and-batch-numbers","content":"Starts at"},"1913":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-78","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#frame-set-and-batch-numbers","content":"Frame-set number"},"1914":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-79","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#frame-set-and-batch-numbers","content":"Frame sets received by one camera's capture thread"},"1915":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-80","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#frame-set-and-batch-numbers","content":"0 per camera. It also counts frames discarded during start-up, so numbers of different cameras are not aligned."},"1916":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-81","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#frame-set-and-batch-numbers","content":"Batch number"},"1917":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-82","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#frame-set-and-batch-numbers","content":"Batches emitted by the batcher"},"1918":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-83","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#frame-set-and-batch-numbers","content":"0"},"1919":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-84","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#frame-set-and-batch-numbers","content":"An encoded bundle's frame-set number is the camera's frame-set number in\n`per_camera` mode and the batch number in `concatenated_batch` mode. Colour\nand depth of one bundle always carry the same number."},"1920":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-85","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#capture-profiles","content":"All cameras use the same `streams` profile\n(Configuration). The SDK rejects a profile the\ncamera does not offer when the camera starts."},"1921":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-86","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#capture-profiles","content":"Supported by the server"},"1922":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-87","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#capture-profiles","content":"Dev config"},"1923":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-88","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#capture-profiles","content":"Depth"},"1924":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-89","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#capture-profiles","content":"`depth_u16`, any size and rate the camera offers"},"1925":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-90","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#capture-profiles","content":"640 × 576 at 15 fps"},"1926":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-91","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#capture-profiles","content":"Colour"},"1927":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-92","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#capture-profiles","content":"`rgb8`, `bgr8`, `gray8`"},"1928":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-93","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#capture-profiles","content":"1280 × 720 at 15 fps, `rgb8`"},"1929":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-94","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#capture-profiles","content":"Encoding, RVM and the bilateral depth filter need `rgb8` colour."},"1930":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-95","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#capture-profiles","content":"With encoding on, colour and depth `fps` must be equal."},"1931":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-96","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#capture-profiles","content":"The Femto Bolt offers colour at 1280 × 720 in 5, 15, 25 and 30 fps. `rgb8`\nand `bgr8` are converted from the camera's format by the SDK, on the CPU."},"1932":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-97","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#latency-frame-rate-and-colour-timing","content":"Most of the end-to-end latency is on the camera side, before the SDK\ndelivers a frame set. From the baseline of 2026-09-26\n(`server/docs/architecture/latency-review/baseline-2026-09-26.md`; two\nFemto Bolts, 15 fps, `rgb8`):"},"1933":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-98","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#latency-frame-rate-and-colour-timing","content":"Measured"},"1934":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-99","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#latency-frame-rate-and-colour-timing","content":"p50"},"1935":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-100","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#latency-frame-rate-and-colour-timing","content":"p99"},"1936":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-101","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#latency-frame-rate-and-colour-timing","content":"Capture → depth received by the host"},"1937":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-102","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#latency-frame-rate-and-colour-timing","content":"94.4 ms"},"1938":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-103","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#latency-frame-rate-and-colour-timing","content":"98.6 ms"},"1939":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-104","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#latency-frame-rate-and-colour-timing","content":"Capture → colour received by the host"},"1940":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-105","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#latency-frame-rate-and-colour-timing","content":"134.2 ms"},"1941":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-106","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#latency-frame-rate-and-colour-timing","content":"146.8 ms"},"1942":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-107","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#latency-frame-rate-and-colour-timing","content":"SDK colour conversion and frame sync (`sdk_internal`)"},"1943":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-108","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#latency-frame-rate-and-colour-timing","content":"8.7–10.5 ms"},"1944":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-109","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#latency-frame-rate-and-colour-timing","content":"12.8–14.9 ms"},"1945":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-110","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#latency-frame-rate-and-colour-timing","content":"CPU alignment (`align`)"},"1946":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-111","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#latency-frame-rate-and-colour-timing","content":"2.5–4.1 ms"},"1947":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-112","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#latency-frame-rate-and-colour-timing","content":"6.3–7.6 ms"},"1948":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-113","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#latency-frame-rate-and-colour-timing","content":"**Colour arrives after depth.** At 15 fps colour reaches the host about\n40 ms after depth (8–13 ms at 30 fps in the SDK probe). The SDK holds depth until the\nmatching colour frame is there, so every frame set waits for colour. This\nhappens in the camera and USB path, not in the server."},"1949":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-114","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#latency-frame-rate-and-colour-timing","content":"**30 fps is much faster.** In a single-camera SDK probe, 30 fps cut the\ncamera-side latency by about 64–66 ms compared with 15 fps, whatever the\ncolour format. The server still runs the rig at 15 fps: 30 fps has not\nbeen validated with RVM, the encoder settings and hardware sync (roadmap\nPerformance step 1b)."},"1950":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-115","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#latency-frame-rate-and-colour-timing","content":"The capture timestamps come from the SDK's clock mapping, so absolute\ncapture-to-host numbers may carry a constant offset. Comparisons between\nruns are valid."},"1951":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-116","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#limits-and-guarantees","content":"**One camera model per rig.** All cameras must report the same model\nname and share one capture profile."},"1952":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-117","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#limits-and-guarantees","content":"**Orbbec only.** `vendor` accepts only `orbbec`."},"1953":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-118","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#limits-and-guarantees","content":"**No hot-plug.** The camera set is fixed at start-up. A camera that fails\nor is unplugged while running ends its capture thread (logged as\n`Orbbec capture error: ...` when the SDK reports an error); the server keeps\nrunning but produces no more batches. Restart it."},"1954":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-119","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#limits-and-guarantees","content":"**Bounded memory.** Frame sets waiting for partners are limited per\ncamera; nothing on the capture side can grow without bound."},"1955":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-120","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#limits-and-guarantees","content":"**No waiting on later stages.** The capture thread only pushes into the\nupload queue, which drops its oldest batch when full."},"1956":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-121","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#troubleshooting","content":"Sync and start-up failures (`propertyId: 1038`, role readback mismatch,\nmissing cameras) are in Run the server. Low\nbatch rates, skew and uneven cameras are in\nRead the telemetry."},"1957":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-122","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#related-pages","content":"How the server works"},"1958":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-123","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#related-pages","content":"Configuration: `sync` and `streams`"},"1959":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-124","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#related-pages","content":"Camera calibration"},"1960":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-125","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#related-pages","content":"Latency"},"1961":{"id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync-126","page_id":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/capture-and-sync#related-pages","content":"Read the telemetry"},"1962":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","type":"page","content":"Configuration","breadcrumbs":["HSLU OrbbecStreamer","Server","Get started"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/configuration"},"1963":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-0","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration","content":"The live YAML config file, every option it accepts, and how to check a config before you run it."},"1964":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-1","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/configuration#the-config-directory","content":"The config directory"},"1965":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-2","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/configuration#point-the-server-at-a-config","content":"Point the server at a config"},"1966":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-3","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/configuration#check-a-config-without-cameras","content":"Check a config without cameras"},"1967":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-4","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/configuration#file-format","content":"File format"},"1968":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-5","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/configuration#minimal-example","content":"Minimal example"},"1969":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-6","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/configuration#option-reference","content":"Option reference"},"1970":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-7","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/configuration#run","content":"`run`"},"1971":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-8","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/configuration#setup","content":"`setup`"},"1972":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-9","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/configuration#cameras","content":"`cameras`"},"1973":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-10","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/configuration#sync","content":"`sync`"},"1974":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-11","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/configuration#streams","content":"`streams`"},"1975":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-12","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/configuration#mask","content":"`mask`"},"1976":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-13","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/configuration#processing","content":"`processing`"},"1977":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-14","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/configuration#encoding","content":"`encoding`"},"1978":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-15","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/configuration#calibration","content":"`calibration`"},"1979":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-16","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/configuration#preview","content":"`preview`"},"1980":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-17","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/configuration#debug_recording","content":"`debug_recording`"},"1981":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-18","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/configuration#telemetry","content":"Telemetry"},"1982":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-19","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/configuration#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"1983":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-20","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration","content":"The live pipeline reads one YAML file that lists the cameras, capture\nprofiles, synchronisation, GPU processing, encoding, calibration and debug\nrecording. The development config is `server/config/dev/live.yaml`. The\nparser is `server/src/config/LiveConfig.cpp`; this page follows it."},"1984":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-21","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#the-config-directory","content":"Only `live.yaml` is checked in. The two JSON files are created on the\nmachine that owns the cameras. When they are missing the server still starts:\nit uses a linear depth mapping and reports that setup (camera-pose\ncalibration) is needed."},"1985":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-22","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#the-config-directory","content":"Every relative path in the config (`rvm_engine_path`,\n`quantization_profile_path`, `camera_pose_path`, `debug_recording.directory`)\nis resolved against the working directory. Run the server from `server/`."},"1986":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-23","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#point-the-server-at-a-config","content":"The option depends on the command:"},"1987":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-24","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#point-the-server-at-a-config","content":"Command"},"1988":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-25","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#point-the-server-at-a-config","content":"Config option"},"1989":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-26","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#point-the-server-at-a-config","content":"Default"},"1990":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-27","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#point-the-server-at-a-config","content":"Live pipeline"},"1991":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-28","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#point-the-server-at-a-config","content":"`--live <file>`"},"1992":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-29","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#point-the-server-at-a-config","content":"none; required"},"1993":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-30","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#point-the-server-at-a-config","content":"Local camera-pose calibration"},"1994":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-31","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#point-the-server-at-a-config","content":"`--live <file> --calibrate-camera-pose`"},"1995":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-32","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#point-the-server-at-a-config","content":"none; required"},"1996":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-33","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#point-the-server-at-a-config","content":"Print the ChArUco board"},"1997":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-34","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#point-the-server-at-a-config","content":"`--print-charuco-board <png> [--live <file>]`"},"1998":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-35","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#point-the-server-at-a-config","content":"built-in board if `--live` is absent"},"1999":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-36","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#point-the-server-at-a-config","content":"Synchronised-capture test"},"2000":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-37","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#point-the-server-at-a-config","content":"`--orbbec-live-sync-test [--config <file>]`"},"2001":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-38","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#point-the-server-at-a-config","content":"`config/dev/live.yaml`"},"2002":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-39","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#point-the-server-at-a-config","content":"Depth quantization calibrator"},"2003":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-40","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#point-the-server-at-a-config","content":"`orbbec_streamer_depth_quantization_calibrator [--config <file>]`"},"2004":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-41","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#point-the-server-at-a-config","content":"`config/dev/live.yaml`"},"2005":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-42","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#point-the-server-at-a-config","content":"`--config` of `orbbec_streamer` is read only by `--orbbec-live-sync-test`. To\nrun the live pipeline use `--live`. `config/dev/live.yaml` describes the\ndevelopment rig (its camera serials, hardware sync, the RVM mask and full debug\nrecording), so copy and adapt it first; see\nAdapt the config to your rig."},"2006":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-43","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#point-the-server-at-a-config","content":"Use `build/dev-relwithdebinfo/` instead of `build/dev-debug/` for the\noptimised build."},"2007":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-44","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#check-a-config-without-cameras","content":"The loader rejects an unknown key, a bad value or an inconsistent combination\nbefore any camera is opened. There are two checks."},"2008":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-45","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#check-a-config-without-cameras","content":"**Parse and validate the file.** Printing the calibration board loads the\nconfig through the same loader and does not touch cameras:"},"2009":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-46","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#check-a-config-without-cameras","content":"Expected result: exit code 0 and a line such as"},"2010":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-47","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#check-a-config-without-cameras","content":"This check does not validate `mask.backend` or\n`processing.depth_filter_backend`; those names are checked when the live\npipeline starts."},"2011":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-48","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#check-a-config-without-cameras","content":"**Full start-up check.** Copy the config, prefix every serial number so no\ncamera matches, disable the preview and shorten the camera wait. The server\nthen validates everything, logs the effective settings and stops because no\ncamera matches:"},"2012":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-49","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#check-a-config-without-cameras","content":"Expected result: the `live config`, `live streams`, `live mask`,\n`live processing` and `live encoding` log lines, then"},"2013":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-50","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#check-a-config-without-cameras","content":"Any other `orbbec-streamer failed:` message is a config error; see\nTroubleshooting. This only works when every camera has a\n`serial_number`; a camera without one matches any connected device. The check\nstops before the RVM engine file is opened, so a missing engine shows up only\nin a real run."},"2014":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-51","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#file-format","content":"The loader is a small line parser, not a full YAML implementation:"},"2015":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-52","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#file-format","content":"A line is `key: value`, a section header `key:` or a list item `- ...`.\nIndentation is ignored; a key belongs to the last section header above it."},"2016":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-53","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#file-format","content":"Unknown sections and unknown keys are errors, so typos are caught."},"2017":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-54","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#file-format","content":"`#` starts a comment, except inside double quotes. Strings may be\nquoted with `\"` or `'` or left bare."},"2018":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-55","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#file-format","content":"Booleans: `true`, `false`, `yes`, `no`, `1`, `0`."},"2019":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-56","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#file-format","content":"List items are allowed only under `cameras` and\n`debug_recording.camera_ids`. The only inline array is `mask.bbox_xywh`."},"2020":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-57","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#file-format","content":"Omitted keys take the defaults in the tables below. The defaults are the\ncode defaults, which sometimes differ from `config/dev/live.yaml`."},"2021":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-58","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#minimal-example","content":"One camera, no segmentation model (every pixel counts as foreground),\nencoding on, no preview window:"},"2022":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-59","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#minimal-example","content":"`fill_all` and `none` give the same depth here (colour aligned to depth, so\nboth have the depth resolution): without a mask the bilateral filter treats\nevery pixel as foreground. `fill_all` also produces a mask image\n(all 255) for the preview and the encoder; `none` skips that work."},"2023":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-60","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#minimal-example","content":"Without `serial_number` the server takes the first Orbbec camera it finds.\nThis file passes both checks above (add a `serial_number` for the start-up\ncheck)."},"2024":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-61","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#run","content":"Key"},"2025":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-62","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#run","content":"Type"},"2026":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-63","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#run","content":"Default"},"2027":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-64","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#run","content":"Description"},"2028":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-65","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#run","content":"`camera_wait_timeout_ms`"},"2029":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-66","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#run","content":"integer"},"2030":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-67","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#run","content":"`5000`"},"2031":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-68","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#run","content":"How long start-up waits for all configured cameras to appear. After the timeout the server continues with the cameras it found."},"2032":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-69","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#run","content":"`preview`"},"2033":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-70","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#run","content":"bool"},"2034":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-71","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#run","content":"`true`"},"2035":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-72","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#run","content":"Opens a local OpenCV preview window. It runs on its own thread and shows the newest frame it can keep up with, so it never blocks the capture, processing or encoding threads. It holds one colour frame's GPU buffer while it draws. Disabled automatically, with a warning, when neither `DISPLAY` nor `WAYLAND_DISPLAY` is set."},"2036":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-73","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#setup","content":"Used by the depth quantization cal