-quantization-calibrator#config-keys-it-reads","content":"Default for `--uniform-mix`."},"2471":{"id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator-75","page_id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator#config-keys-it-reads","content":"`setup.maximum_duration_seconds`"},"2472":{"id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator-76","page_id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator#config-keys-it-reads","content":"`60`"},"2473":{"id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator-77","page_id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator#config-keys-it-reads","content":"Default for `--duration-s` (1–60)."},"2474":{"id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator-78","page_id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator#config-keys-it-reads","content":"`setup.warmup_seconds`"},"2475":{"id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator-79","page_id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator#config-keys-it-reads","content":"`5`"},"2476":{"id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator-80","page_id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator#config-keys-it-reads","content":"Discarded start of the run."},"2477":{"id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator-81","page_id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator#config-keys-it-reads","content":"`processing.bilateral_mask_threshold`"},"2478":{"id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator-82","page_id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator#config-keys-it-reads","content":"`32`"},"2479":{"id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator-83","page_id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator#config-keys-it-reads","content":"Minimum mask value (0–255) for a pixel to count."},"2480":{"id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator-84","page_id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator#config-keys-it-reads","content":"`cameras`, `sync`, `streams`, `mask`, `processing`"},"2481":{"id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator-85","page_id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator#config-keys-it-reads","content":"Same meaning as for the live server."},"2482":{"id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator-86","page_id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator#expected-result","content":"When a compatible profile already exists (no cameras are opened):"},"2483":{"id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator-87","page_id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator#expected-result","content":"A new calibration logs the selected cameras, then a start line and a result\nline of this form (numbers depend on your scene):"},"2484":{"id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator-88","page_id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator#expected-result","content":"`calibration_mae_mm(linear/selected)` compares the two profiles on your data.\n`maximum_gap_mm` is the largest step between neighbouring codes, so it is the\nworst-case resolution anywhere in the range.\n`rejected(upload/processing)` counts captured batches that a full queue\ndropped (the oldest one goes), and `upload_slot_drops` batches dropped because\nevery GPU upload slot was in use. Both only mean fewer samples; the profile is\nstill built from the rest."},"2485":{"id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator-89","page_id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator#the-profile-file","content":"The output is snake_case JSON (server-internal; the wire form is camelCase,\nsee `protocol/wire-format.md` §8). Abbreviated:"},"2486":{"id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator-90","page_id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator#the-profile-file","content":"On load the server checks the schema version, that entries 0, 1, 2, 1022 and\n1023 are `0, min, min, max, max`, and that the table never decreases. It then\nbuilds the 65,536-entry depth-to-code table once and uploads it to the GPU, so\nencoding stays one lookup per pixel."},"2487":{"id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator-91","page_id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator#what-the-live-server-shows","content":"At startup, `orbbec_streamer --live config/dev/live.yaml` logs one of:"},"2488":{"id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator-92","page_id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator#what-the-live-server-shows","content":"The server's setup state reports the depth-quantization calibration as\n`valid` when the file was loaded and `missing` (\"using the linear default\nprofile\") otherwise. Either way the server is ready: only the camera pose is\nrequired (see Camera pose calibration). The profile\nand its table are part of the setup metadata that clients receive; the\nnetwork listener that delivers it to browsers is not implemented yet. Running\na depth-quantization calibration from a client is also not supported yet (the\nserver rejects that calibration kind)."},"2489":{"id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator-93","page_id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator#troubleshooting","content":"Message or symptom"},"2490":{"id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator-94","page_id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator#troubleshooting","content":"Cause and fix"},"2491":{"id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator-95","page_id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator#troubleshooting","content":"`--config: File does not exist: config/dev/live.yaml`"},"2492":{"id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator-96","page_id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator#troubleshooting","content":"You are not in `server/`. `cd server` or pass an absolute `--config`."},"2493":{"id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator-97","page_id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator#troubleshooting","content":"`Existing depth profile range does not match live config; use --force to recalibrate`"},"2494":{"id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator-98","page_id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator#troubleshooting","content":"You changed `minimum_depth_mm` or `maximum_depth_mm`. Run again with `--force`."},"2495":{"id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator-99","page_id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator#troubleshooting","content":"Live server exits with `Depth quantization profile range does not match live config: <path>`"},"2496":{"id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator-100","page_id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator#troubleshooting","content":"Same cause, seen by the live server; it does not fall back to linear. Recalibrate with `--force`, or delete the file to use the linear profile."},"2497":{"id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator-101","page_id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator#troubleshooting","content":"`Required camera is unavailable: cam0` or `No configured cameras are available for depth calibration`"},"2498":{"id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator-102","page_id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator#troubleshooting","content":"Check USB and power, the `serial_number` values in `cameras`, and that no other process holds the cameras. Raise `run.camera_wait_timeout_ms` if the cameras enumerate slowly."},"2499":{"id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator-103","page_id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator#troubleshooting","content":"`Depth calibration collected no valid masked in-range samples`"},"2500":{"id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator-104","page_id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator#troubleshooting","content":"Nothing in the foreground mask was inside the range. Put a person in view, check the depth range, lower `processing.bilateral_mask_threshold`, or make sure the run lasts longer than the warm-up."},"2501":{"id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator-105","page_id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator#troubleshooting","content":"`Calibration duration must be in [1, 60] seconds` / `Calibration duration must exceed setup.warmup_seconds`"},"2502":{"id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator-106","page_id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator#troubleshooting","content":"Fix `--duration-s` or the `setup` section."},"2503":{"id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator-107","page_id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator#troubleshooting","content":"`Adaptive uniform mix must be in [0, 1]`"},"2504":{"id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator-108","page_id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator#troubleshooting","content":"Fix `--uniform-mix` or `encoding.depth.adaptive_uniform_mix`."},"2505":{"id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator-109","page_id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator#troubleshooting","content":"Error while loading the RVM engine"},"2506":{"id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator-110","page_id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator#troubleshooting","content":"`mask.backend: rvm` needs the TensorRT engine at `mask.rvm_engine_path`. Build it, or calibrate with `mask.backend: fill_all` (then background pixels are counted too)."},"2507":{"id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator-111","page_id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator#troubleshooting","content":"`selected=linear` after a run"},"2508":{"id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator-112","page_id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator#troubleshooting","content":"The adaptive table was not better on your data, for example with a very even depth spread or `--uniform-mix 1`. Nothing to fix."},"2509":{"id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator-113","page_id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator#troubleshooting","content":"`config/dev/depth-quantization.json` appears in `git status`"},"2510":{"id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator-114","page_id":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/depth-quantization-calibrator#troubleshooting","content":"`server/.gitignore` ignores `config/*/depth-quantization.json`, so the file shows up only when it is already tracked because someone committed it. The file is specific to one room and camera setup. To stop tracking it, run `git rm --cached config/dev/depth-quantization.json`. To commit a new version on purpose, use `git add -f config/dev/depth-quantization.json`."},"2511":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","type":"page","content":"Encoding","breadcrumbs":["HSLU OrbbecStreamer","Server","How it works"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/encoding"},"2512":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-0","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding","content":"How the server encodes colour and depth with NVENC HEVC, its low-delay settings, bitrates, keyframes and encoder sessions."},"2513":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-1","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/encoding#how-it-works","content":"How it works"},"2514":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-2","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/encoding#low-delay-settings","content":"Low-delay settings"},"2515":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-3","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/encoding#bitrate-and-rate-control","content":"Bitrate and rate control"},"2516":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-4","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/encoding#gop-and-keyframes","content":"GOP and keyframes"},"2517":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-5","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/encoding#encoder-sessions","content":"Encoder sessions"},"2518":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-6","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/encoding#what-you-can-configure","content":"What you can configure"},"2519":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-7","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/encoding#measured-timing","content":"Measured timing"},"2520":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-8","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/encoding#limits-and-guarantees","content":"Limits and guarantees"},"2521":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-9","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/encoding#related-pages","content":"Related pages"},"2522":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-10","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding","content":"The server encodes every synchronised frame set on the GPU with NVENC. Colour\nand depth are two independent HEVC streams that together form one logical\nbundle. Encoding is on when `encoding.enabled: true`; the encoded bundles go\nto the debug recorder today and to browsers once serving exists (see\nServe to browsers)."},"2523":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-11","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#how-it-works","content":"One encoder thread takes processed batches from a short queue and encodes\ncolour, then depth, for each bundle:"},"2524":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-12","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#how-it-works","content":"Channel"},"2525":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-13","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#how-it-works","content":"Input"},"2526":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-14","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#how-it-works","content":"HEVC profile"},"2527":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-15","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#how-it-works","content":"Signal"},"2528":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-16","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#how-it-works","content":"Colour"},"2529":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-17","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#how-it-works","content":"RGB8 after colour-to-depth alignment, converted on the GPU to NV12"},"2530":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-18","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#how-it-works","content":"Main (8-bit 4:2:0)"},"2531":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-19","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#how-it-works","content":"BT.709, limited range, signalled in the VUI"},"2532":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-20","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#how-it-works","content":"Depth"},"2533":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-21","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#how-it-works","content":"Filtered depth in mm, converted on the GPU to one 10-bit code per pixel through the depth quantization LUT, stored in P010 luma"},"2534":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-22","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#how-it-works","content":"Main10 (10-bit 4:2:0)"},"2535":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-23","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#how-it-works","content":"Full range, no colour description"},"2536":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-24","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#how-it-works","content":"Both channels have the same size: one depth image per camera (640 × 576 with\nthe dev config), or all cameras side by side in `concatenated_batch` mode. The\ncode values, the reconstruction LUT and the tile layout are described in\nStream layout; how the LUT is fitted is\nin Depth quantization calibrator. The\nnormative bitstream definition is `protocol/wire-format.md` (§4, §6, §8)."},"2537":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-25","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#low-delay-settings","content":"Every session uses the same settings, set in `src/video/NvencHevcEncoder.cpp`.\nNone of them is configurable."},"2538":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-26","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#low-delay-settings","content":"Setting"},"2539":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-27","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#low-delay-settings","content":"Value"},"2540":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-28","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#low-delay-settings","content":"Effect"},"2541":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-29","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#low-delay-settings","content":"Preset / tuning"},"2542":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-30","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#low-delay-settings","content":"P1, ultra-low latency"},"2543":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-31","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#low-delay-settings","content":"Fastest preset"},"2544":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-32","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#low-delay-settings","content":"Frame types"},"2545":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-33","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#low-delay-settings","content":"I and P only (`frameIntervalP = 1`)"},"2546":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-34","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#low-delay-settings","content":"No B-frames, no reordering"},"2547":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-35","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#low-delay-settings","content":"Look-ahead"},"2548":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-36","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#low-delay-settings","content":"Off"},"2549":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-37","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#low-delay-settings","content":"The encoder never waits for later frames"},"2550":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-38","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#low-delay-settings","content":"Reorder delay"},"2551":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-39","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#low-delay-settings","content":"Zero (`zeroReorderDelay`)"},"2552":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-40","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#low-delay-settings","content":"Each input frame produces its access unit at once"},"2553":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-41","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#low-delay-settings","content":"Rate control"},"2554":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-42","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#low-delay-settings","content":"CBR, single pass, no adaptive