age_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#bitrate-and-rate-control","content":"Bitrates are set per camera in the config:"},"2566":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-54","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#bitrate-and-rate-control","content":"Key"},"2567":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-55","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#bitrate-and-rate-control","content":"Default"},"2568":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-56","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#bitrate-and-rate-control","content":"Applies to"},"2569":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-57","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#bitrate-and-rate-control","content":"`encoding.color.bitrate_bps`"},"2570":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-58","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#bitrate-and-rate-control","content":"12 000 000"},"2571":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-59","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#bitrate-and-rate-control","content":"Colour, per camera"},"2572":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-60","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#bitrate-and-rate-control","content":"`encoding.depth.bitrate_bps`"},"2573":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-61","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#bitrate-and-rate-control","content":"8 000 000"},"2574":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-62","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#bitrate-and-rate-control","content":"Depth, per camera"},"2575":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-63","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#bitrate-and-rate-control","content":"In `per_camera` mode each camera's encoders run at these rates. In\n`concatenated_batch` mode the single colour and depth encoders run at the\nrate times the number of cameras (two cameras: 24 and 16 Mbit/s). With the\ndefaults at 15 fps a colour access unit is about 100 kB per camera and a depth\naccess unit about 67 kB."},"2576":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-64","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#bitrate-and-rate-control","content":"The bitrate is fixed for the whole run. It also sets the HEVC level in the\ncodec string (see Stream layout). Adapting the\nbitrate to a client's network is planned with serving (latency plan step 9)\nand does not exist yet."},"2577":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-65","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#gop-and-keyframes","content":"**Periodic keyframes.** Every stream starts with an IDR and repeats one every\n`encoding.gop_length` frames (default 60, which is 4 s at 15 fps). `0` means\nan infinite GOP: only the first frame and on-demand keyframes are IDR."},"2578":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-66","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#gop-and-keyframes","content":"**Aligned per bundle.** Colour and depth of one bundle are always keyframes\non the same frame set: they share the GOP length and start together, and a\nforced keyframe is applied to both. This is accepted contract change 0006\npart A. In `concatenated_batch` the bundle is the whole rig (`multicam`); in\n`per_camera` each camera is its own bundle with its own keyframe cadence."},"2579":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-67","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#gop-and-keyframes","content":"**On-demand keyframes.** The encoder can force an aligned keyframe (IDR on\ncolour and depth, with parameter sets) on the next frame set of one bundle,\nor of every bundle. This is what a client needs after it joins, after the\nserver drops data for it, or after a stream rotation. Without it the client\nwaits up to a whole GOP."},"2580":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-68","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#gop-and-keyframes","content":"Requests are thread-safe and never block the encoder."},"2581":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-69","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#gop-and-keyframes","content":"Forced keyframes of one bundle are at least 250 ms apart (fixed)."},"2582":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-70","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#gop-and-keyframes","content":"Requests that arrive in between are coalesced into one keyframe."},"2583":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-71","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#gop-and-keyframes","content":"A request that arrives too early is deferred to the first frame set after\nthe 250 ms, never dropped."},"2584":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-72","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#gop-and-keyframes","content":"A periodic IDR serves pending requests, but does not delay the next forced\none."},"2585":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-73","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#gop-and-keyframes","content":"Status: the encoder side (`NvencEncodeStage::request_keyframe`) is\nimplemented and tested. Nothing calls it yet; the network layer will call it\non join, drop and rotation once serving exists. A client-facing keyframe\nrequest is proposed in contract change 0014."},"2586":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-74","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#encoder-sessions","content":"Layout"},"2587":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-75","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#encoder-sessions","content":"NVENC sessions"},"2588":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-76","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#encoder-sessions","content":"`concatenated_batch`"},"2589":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-77","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#encoder-sessions","content":"2 (one colour, one depth)"},"2590":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-78","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#encoder-sessions","content":"`per_camera`"},"2591":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-79","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#encoder-sessions","content":"2 per camera"},"2592":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-80","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#encoder-sessions","content":"Consumer GeForce drivers cap the number of concurrent NVENC sessions per\nsystem, and other encoders (another server instance, OBS, ffmpeg) count\nagainst it. With many cameras in `per_camera` mode the server can fail to\nopen a session; `concatenated_batch` needs only two. Check the current count\nwith `nvidia-smi --query-gpu=encoder.stats.sessionCount --format=csv`."},"2593":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-81","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#encoder-sessions","content":"In `per_camera` mode the cameras are encoded one after another on the same\nthread, and the bundles of a batch are handed off together after the last\ncamera."},"2594":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-82","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#what-you-can-configure","content":"All keys are in the `encoding` section; see\nConfiguration for types and validation."},"2595":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-83","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#what-you-can-configure","content":"Key"},"2596":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-84","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#what-you-can-configure","content":"Default"},"2597":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-85","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#what-you-can-configure","content":"What it changes"},"2598":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-86","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#what-you-can-configure","content":"`enabled`"},"2599":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-87","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#what-you-can-configure","content":"`false`"},"2600":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-88","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#what-you-can-configure","content":"Turns encoding on"},"2601":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-89","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#what-you-can-configure","content":"`session_mode`"},"2602":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-90","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#what-you-can-configure","content":"`per_camera`"},"2603":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-91","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#what-you-can-configure","content":"Stream layout; see Stream layout"},"2604":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-92","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#what-you-can-configure","content":"`gpu_ordinal`"},"2605":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-93","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#what-you-can-configure","content":"`0`"},"2606":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-94","page_id":"/docs/server/encoding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/encoding#what-you-can-configure","content":"CUDA device used by NVENC"},"2607":{"id":"/docs/server/encoding-95","p