r/getting-started-notes-12","page_id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes#requirements-in-brief","content":"CUDA toolkit 13 at `/usr/local/cuda`. Tested: 13.3."},"2661":{"id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes-13","page_id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes#requirements-in-brief","content":"TensorRT 11 C++ SDK. It is always needed to build. The RVM engine is needed\nonly for `mask.backend: rvm`. Tested: 11.1.0.106."},"2662":{"id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes-14","page_id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes#requirements-in-brief","content":"Orbbec SDK 2.8.7."},"2663":{"id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes-15","page_id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes#requirements-in-brief","content":"Orbbec cameras on USB 3, all the same model. Tested: 2 × Femto Bolt with\nfirmware 1.1.2, hardware-synchronised."},"2664":{"id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes-16","page_id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes#requirements-in-brief","content":"GCC 15 (`/usr/bin/g++-15`), CMake 3.25 or newer, Ninja."},"2665":{"id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes-17","page_id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes#requirements-in-brief","content":"Python 3.12 or newer with uv, only to build the RVM engine."},"2666":{"id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes-18","page_id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes#requirements-in-brief","content":"About 10 GB of disk for one build directory and the vcpkg cache."},"2667":{"id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes-19","page_id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes#install-commands-in-order","content":"Steps 2 to 5 need `sudo`. Skip step 3 if the machine already has driver 580+\nand CUDA 13 at `/usr/local/cuda`."},"2668":{"id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes-20","page_id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes#install-commands-in-order","content":"Clone the repository with its submodules:"},"2669":{"id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes-21","page_id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes#install-commands-in-order","content":"Without a GitHub SSH key, clone over HTTPS and fetch the submodules the\nsame way:"},"2670":{"id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes-22","page_id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes#install-commands-in-order","content":"Install the system packages:"},"2671":{"id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes-23","page_id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes#install-commands-in-order","content":"Install CUDA from NVIDIA's repository and the tested 580 driver from\nUbuntu, then reboot. This sequence has not been run on a fresh machine;\nsee Install for why the driver does\nnot come from `cuda-drivers`:"},"2672":{"id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes-24","page_id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes#install-commands-in-order","content":"Install TensorRT from the same repository. Plain `tensorrt-dev` installs\nthe newest build (`11.3.0.99-1+cuda13.4`); the tested one is\n`11.1.0.106-1+cuda13.3` (see Install):"},"2673":{"id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes-25","page_id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes#install-commands-in-order","content":"Install the Orbbec SDK. This also installs the udev rule for the cameras:"},"2674":{"id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes-26","page_id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes#install-commands-in-order","content":"Put CUDA on your shell's `PATH` (`make check-env` runs `nvcc`), then\nbootstrap vcpkg and check the toolchain (in `server/`):"},"2675":{"id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes-27","page_id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes#install-commands-in-order","content":"Configure, build and run the tests that need no camera (in `server/`). The\nfirst configure builds the vcpkg dependencies and takes a long time."},"2676":{"id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes-28","page_id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes#install-commands-in-order","content":"Check the GPU and the cameras (in `server/`):"},"2677":{"id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes-29","page_id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes#install-commands-in-order","content":"Optional: install uv with its official\ninstaller (it is not packaged for Ubuntu), open a new shell, then build the\nRVM segmentation engines (in `server/`):"},"2678":{"id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes-30","page_id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes#install-commands-in-order","content":"Expected results: step 7 ends with `100% tests passed, 0 tests failed out of\n38`. Step 8 ends with `NVENC capability test passed` and\n`Orbbec provider smoke test OK`."},"2679":{"id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes-31","page_id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes#what-a-new-user-can-do-today","content":"Build the server and run its tests and smoke tests."},"2680":{"id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes-32","page_id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes#what-a-new-user-can-do-today","content":"Run the live capture, GPU processing and encoding pipeline locally with\n`./build/dev-debug/orbbec_streamer --live config/local/live.yaml`. Run it\nfrom `server/`, because the config's paths are relative to the working\ndirectory. First copy `config/dev/live.yaml` and adapt it: it names the\ndevelopment rig's camera serials, enables hardware sync, uses the RVM mask\nand records to `debug/live`. See\nAdapt the config to your rig and\nConfiguration."},"2681":{"id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes-33","page_id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes#what-a-new-user-can-do-today","content":"Calibrate the camera poses and the depth quantization locally (see\nCamera pose calibration and\nDepth quantization calibrator)."},"2682":{"id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes-34","page_id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes#what-a-new-user-can-do-today","content":"Not yet available: the server does not serve browsers yet. The production\nWebTransport listener is not implemented. ADR 0002 proposes a gateway built\non Go `webtransport-go`, and a spike exists in `server/spike/webtransport`.\nThe `--websocket-test` flag is a placeholder, not a transport."},"2683":{"id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes-35","page_id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes#environment-variables","content":"The server code, CMake files and scripts read only the variables below. The\nscripts in `server/scripts/` read no environment variables; they find `git`,\n`nvcc`, `nvidia-smi` and `trtexec` on `PATH`."},"2684":{"id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes-36","page_id":"/docs/server/getting-started-notes","tags":[],"type