ontent":"Bilateral depth filter"},"2764":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-6","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#measured-cost","content":"Measured cost"},"2765":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-7","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#limits","content":"Limits"},"2766":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-8","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"2767":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-9","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#related-pages","content":"Related pages"},"2768":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-10","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","content":"After a multi-camera batch is formed, the server copies it to the GPU and\nruns two steps on every camera's frames: a **foreground mask** (which pixels\nbelong to the person) and a **depth filter** (edge-preserving smoothing that\nalso removes the background from depth). The result goes to the encoder.\nThe code is in `server/src/gpu/`, `server/src/processing/` and\n`server/src/segmentation/`."},"2769":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-11","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","content":"Colour-to-depth alignment is not part of this stage. It happens earlier, in\nthe Orbbec SDK on the CPU; see\nCapture and synchronisation."},"2770":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-12","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#upload","content":"The upload thread takes each batch from the upload queue and, for every\nframe:"},"2771":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-13","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#upload","content":"takes an **upload slot**: a pinned host buffer plus a GPU buffer of the\nframe's size;"},"2772":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-14","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#upload","content":"copies the frame from the SDK's memory into the pinned buffer (CPU);"},"2773":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-15","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#upload","content":"starts an asynchronous host-to-GPU copy on the upload CUDA stream and\nrecords a CUDA event that marks the copy as done."},"2774":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-16","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#upload","content":"The upload thread does not wait for the copy. A slot is reused only when no\nstage holds its frame any more and its copy has finished. Slots are created\non demand up to a limit that the server computes from the queue sizes (41\nwith `config/dev/live.yaml`); with those sizes, at most about 45 MB of\npinned host memory and the same on the GPU. When every slot is in use, the\nnew batch is dropped and counted; see\nRead the telemetry."},"2775":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-17","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#upload","content":"Measured (baseline of 2026-09-26, two cameras): upload queue + submit\n0.6–0.8 ms p50, 1.7–2.0 ms p99."},"2776":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-18","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#the-processing-stage","content":"The processing thread waits for the batch's upload events, runs the mask\nand the depth filter on its own CUDA stream for all cameras, waits for that\nstream to finish, and hands the batch to the encoder. The encoder then works\non a batch whose GPU data is complete."},"2777":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-19","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#the-processing-stage","content":"For each camera the processed batch contains:"},"2778":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-20","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#the-processing-stage","content":"Item"},"2779":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-21","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#the-processing-stage","content":"Size and format"},"2780":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-22","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#the-processing-stage","content":"Present when"},"2781":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-23","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#the-processing-stage","content":"Aligned colour"},"2782":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-24","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#the-processing-stage","content":"Depth size, RGB8 (the uploaded frame, unchanged)"},"2783":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-25","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#the-processing-stage","content":"Always"},"2784":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-26","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#the-processing-stage","content":"Raw depth"},"2785":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-27","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#the-processing-stage","content":"Depth size, 16-bit mm (the uploaded frame, unchanged)"},"2786":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-28","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#the-processing-stage","content":"Always"},"2787":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-29","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#the-processing-stage","content":"Foreground mask"},"2788":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-30","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#the-processing-stage","content":"Depth size, 8-bit, 0 = background, 255 = foreground"},"2789":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-31","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#the-processing-stage","content":"`mask.backend` is not `none`"},"2790":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-32","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#the-processing-stage","content":"Filtered depth"},"2791":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-33","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#the-processing-stage","content":"Depth size, 16-bit mm, 0 = invalid"},"2792":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-34","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#the-processing-stage","content":"`processing.depth_filter_backend` is not `none`"},"2793":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-35","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#the-processing-stage","content":"The encoder uses the filtered depth when there is one, otherwise the raw\ndepth. It encodes depth pixels whose mask value is 0 as \"invalid\" (code 0;\nsee Stream layout). Colour is never\nmasked."},"2794":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-36","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#foreground-mask-backends","content":"Set with `mask.backend` (Configuration):"},"2795":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-37","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#foreground-mask-backends","content":"Backend"},"2796":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-38","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#foreground-mask-backends","content":"What it does"},"2797":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-39","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#foreground-mask-backends","content":"Status"},"2798":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-40","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#foreground-mask-backends","content":"`rvm`"},"2799":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-41","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#foreground-mask-backends","content":"Robust Video Matting (MobileNetV3) on TensorRT, FP16. One inference for all cameras of a batch. Outputs a soft alpha matte (0–255). Keeps a recurrent state from frame to frame."},"2800":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-42","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#foreground-mask-backends","content":"The working segmenter. Needs a TensorRT engine (Install)."},"2801":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-43","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#foreground-mask-backends","content":"`fill_all`"},"2802":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-44","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#foreground-mask-backends","content":"Every pixel is foreground (255)."},"2803":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-45","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#foreground-mask-backends","content":"Test backend; use it to run without segmentation."},"2804":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-46","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#foreground-mask-backends","content":"`rgb_luma_threshold`"},"2805":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-47","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#foreground-mask-backends","content":"Foreground where the colour's luma is above 128 (fixed)."},"2806":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-48","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#foreground-mask-backends","content":"Test backend."},"2807":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-49","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#foreground-mask-backends","content":"`none`"},"2808":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-50","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#foreground-mask-backends","content":"No mask is produced."},"2809":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-51","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#foreground-mask-backends","content":"Works only with `depth_filter_backend: identity_copy` or `none`; see Limits."},"2810":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-52","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#foreground-mask-backends","content":"`sam3`"},"2811":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-53","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#foreground-mask-backends","content":"Placeholder: every pixel is foreground, like `fill_all`."},"2812":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-54","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#foreground-mask-backends","content":"Not a segmenter. It is the code default, so set `backend` explicitly."},"2813":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-55","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#foreground-mask-backends","content":"`tensorrt`, `onnxruntime`"},"2814":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-56","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#foreground-mask-backends","content":"-"},"2815":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-57","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#foreground-mask-backends","content":"Accepted by the config, then fail at the first batch with `Selected foreground mask backend is not implemented`."},"2816":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-58","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#foreground-mask-backends","content":"`mask.prompt_type`, `mask.text_prompt` and `mask.bbox_xywh` are passed to\nthe segmenter, but no current backend uses them."},"2817":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-59","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#the-rvm-engine","content":"The engine is built by `scripts/setup_rvm.py` for a fixed batch size,\nimage size and downsample ratio, all in its file name, for example\n`rvm_mobilenetv3_b2_640x576_ds0.5_float16.engine`: batch 2, 640 × 576,\nratio 0.5. At start-up the server checks the engine's tensors against:"},"2818":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-60","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#the-rvm-engine","content":"the number of **active** cameras (the batch size),"},"2819":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-61","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#the-rvm-engine","content":"the depth size (colour is aligned to it),"},"2820":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-62","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#the-rvm-engine","content":"`mask.rvm_downsample_ratio`."},"2821":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-63","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#the-rvm-engine","content":"A mismatch stops the server before the pipeline starts, after the cameras\nare opened. If a configured camera is missing, the active count drops and\nthe batch-2 engine no longer fits."},"2822":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-64","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#the-rvm-engine","content":"RVM's recurrent state carries over from one batch to the next. It is not\nreset when batches are dropped, so the matte can take a few frames to\nsettle after a stall."},"2823":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-65","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#bilateral-depth-filter","content":"`processing.depth_filter_backend: bilateral_cuda` (the default) runs a\ncolour-guided bilateral filter on each camera's depth\n(Configuration). For each depth pixel:"},"2824":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-66","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#bilateral-depth-filter","content":"If its mask value is below 128, the output is 0 (invalid). This is where\nthe background is removed. The threshold is fixed;\n`processing.bilateral_mask_threshold` does not change it."},"2825":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-67","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#bilateral-depth-filter","content":"Otherwise the output is a weighted mean of the non-zero depth values in a\nsquare window around it, using only foreground neighbours. The weight\nfalls off with pixel distance (spatial sigma) and with the RGB colour\ndifference to the centre pixel (colour sigma), so depth edges that follow\ncolour edges stay sharp."},"2826":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-68","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#bilateral-depth-filter","content":"A foreground pixel with no depth gets a value from its neighbours when any\nof them has one, so small holes are filled. With no valid neighbour it\nstays 0."},"2827":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-69","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#bilateral-depth-filter","content":"Key"},"2828":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-70","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#bilateral-depth-filter","content":"Default"},"2829":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-71","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#bilateral-depth-filter","content":"Effect"},"2830":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-72","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#bilateral-depth-filter","content":"`bilateral_radius_ratio`"},"2831":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-73","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#bilateral-depth-filter","content":"2/576"},"2832":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-74","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#bilateral-depth-filter","content":"Window radius = ratio × the smaller image side, rounded. 2 pixels (a 5 × 5 window) at 640 × 576."},"2833":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-75","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#bilateral-depth-filter","content":"`bilateral_spatial_sigma_ratio`"},"2834":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-76","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#bilateral-depth-filter","content":"2/576"},"2835":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-77","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#bilateral-depth-filter","content":"Spatial sigma = ratio × the smaller image side. 2 pixels at 640 × 576."},"2836":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-78","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#bilateral-depth-filter","content":"`bilateral_color_sigma`"},"2837":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-79","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#bilateral-depth-filter","content":"60"},"2838":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-80","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#bilateral-depth-filter","content":"Colour sigma in RGB units (0–255). `0` turns the colour term off (pure spatial filter)."},"2839":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-81","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#bilateral-depth-filter","content":"`bilateral_maximum_radius_pixels`"},"2840":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-82","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#bilateral-depth-filter","content":"16"},"2841":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-83","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#bilateral-depth-filter","content":"Upper limit for the resolved radius. A larger radius is an error, not clamped."},"2842":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-84","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#bilateral-depth-filter","content":"The other depth filter backends are `identity_copy` (copies depth\nunchanged) and `none` (no filtered depth; the encoder uses raw depth). With\neither one, the background is removed only where the mask is exactly 0: a\nsoft RVM matte keeps depth for every pixel above 0."},"2843":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-85","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#measured-cost","content":"From the baseline of 2026-09-26\n(`server/docs/architecture/latency-review/baseline-2026-09-26.md`: two\nFemto Bolts, 640 × 576 at 15 fps, RTX 4090, `dev-relwithdebinfo` build):"},"2844":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-86","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#measured-cost","content":"Stage"},"2845":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-87","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#measured-cost","content":"p50"},"2846":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-88","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#measured-cost","content":"p99"},"2847":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-89","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#measured-cost","content":"Upload (queue + staging + copy enqueued)"},"2848":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-90","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#measured-cost","content":"0.6–0.8 ms"},"2849":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-91","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#measured-cost","content":"1.7–2.0 ms"},"2850":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-92","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#measured-cost","content":"Processing, `fill_all` mask + bilateral filter, both cameras"},"2851":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-93","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#measured-cost","content":"0.25–0.48 ms"},"2852":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-94","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#measured-cost","content":"1.0–1.2 ms"},"2853":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-95","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#measured-cost","content":"RVM was not part of the baseline (no engine on the measuring host), so its\ncost is not measured yet. It adds to `processing` in the\nlatency report; at 15 fps the stage has\n66.7 ms per batch before it starts to drop."},"2854":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-96","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#limits","content":"**`mask.backend: none`** produces no mask; `bilateral_cuda` then treats\nevery pixel as foreground, which gives the same depth as `fill_all` when\ncolour is aligned to depth (`streams.alignment: color_to_depth`)."},"2855":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-97","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#limits","content":"**Colour must be `rgb8`** for `rvm`, `rgb_luma_threshold` and\n`bilateral_cuda`. With another colour format the simple masks are skipped\nand RVM and the bilateral filter stop the server."},"2856":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-98","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#limits","content":"**The radius limit is checked at the first batch**, not when the config is\nloaded: `Resolved bilateral radius exceeds maximum_radius_pixels`."},"2857":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-99","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#limits","content":"**The RVM engine is fixed** in batch size, image size and downsample\nratio. Changing the number of cameras or the depth profile needs another\nengine."},"2858":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-100","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#limits","content":"**Output buffers are pooled.** Masks and filtered depths come from a pool\nsized for everything in flight, so a running pipeline makes no GPU\nallocations or frees (a `cudaFree` waits for all GPU work: 50 ms during a\n50 ms kernel, against 0 µs for returning a buffer to the pool). The pool\ngrows during the first batches and then stays constant."},"2859":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-101","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#limits","content":"**One GPU.** Upload, processing and RVM use the default CUDA device;\n`encoding.gpu_ordinal` selects the device only for NVENC. Keep it at `0`\non a multi-GPU machine unless you have checked the setup."},"2860":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-102","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#troubleshooting","content":"Message or symptom"},"2861":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-103","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#troubleshooting","content":"Fix"},"2862":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-104","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#troubleshooting","content":"`orbbec-streamer failed: Resolved bilateral radius exceeds maximum_radius_pixels`"},"2863":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-105","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#troubleshooting","content":"Lower `bilateral_radius_ratio` or raise `bilateral_maximum_radius_pixels`."},"2864":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-106","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#troubleshooting","content":"`orbbec-streamer failed: Unexpected static TensorRT shape for ...`"},"2865":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-107","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#troubleshooting","content":"The engine does not match the active cameras or the depth size. Build the matching engine and set `mask.rvm_engine_path`."},"2866":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-108","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#troubleshooting","content":"`RVM requires exactly one usable RGB8 color frame per synchronized camera`, `Bilateral RGB input pointer is null` or `NVENC frame set is missing RGB8 color or DepthU16 input`"},"2867":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-109","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#troubleshooting","content":"Set `streams.color.format: rgb8`."},"2868":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-110","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#troubleshooting","content":"`Selected foreground mask backend is not implemented`"},"2869":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-111","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#troubleshooting","content":"`tensorrt` or `onnxruntime`. Use `rvm` or `fill_all`."},"2870":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-112","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#troubleshooting","content":"`process` drops rising in the telemetry"},"2871":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-113","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#troubleshooting","content":"See Read the telemetry."},"2872":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-114","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#related-pages","content":"How the server works"},"2873":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-115","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#related-pages","content":"Capture and synchronisation"},"2874":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-116","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#related-pages","content":"Configuration: `mask` and `processing`"},"2875":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-117","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#related-pages","content":"Encoding"},"2876":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-118","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#related-pages","content":"Stream layout"},"2877":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-119","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#related-pages","content":"Latency"},"2878":{"id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing-120","page_id":"/docs/server/gpu-processing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/gpu-processing#related-pages","content":"Depth quantization calibrator"},"2879":{"id":"/docs/server","page_id":"/docs/server","type":"page","content":"Server","breadcrumbs":["HSLU OrbbecStreamer","Server"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/server"},"2880":{"id":"/docs/server-0","page_id":"/docs/server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server","content":"The C++/CUDA server that captures, encodes and streams Orbbec camera data."},"2881":{"id":"/docs/server-1","page_id":"/docs/server","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server#status","content":"Status"},"2882":{"id":"/docs/server-2","page_id":"/docs/server","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server#where-to-start","content":"Where to start"},"2883":{"id":"/docs/server-3","page_id":"/docs/server","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/server#how-it-works","content":"How it works"},"2884":{"id":"/docs/server-4","page_id":"/docs/server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server","content":"The server captures colour and depth from one or more hardware-synchronised\nOrbbec cameras, aligns colour to depth in the Orbbec SDK, segments and filters\nthe frames on the GPU, and encodes colour (HEVC Main) and depth (HEVC Main10)\nwith NVENC.\nBrowsers will receive the streams