hands the frames to\nthe server. The server code adds about 6–8 ms typically and about 12 ms at\np99. Capture timestamps come from the camera clock mapped to the host clock,\nso absolute capture-relative numbers may carry a constant offset;\ndifferences and everything after the SDK are exact."},"3070":{"id":"/docs/server/latency-54","page_id":"/docs/server/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/latency#where-the-time-goes","content":"Not in the baseline: RVM segmentation (adds to GPU processing), the preview\nwindow, and the network (serving is not implemented yet; see\nServe to browsers)."},"3071":{"id":"/docs/server/latency-55","page_id":"/docs/server/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/latency#targets","content":"Proposed p99 budgets from the latency review. They are targets, not\nguarantees."},"3072":{"id":"/docs/server/latency-56","page_id":"/docs/server/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/latency#targets","content":"Segment"},"3073":{"id":"/docs/server/latency-57","page_id":"/docs/server/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/latency#targets","content":"Target"},"3074":{"id":"/docs/server/latency-58","page_id":"/docs/server/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/latency#targets","content":"Status"},"3075":{"id":"/docs/server/latency-59","page_id":"/docs/server/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/latency#targets","content":"SDK delivers → access unit handed off"},"3076":{"id":"/docs/server/latency-60","page_id":"/docs/server/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/latency#targets","content":"≤ 12 ms p99 (≤ 8 ms p50), RVM included"},"3077":{"id":"/docs/server/latency-61","page_id":"/docs/server/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/latency#targets","content":"Met at 11.5–12.3 ms without RVM; RVM not yet measured"},"3078":{"id":"/docs/server/latency-62","page_id":"/docs/server/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/latency#targets","content":"Access unit ready → bytes handed to QUIC"},"3079":{"id":"/docs/server/latency-63","page_id":"/docs/server/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/latency#targets","content":"≤ 0.5 ms p99 (≤ 0.2 ms p50)"},"3080":{"id":"/docs/server/latency-64","page_id":"/docs/server/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/latency#targets","content":"Needs serving; the WebTransport spike measured \\< 0.5 ms"},"3081":{"id":"/docs/server/latency-65","page_id":"/docs/server/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/latency#targets","content":"Drop or join → first aligned keyframe delivered"},"3082":{"id":"/docs/server/latency-66","page_id":"/docs/server/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/latency#targets","content":"≤ 2 frame intervals"},"3083":{"id":"/docs/server/latency-67","page_id":"/docs/server/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/latency#targets","content":"Encoder side ready (on-demand keyframes); needs serving"},"3084":{"id":"/docs/server/latency-68","page_id":"/docs/server/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/latency#targets","content":"Sensor → SDK delivery"},"3085":{"id":"/docs/server/latency-69","page_id":"/docs/server/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/latency#targets","content":"Measure first, then set"},"3086":{"id":"/docs/server/latency-70","page_id":"/docs/server/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/latency#targets","content":"Camera-side; see the frame-rate lever below"},"3087":{"id":"/docs/server/latency-71","page_id":"/docs/server/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/latency#what-the-server-does-to-avoid-adding-latency","content":"**Short latest-wins queues.** The upload, processing and encode queues hold\n2 batches each (encode: `encoding.queue_capacity`, default 2). A full queue\ndrops its oldest batch, so after a stall the pipeline continues with the\nnewest frames instead of working through a backlog. In a test with the\nencoder slowed to twice the frame period, batch → hand-off stayed at\n46 ms p50 / 67 ms p90, against 248 / 267 ms with the earlier deep queues."},"3088":{"id":"/docs/server/latency-72","page_id":"/docs/server/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/latency#what-the-server-does-to-avoid-adding-latency","content":"**Bounded GPU memory.** The number of upload slots is computed from\neverything that can hold a batch. If they still run out, the batch is\ndropped and counted; the server never stops for it."},"3089":{"id":"/docs/server/latency-73","page_id":"/docs/server/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/latency#what-the-server-does-to-avoid-adding-latency","content":"**Side paths on their own threads.** The preview window runs on its own\nthread and only takes a frame when it is idle; a 150 ms preview left the\nprocessing → encode hand-off at 8 µs p50. Debug recorders never block;\nthey drop and count instead."},"3090":{"id":"/docs/server/latency-74","page_id":"/docs/server/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/latency#what-the-server-does-to-avoid-adding-latency","content":"**Rate-limited logging.** Drop warnings are logged at most once per second\nper stage, with the number suppressed; the counters stay exact."},"3091":{"id":"/docs/server/latency-75","page_id":"/docs/server/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/latency#what-the-server-does-to-avoid-adding-latency","content":"**Low-delay encoding.** No B-frames, no look-ahead, zero reorder delay, a\none-frame VBV; see Encoding."},"3092":{"id":"/docs/server/latency-76","page_id":"/docs/server/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/latency#what-the-server-does-to-avoid-adding-latency","content":"**On-demand keyframes.** The encoder can force an aligned keyframe for one\nbundle (at most every 250 ms), so a client that joins or loses data does\nnot wait for the next periodic IDR (up to 4 s at the default GOP). The\nnetwork caller comes with serving."},"3093":{"id":"/docs/server/latency-77","page_id":"/docs/server/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/latency#what-the-server-does-to-avoid-adding-latency","content":"A slow consumer never blocks capture, GPU processing or NVENC."},"3094":{"id":"/docs/server/latency-78","page_id":"/docs/server/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/latency#the-biggest-lever-frame-rate","content":"The dev config captures at 15 fps. Measured on the cameras alone, 30 fps cuts\nthe camera-side latency by about 65 ms (colour arrival 133 → 68 ms with raw\nMJPG, 141 → 77 ms with YUYV; depth 93–96 → 60–64 ms). That is about ten times\nthe whole server pipeline, and it also halves the cost of any one-frame wait\n(67 ms → 33 ms)."},"3095":{"id":"/docs/server/latency-79","page_id":"/docs/server/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/latency#the-biggest-lever-frame-rate","content":"Switching to 30 fps is a pending product decision. It needs an RVM and NVENC\nheadroom check at 33 ms per frame, re-validation of the ToF interference and\nsync settings, and a bitrate and GOP review. No contract change is needed;\nthe frame rate is in the stream descriptor. The rate is set with\n`streams.depth.fps` and `streams.color.fps` (see\nConfiguration)."},"3096":{"id":"/docs/server/latency-80","page_id":"/docs/server/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/latency#measure-it-yourself","content":"Use the optimised build and log mode, so the latency reports are not\noverwritten:"},"3097":{"id":"/docs/server/latency-81","page_id":"/docs/server/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/latency#measure-it-yourself","content":"The server prints stage-by-stage percentiles every 5 s and for the whole\nsession at shutdown. Compare `sdk->handoff` (the server's own part) and\n`capture->handoff` (end to end on the server host) against the tables above.\nEvery metric is explained in\nRead the telemetry, with reference values in\nWhat good looks like."},"3098":{"id":"/docs/server/latency-82","page_id":"/docs/server/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/latency#measure-it-yourself","content":"Keep a quiet machine: CPU contention shows up as a higher `sdk->handoff` p99\nand `batch_wait`, because alignment runs on the CPU per camera."},"3099":{"id":"/docs/server/latency-83","page_id":"/docs/server/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/latency#plan-status","content":"The latency plan, from `ROADMAP.md` (Performance):"},"3100":{"id":"/docs/server/latency-84","page_id":"/docs/server/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/latency#plan-status","content":"Step"},"3101":{"id":"/docs/server/latency-85","page_id":"/docs/server/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/latency#plan-status","content":"What"},"3102":{"id":"/docs/server/latency-86","page_id":"/docs/server/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/latency#plan-status","content":"Status"},"3103":{"id":"/docs/server/latency-87","page_id":"/docs/server/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/latency#plan-status","content":"1"},"3104":{"id":"/docs/server/latency-88","page_id":"/docs/server/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/latency#plan-status","content":"Stage instrumentation and hardware baseline"},"3105":{"id":"/docs/server/latency-89","page_id":"/docs/server/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/latency#plan-status","content":"Done"},"3106":{"id":"/docs/server/latency-90","page_id":"/docs/server/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/latency#plan-status","content":"1b"},"3107":{"id":"/docs/server/latency-91","page_id":"/docs/server/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/latency#plan-status","content":"Capture at 30 fps"},"3108":{"id":"/docs/server/latency-92","page_id":"/docs/server/latency","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/latency#plan-status","content":"Pending product decision"},"3109":{"id":"/docs/server/laten