latency reports within a second.\nTo keep every report, use log mode:"},"3702":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-26","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#choose-the-display-mode","content":"`ORBBEC_STREAMER_STATUS_MODE`"},"3703":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-27","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#choose-the-display-mode","content":"Behaviour"},"3704":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-28","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#choose-the-display-mode","content":"unset"},"3705":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-29","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#choose-the-display-mode","content":"In-place display if stdout is a terminal, `TERM` is not `dumb` and `NO_COLOR` is unset; otherwise log mode."},"3706":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-30","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#choose-the-display-mode","content":"`log`"},"3707":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-31","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#choose-the-display-mode","content":"Every table is an ordinary log line. Use this for measurements and log files."},"3708":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-32","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#choose-the-display-mode","content":"`dashboard`"},"3709":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-33","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#choose-the-display-mode","content":"Always redraw in place."},"3710":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-34","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#choose-the-display-mode","content":"The in-place display is closed before the session summary is printed, so the\nsummary stays on screen."},"3711":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-35","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#rate-tables","content":"Example from a run with two Femto Bolt cameras at 15 fps,\n`session_mode: concatenated_batch` and debug recording on:"},"3712":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-36","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#rate-tables","content":"Rates are counts in the last interval (about 1 s) divided by its length, so\nsingle readings jump between 14 and 16 at 15 fps."},"3713":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-37","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#live-pipeline","content":"Row"},"3714":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-38","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#live-pipeline","content":"`fps`"},"3715":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-39","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#live-pipeline","content":"`dropped`"},"3716":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-40","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#live-pipeline","content":"`MiB/s`"},"3717":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-41","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#live-pipeline","content":"`capture`"},"3718":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-42","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#live-pipeline","content":"Synchronised batches (one frame set from every camera) per second."},"3719":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-43","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#live-pipeline","content":"-"},"3720":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-44","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#live-pipeline","content":"-"},"3721":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-45","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#live-pipeline","content":"`upload`"},"3722":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-46","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#live-pipeline","content":"Batches copied to the GPU per second."},"3723":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-47","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#live-pipeline","content":"Total batches dropped since start: evicted from the full upload queue (2 batches), plus batches dropped because every GPU upload slot was in use."},"3724":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-48","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#live-pipeline","content":"-"},"3725":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-49","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#live-pipeline","content":"`process`"},"3726":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-50","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#live-pipeline","content":"Batches through GPU processing (mask, depth filter) per second."},"3727":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-51","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#live-pipeline","content":"Total evicted from the full processing queue (2 batches)."},"3728":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-52","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#live-pipeline","content":"-"},"3729":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-53","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#live-pipeline","content":"`encode`"},"3730":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-54","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#live-pipeline","content":"Encoded camera views per second. With N cameras this is N × the batch rate, in both encoding modes."},"3731":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-55","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#live-pipeline","content":"Total evicted from the full encode queue (`encoding.queue_capacity`, default 2)."},"3732":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-56","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#live-pipeline","content":"Encoded colour + depth bitstream, MiB/s."},"3733":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-57","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#live-pipeline","content":"`preview`"},"3734":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-58","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#live-pipeline","content":"Preview frames shown per second (only with an open preview window). The preview runs on its own thread and shows the newest batch whenever it is free, so a rate below `capture` is normal and does not slow the pipeline."},"3735":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-59","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#live-pipeline","content":"-"},"3736":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-60","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#live-pipeline","content":"-"},"3737":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-61","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#live-pipeline","content":"`dropped` is a running total, not a rate, and it is exact. The queues are\nshort and \"latest wins\": a full queue drops its **oldest** batch and keeps the\nnew one, so after a stall the pipeline carries on with the newest frames\ninstead of working through a backlog. The stage then logs a warning, at most\none per second per stage, with the number of drops since its previous warning:"},"3738":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-62","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#live-pipeline","content":"The other two warnings are `processing queue full: dropped the oldest uploaded\nGPU batch` and `encode queue full: dropped the oldest processed GPU batch`. The\nfirst warning of a run reports `0 more`."},"3739":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-63","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#live-pipeline","content":"At start-up the server logs the queue sizes and how many GPU upload slots it\nreserved for them (here `config/dev/live.yaml`: two cameras, debug GPU-input\nrecording and the preview on):"},"3740":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-64","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#live-pipeline","content":"Each captured frame needs one upload slot until the encoder is done with its\nbatch; the count covers every batch the queues and stages can hold at once.\nIf they still run out, the batch is dropped and counted, and about once per\nsecond the server logs `upload slots exhausted: dropped N captured batch(es)\nin the last second ...`. The server keeps running."},"3741":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-65","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#camera-ingress","content":"One row per camera, counted where the Orbbec SDK hands frames to the server,\nbefore cross-camera batching."},"3742":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-66","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#camera-ingress","content":"Column"},"3743":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-67","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#camera-ingress","content":"Meaning"},"3744":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-68","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#camera-ingress","content":"`camera`"},"3745":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-69","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#camera-ingress","content":"Runtime camera id, `orbbec:<serial>`."},"3746":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-70","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#camera-ingress","content":"`frame_sets/s`"},"3747":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-71","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#camera-ingress","content":"Colour + depth pairs per second from this camera."},"3748":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-72","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#camera-ingress","content":"`frames/s`"},"3749":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-73","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#camera-ingress","content":"Individual frames per second (2 per frame set)."},"3750":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-74","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#camera-ingress","content":"`MiB/s`"},"3751":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-75","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#camera-ingress","content":"Raw frame bytes per second received from the SDK."},"3752":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-76","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#debug-recording-rates","content":"Shown only when debug recording is on."},"3753":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-77","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#debug-recording-rates","content":"Field"},"3754":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-78","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#debug-recording-rates","content":"Meaning"},"3755":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-79","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#debug-recording-rates","content":"`queues(in/out)`"},"3756":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-80","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#debug-recording-rates","content":"Batches waiting for the recorder: GPU inputs / encoded outputs."},"3757":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-81","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#debug-recording-rates","content":"`drops(in/out)`"},"3758":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-82","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#debug-recording-rates","content":"Total batches the recorder dropped because it fell behind. Recording never slows the pipeline; it drops instead."},"3759":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-83","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#debug-recording-rates","content":"`worker`"},"3760":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-84","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#debug-recording-rates","content":"`ok`, or `failed` after a recorder error (logged as `<name> debug worker disabled: <reason>`)."},"3761":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-85","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#debug-recording-rates","content":"`in_color`, `in_depth`"},"3762":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-86","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#debug-recording-rates","content":"Frames per second written to `gpu-input-*.mkv`."},"3763":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-87","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#debug-recording-rates","content":"`out_color`, `out_depth`"},"3764":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-88","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#debug-recording-rates","content":"Encoded access units per second received for recording."},"3765":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-89","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#debug-recording-rates","content":"`dec_color`, `dec_depth`"},"3766":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-90","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#debug-recording-rates","content":"Frames per second decoded locally (with `locally_decode_gpu_outputs`)."},"3767":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-91","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#debug-recording-rates","content":"`decoder`"},"3768":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-92","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#debug-recording-rates","content":"Colour/depth decoder backend, for example `ffmpeg-cuda`, or `disabled`."},"3769":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-93","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#debug-recording-rates","content":"The `multicam` row is the concatenated encoder output in\n`concatenated_batch` mode."},"3770":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-94","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#latency-report","content":"Every 5 s (a real window: two cameras at 15 fps, `concatenated_batch`,\n`mask.backend: fill_all`, no preview):"},"3771":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-95","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#latency-report","content":"Each line is one metric: the number of samples `n`, then the 50th, 99th and\n99.9th percentile and the maximum, in milliseconds. Metrics without samples\nare left out."},"3772":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-96","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#latency-report","content":"**p50** is the typical value. **p99** is exceeded by 1 in 100 samples;\nthis is the number to compare against targets. **p99.9** and **max** show\nrare stalls. With about 75 batches per 5 s window at 15 fps, p99, p99.9\nand max are close to the single worst sample; use the whole-session report for tails."},"3773":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-97","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#latency-report","content":"Percentiles are histogram bucket upper bounds with about 3 % resolution.\nThat is why the same values (for example `146.801`) repeat. `max` is exact."},"3774":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-98","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#latency-report","content":"All times are measured on the steady clock of the server. Metrics starting\nwith `capture` use the camera's global timestamp, which the SDK maps to the\nhost clock; they can include a constant offset. Differences between runs\nare still valid, and everything downstream of the SDK is exact."},"3775":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-99","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#latency-report","content":"Per-camera metrics count one sample per camera per batch, so their `n` is\ntwice the batch count with two cameras."},"3776":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-100","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#latency-report","content":"The report window starts when the pipeline starts, so the first report\nincludes start-up effects."},"3777":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-101","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#metrics","content":"In the order they are printed. *Per camera* metrics come from each camera's\nframe set; the others from the batch."},"3778":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-102","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#metrics","content":"Metric"},"3779":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-103","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#metrics","content":"From → to"},"3780":{"id":"/docs/server/telemetry-104","page_id":"/docs/server/telemetry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/telemetry#metrics","content":"What it contains"},"3781":{"id":"/docs/server/telem