0 s`:** the run hung. Reload\nthe page, and check the browser console."],[543,"**`failed` with `watchdog: not done after 90 s`:** the run hung. Reload\nthe page and check the browser console."],[1225,"**`Forced out of setup. The connection closed: …`:** the session ended.\nSelect **Back to servers**, wait until the card is live again (the\nclient reconnects by itself), then select **Set up** again."],[1224,"**`Forced out of setup. The setup lease expired.` in the middle of a\nrun:** the lock ran out. The client committed nothing. What the server\ndoes with a run whose lock ends is not defined by the protocol contract\nyet (change request 0012 is open); the mock server cancels it. Check\nthe connection (the card's network line and last close), then select\n**Enter setup again**. If the state line still shows `running`, the run\ncontinued on the server; otherwise start it again."],[154,"**`histogram: depth histogram has N bins, expected 1024`:** the server\nsent a histogram of the wrong size; the client does not draw it."],[153,"**`histogram: not reported by the server`:** the server sent no\nhistogram with its progress. The numbers above still apply."],[30,"**`last close: transport error: …` and status `error`:** the session could\nnot be opened."],[2854,"**`mask.backend: none`** produces no mask; `bilateral_cuda` then treats\nevery pixel as foreground, which gives the same depth as `fill_all` when\ncolour is aligned to depth (`streams.alignment: color_to_depth`)."],[269,"**`media` is `snapshot only, no media` although you want frames:**\n`client/reference/hevc-web/` is missing or incomplete; `fallbackReason`\nin the report says which. The scenario does not need media; the counts\nsimply stay at 0. See\nLatency for how to get the folder."],[1142,"**`Metadata is stale: a shared update was withheld.`:** shared updates\nare off, and another client changed something. Select\n**Refresh stale metadata**, or turn shared updates back on and then\nrefresh."],[221,"**`npm: command not found`:**"],[35,"**`Protocol version mismatch; cannot connect.`** or\n`last close: protocol error version-mismatch: …`: the server speaks\nanother major protocol version. Update the client or the server.\nThe client does not retry."],[1148,"**`Reconnect failed: …`:** the new session could not be opened. The\ntext after the colon is the reason, as in the **last close** line.\n`closed locally: server <id> is already connected through <entry>`\nmeans another card still shows that server: remove one of the two."],[1143,"**`Refresh server error <code>: <message>`:** the server could not\nanswer the refresh (from the mock server: `Refresh server error busy: …`).\nTry again."],[1141,"**`Release lock failed (no-lease)`:** this client does not hold the lock\nany more, for example because it expired. Nothing needs releasing."],[93,"**`renderer notes` in the panel:** expand them. They say why WebGPU was\nskipped, for example `WebGPU not supported`."],[90,"**`rendering-incompatible` on a desktop browser:** hardware acceleration\nmay be off. Turn on \"Use graphics acceleration when available\" in\nthe browser settings, then check `chrome://gpu` (Chrome or Edge) for\nWebGL2 and WebGPU status."],[511,"**`skipRevisions` does not make the client resync:** a forward revision\ngap is not treated as an error until change request 0007 is decided. Use\n`sendStaleRevision` to exercise the resync path."],[151,"**`Start rejected (<code>): <message>`** (or Cancel, Commit): the server\nrefused the request. The code and message are the server's own. From\nthe mock server, for example: `calibration-running` (another run is\nin progress), `calibration-not-running`, `not-lock-owner`."],[3044,"**11.5–12.3 ms**"],[3047,"**155–159 ms**"],[3048,"**168–172 ms**"],[1949,"**30 fps is much faster.** In a single-camera SDK probe, 30 fps cut the\ncamera-side latency by about 64–66 ms compared with 15 fps, whatever the\ncolour format. The server still runs the rig at 15 fps: 30 fps has not\nbeen validated with RVM, the encoder settings and hardware sync (roadmap\nPerformance step 1b)."],[3043,"**5.4–7.7 ms**"],[718,"**A local draft.** You change the placement in this browser. Your 3D\nview shows the draft at once, but nothing is sent to the server."],[3473,"**A recalibration keeps the server ready.** While a new run replaces a\nvalid pose, the committed poses stay in use, readiness stays `ready` and\nmedia is paused for setup. The log shows `CALIBRATING`."],[1226,"**A result was never committed:** a result comes into force only with\n**Commit**. When you leave or lose the lock, the client discards its\ncopy. Run the calibration again and commit it before leaving."],[1137,"**Acquire lock is refused:**"],[1083,"**Acquire lock**"],[1136,"**Acquire lock** on the card only holds the lock. To run calibrations, use\n**Set up**; it adopts a lock this client already holds."],[1133,"**Acquire lock** turns the label into `locked-by-me`, and the lock line\ncounts down from 15 s, restarting every 5 s. Other clients show\n`locked-by-other` and the name of this client."],[2408,"**Adaptive quantile**: codes are packed more densely at the depths your\nscene actually uses, so the quantization error is smaller where people are."],[2578,"**Aligned per bundle.** Colour and depth of one bundle are always keyframes\non the same frame set: they share the GOP length and start together, and a\nforced keyframe is applied to both. This is accepted contract change 0006\npart A. In `concatenated_batch` the bundle is the whole rig (`multicam`); in\n`per_camera` each camera is its own bundle with its own keyframe cadence."],[1047,"**Another client's lock** shows the expiry the server **last announced**,\nfor example `last announced expiry in 9 s`. The holder also renews every\n5 s, but this client learns the new expiry only if the server announces\nthe lock state again after each renewal. That re-announcement is the\nclient's proposal in change request 0008, not yet part of the protocol\ncontract. When the announced time has passed, the card shows\n`expiry passed as last announced; the server may have renewed it`: the\nlock may still be held, and the lock line changes only when the server\nannounces it."],[752,"**Arrow Up** and **Arrow Down** step by 0.01 m or 1°; hold **Shift**\nfor ten times that. The **−** and **+** buttons next to each field do\nthe same with the mouse."],[1177,"**Back to servers** once the session has ended;"],[1430,"**Batching.** The frame batcher waits until every camera has a frame set\nwhose capture timestamps lie within `sync.timestamp_tolerance_us`, then\nemits one batch. The batch always holds one frame set per camera, in\nconfig order."],[1294,"**Blending of overlapping cameras.** Where two cameras see the same\nsurface, both sets of points are drawn."],[3658,"**Both channels**"],[3088,"**Bounded GPU memory.** The number of upload slots is computed from\neverything that can hold a batch. If they still run out, the batch is\ndropped and counted; the server never stops for it."],[1954,"**Bounded memory.** Frame sets waiting for partners are limited per\ncamera; nothing on the capture side can grow without bound."],[593,"**Browser:**"],[186,"**Build:** writes `client/dist/index.html` and `client/dist/assets/` (the\nmain bundle, Babylon.js chunks that load on demand, and source maps)."],[1049,"**Bundle rows**, for example\n`bundle-cam0: 1 camera, available; ready, drawing`:"],[1048,"**Calibration rows** are highlighted when a kind has `failed`, or when\n`camera-pose` or `depth-quantization` is not `valid` (and not\n`running`): the server cannot stream until those two are valid. The\n`network` kind is per client and never blocks streaming."],[1036,"**calibration**"],[107,"**Camera pose**"],[652,"**Camera-pose calibration screen**, once the protocol contract defines\nit, and **network calibration** (change request 0018)."],[3954,"**Can I see my own camera in the browser today?** Not yet. WebTransport\nserving is not implemented (see Serve to browsers),\nso a browser cannot connect to a real server. Run\nFirst stream on the server instead;\noptionally preview a hand-built recording in the client (see\nPlay back .hevc recordings)."],[3046,"**Capture → hand-off** (`capture->handoff`)"],[1429,"**Capture.** Each camera has one capture thread. It takes a colour +\ndepth frame set from the Orbbec SDK, aligns colour to depth (in the SDK,\non the CPU) and passes the frame set to the batcher."],[37,"**Card `streaming` but `uploaded 0`:**"],[617,"**Certificates:**"],[520,"**Client A** has a 3D view (WebGPU or WebGL2; none if neither starts)\nand decodes with WebCodecs when the browser can."],[554,"**Client A** uses the app's own setup workspace, through the same\ncontroller the workspace's buttons use."],[521,"**Client B** has no 3D view."],[555,"**Client B** shows the app's server cards. It holds the lock in one\nstep and shows which revision is in force."],[926,"**Colour .hevc**: `colour.hevc`"],[1948,"**Colour arrives after depth.** At 15 fps colour reaches the host about\n40 ms after depth (8–13 ms at 30 fps in the SDK probe). The SDK holds depth until the\nmatching colour frame is there, so every frame set waits for colour. This\nhappens in the camera and USB path, not in the server."],[2855,"**Colour must be `rgb8`** for `rvm`, `rgb_luma_threshold` and\n`bilateral_cuda`. With another colour format the simple masks are skipped\nand RVM and the bilateral filter stop the server."],[3648,"**Colour**"],[1292,"**Coming soon**, tracked in `client/docs/development/ROADMAP.md` (Phase 2):"],[155,"**Commit accepted but the state line still shows the old revision:**\nthe new revision comes into force with the server's next update. It\nnormally follows at once; if it does not, check the card for\n`resynchronising` or a lost connection."],[765,"**Commit placement (expected revision N)** sends the draft to the server\nwith `N`, the revision the draft started from. The protocol names this\nexpected revision but does not define exactly what a server does with\nit; the expected behaviour, and what the mock server does, is to accept\nthe commit only while its placement is still at revision `N`. You need\nthe setup lock, which the setup workspace holds."],[800,"**Commit placement** says `committing a placement needs the setup lock`"],[806,"**Commit placement** says `the draft equals the server placement`"],[803,"**Commit placement** says `waiting for the server state to refresh`"],[719,"**Commit.** **Commit placement** sends the draft to the server. Only\nthen does it become the server's placement, with a new revision number."],[1025,"**Compatibility line**, shown only when something is missing:"],[36,"**Conflict:** two cards point at the same server (for example by IP\naddress and by host name). Remove one."],[1028,"**Conflict**, shown when another card already shows the same server id:\n`conflict: server capture-01 is already rendered by entry-1; this entry is disconnected`."],[26,"**Connect timeout:** a connection attempt that has not completed its\nhandshake after 10 s is closed as `connect timeout`."],[1175,"**Controls:**"],[1147,"**Counts at 0 and `ready, no frame yet` right after a reconnect:**\nexpected for a moment. The new session starts its counts from zero and\nwaits for its first frames. If they stay at 0, check that the server is\nstreaming and that no compatibility line is shown."],[265,"**Counts on this page.** Both clients are wired the same way: a GPU-free\nrenderer that accepts every upload and draws nothing. The counts are per\nsession, so after B's Reconnect they start again from zero, while A's keep\ngrowing. A card that shows `decoded pairs 0 · uploaded 0` and\n`ready, no frame yet` just after the reconnect has not received its new\nsession's first frames yet."],[1040,"**counts**"],[1059,"**Counts** belong to the current session, from its handshake on:"],[443,"**Decode check**"],[1318,"**decoded pairs** goes up, but **uploaded** does not and **dropped** does"],[3617,"**Decoders.** Browsers limit how many hardware video decoders can run at\nonce. Concatenated needs two whatever the camera count."],[927,"**Depth .hevc (Main10)**: `depth.hevc`"],[2267,"**Depth quantization profile.** At start-up the server looks for\n`quantization_profile_path`:"],[109,"**Depth quantization**"],[3652,"**Depth: `QuantizedP010V1`**"],[179,"**Dev server:** Vite prints `Local: http://localhost:5173/`."],[766,"**Discard draft** drops the draft. Your 3D view shows the server's\nplacement again. Nothing is sent."],[3201,"**Disk.** One build directory with its vcpkg dependencies takes about 5 GB.\nThe vcpkg binary cache in `~/.cache/vcpkg` takes about another 4.5 GB."],[3202,"**Display (optional).** The live preview window opens only when `DISPLAY` or\n`WAYLAND_DISPLAY` is set. Without a display, the server still runs and logs\nthat the preview is off."],[3955,"**Do I need the RVM segmentation model to get a first stream?** No.\n`mask.backend: \"fill_all\"` treats the whole frame as foreground and needs no\nmodel or engine file. Building the RVM engine is a separate, optional step;\nsee Install."],[256,"**Drop A's session** and **Drop B's session**: the mock server loses\nthat client's session."],[812,"**Edit placement** says `no server placement known yet`"],[815,"**Edit placement** says `the server placement is not rigid`"],[119,"**elapsed:** time since the run started, for example `1.0 s`;"],[1433,"**Encoding.** The encode thread converts colour to NV12 and depth to\n10-bit codes, encodes both with NVENC and builds an encoded bundle: one\nper batch in `concatenated_batch` mode, one per camera in `per_camera`\nmode (Stream layout)."],[1192,"**Enter setup again** moves focus to the heading too, since the button\ndisappears while the lock is requested."],[1178,"**Enter setup again** once the session has ended and the server is\nstill connected."],[753,"**Enter** applies the field. **Escape** shows the last applied values\nagain."],[91,"**Every server card says the browser lacks HEVC decoding:** the browser has no\nHEVC decoder for this platform. Try another browser or machine with GPU\nvideo decoding. The client still works for control and setup."],[1247,"**Every server in one scene.** Each server's cloud is placed with that\nserver's placement (where the server sits relative to its anchor). Two\nservers never mix, even if they use the same bundle names."],[1381,"**Expected result:** `--cuda-test` reports your GPU and ends\n`CUDA smoke test OK`; `--nvenc-test` reports `main10=true` and ends\n`NVENC capability test passed`. See\nBuild and test for the full output on\nthe reference machine, and its\nTroubleshooting table for every\nfailure message."],[257,"**Expire the lease**: the mock server expires the current lock."],[493,"**Faults:** `dropSession`, `closeSession`, `delaySession`,\n`stallSession` / `resumeSession`, `sendMalformed`, `skipRevisions`,\n`sendStaleRevision`, `refuseSnapshots`, `expireLease`."],[150,"**Forced out in the middle of a run:** the client commits nothing. What\nthe server does with a run whose lock ends is not defined by the\nprotocol contract yet (change request 0012 is open); the mock server\ncancels it. Check the state line when you are back in: if it still\nshows `running`, the run continued on the server. See\nSetup workspace."],[2011,"**Full start-up check.** Copy the config, prefix every serial number so no\ncamera matches, disable the preview and shorten the camera wait. The server\nthen validates everything, logs the effective settings and stops because no\ncamera matches:"],[1432,"**GPU processing.** The processing thread computes the foreground mask\nand filters depth, then hands the batch to the encoder."],[1434,"**Hand-off.** The bundle is recorded for the latency telemetry and passed\nto the debug recorder when output recording is on. This is where the\nnetwork server will take it."],[1642,"**Hardware tests** (label `hardware`) need Orbbec cameras. The\n`orbbec_live_sync_integration_test` opens the cameras by the serial numbers\nin `config/dev/live.yaml`. Edit that file to match your cameras (see\nConfiguration). `nvenc_hevc_round_trip_integration_test`\nalso has this label but needs only a GPU with NVENC. It decodes with the GPU when it can and falls back to FFmpeg software decoding."],[78,"**Headless Chromium 153 (snap) on Linux, over SSH, 2026-09-23:**"],[3618,"**HEVC level.** The server chooses the lowest HEVC level whose picture size,\nsample rate and Main-tier bitrate admit the stream. It uses the whole surface\nand the whole bitrate. With the dev profile (640 × 576 at 15 fps, 12 Mbit/s\ncolour and 8 Mbit/s depth per camera):"],[76,"**HEVC not supported for a channel:** the server card shows a line such as\n`Setup and control only: this browser lacks HEVC colour decoding and HEVC Main10 depth decoding.`"],[1298,"**Hidden-pixel debug view.** The renderer can show pixels closer or\nfarther than the depth range in blue and red. The client has no switch\nfor it."],[123,"**histogram:** how many pixels had each depth code. The chart covers\nthe valid codes 2 to 1022. The line under it gives the counts of the\nthree special codes: `invalid (0)`, `below minimum (1)` and\n`above maximum (1023)`. Switch the **scale** between `log` (the\ndefault, which keeps small counts visible) and `linear`."],[1022,"**Id line:** `serverId: …` (or `serverId: not known yet`), then the\nsource:"],[180,"**In the browser:** a dark 3D view beside a side panel on the\nright."],[494,"**Inspection:** `sessions()`, `sessionOf(clientId)`, `lockHolder()`,\n`snapshot()`, `metadataRevision`, `session.requestCounts`,\n`session.mediaStats(bundleId)`."],[3956,"**Is a missing `camera-pose.json` a problem?** No. The server starts in\n“needs setup” and keeps capturing, processing and encoding normally. See\nStartup states."],[3641,"**Keyframes.** Every stream starts with an IDR frame and repeats one every\n`encoding.gop_length` frames (60 frames is 4 s at 15 fps; `0` disables the\nperiod). The encoder can also force a keyframe on request, which serving\nwill use when a client joins or after it drops data for a slow client. Forced\nkeyframes for one bundle are at least\n250 ms apart. Within a bundle, colour and depth are always keyframes on the\nsame frame set."],[1029,"**Last close:** why the last session ended, for example\n`last close: transport error: …`."],[3642,"**Latency.** Both layouts encode each synchronised batch on one encoder\nthread with the same low-latency settings: CBR, a one-frame buffer, no\nB-frames and no look-ahead. Concatenated produces one larger frame per batch;\nper-camera produces N smaller frames one after another. Measure your rig with\nthe latency log rather than assuming one is faster."],[1038,"**layout**"],[1220,"**Leave setup (release lock)** closes the workspace, and every client\nshows the server `unlocked` again."],[1176,"**Leave setup (release lock)** while the session is active or\nacquiring the lock;"],[2407,"**Linear** (the default): the 1021 valid codes are spread evenly over\n`encoding.depth.minimum_depth_mm`..`maximum_depth_mm`. For the default\n500–5000 mm range one code step is about 4.4 mm."],[1046,"**Lock expiry.** The server sends the expiry in its own clock. The card\nconverts it into a countdown with the clock offset measured by clock\nsync. Until clock sync has a result, it shows the raw server time\ninstead, for example\n`expires at server time 16.000 s (clock offset not known yet)`. When the\ncountdown reaches zero before the server has announced the change, it\nshows `expiry time reached, waiting for the server`. While this client\nholds the lock, it renews it every 5 s, so the countdown restarts from\n15 s."],[1184,"**lock:** `held by this client, expires in 14 s`, as on the server card.\nThe client renews the lock every 5 s, so the countdown restarts from\n15 s. Until clock sync has a result it shows the server time instead,\nfor example `expires at server time 16.000 s (clock offset not known yet)`.\nWhile asking for the lock: `requested, not held yet`. After the session\nended: `not held by this client`."],[1034,"**lock**"],[3091,"**Low-delay encoding.** No B-frames, no look-ahead, zero reorder delay, a\none-frame VBV; see Encoding."],[928,"**Manifest .json**: `manifest.json`"],[3474,"**Media flows only when ready.** Streaming is `streaming` only when media is\nrequested, the pose is valid and no calibration is running. `--live`\nrequests media at start, so a valid pose shows `STREAMING` in the log. No\nbytes leave the server until serving exists."],[485,"**Media:** it comes from a recording (`.hevc` colour and depth files plus\na manifest), the same format as recording playback. Without a recording\nthe server has no media."],[3197,"**Model.** The only tested camera is the Orbbec Femto Bolt. The code talks to\nthe Orbbec SDK, not to a specific model, but all cameras in one rig must be\nthe same model."],[824,"**Move in 3D** shows `a placement commit is in progress`"],[3199,"**Multi-camera sync.** With more than one camera, one camera is the\n`primary` and the others are `secondary`. The primary sends a hardware\ntrigger to the secondaries. You set the roles and delays in the live config\n(`cameras[].role` and the `sync` block, see\nConfiguration). This repository does not document the\nsync cabling. Wire the cameras as described in Orbbec's multi-camera\nsynchronisation guide for your camera model."],[1065,"**Network budget:** `no budget yet` until the server sends one. After\nthat it reads, for example,\n`active 40.0 Mbit/s, server maximum 100.0 Mbit/s, safe for this client 35.0 Mbit/s, network compatible`:"],[1042,"**network**"],[111,"**Network**"],[1953,"**No hot-plug.** The camera set is fixed at start-up. A camera that fails\nor is unplugged while running ends its capture thread (logged as\n`Orbbec capture error: ...` when the SDK reports an error); the server keeps\nrunning but produces no more batches. Restart it."],[506,"**No media:** check all of the following."],[622,"**No server needed to try the client:** the \"Open recording\" form plays\n`.hevc` recordings as if they were servers. See\nPlay back .hevc recordings."],[1955,"**No waiting on later stages.** The capture thread only pushes into the\nupload queue, which drops its oldest batch when full."],[75,"**No WebCodecs:** `decoders: WebCodecs VideoDecoder is unavailable: control and setup only (§16).`"],[72,"**No WebGPU and no WebGL2:**\n`renderer: rendering-incompatible. Rendering incompatible: neither WebGPU nor WebGL2 is available. This browser can still connect as a control and setup client (§16); no point clouds are drawn.`"],[587,"**Node.js:**"],[605,"**None.** The client reads no environment variables: there is no\n`import.meta.env` or `process.env` use in `client/src/`. There are no\n`.env` files, and all configuration is in `client/vite.config.ts`."],[1296,"**Not available, and not on the roadmap yet:**"],[3358,"**Not yet available.** The server does not accept browser connections today.\n`--live` captures, processes and encodes, but hands the encoded bundles only\nto the debug recorder. There is no listening socket and no port to open."],[1018,"**Notes under the header**, shown only when they apply:"],[505,"**Nothing happens in a test:** a `ManualScheduler` only moves when you\ncall `advanceBy` or `advanceTo`, and replies need a few microtask turns\nto settle."],[92,"**Nothing works when opened from another machine by IP address:**\nplain `http://` is only a secure context on `localhost`. The page must\nbe served over HTTPS with a certificate that machine trusts; the\nrepository has no HTTPS dev configuration yet."],[591,"**npm:**"],[121,"**observed range:** for example `500 to 5000 mm`;"],[2579,"**On-demand keyframes.** The encoder can force an aligned keyframe (IDR on\ncolour and depth, with parameter sets) on the next frame set of one bundle,\nor of every bundle. This is what a client needs after it joins, after the\nserver drops data for it, or after a stream rotation. Without it the client\nwaits up to a whole GOP."],[3092,"**On-demand keyframes.** The encoder can force an aligned keyframe for one\nbundle (at most every 250 ms), so a client that joins or loses data does\nnot wait for the next periodic IDR (up to 4 s at the default GOP). The\nnetwork caller comes with serving."],[1951,"**One camera model per rig.** All cameras must report the same model\nname and share one capture profile."],[2859,"**One GPU.** Upload, processing and RVM use the default CUDA device;\n`encoding.gpu_ordinal` selects the device only for NVENC. Keep it at `0`\non a multi-GPU machine unless you have checked the setup."],[1241,"**One point per depth pixel.** Each point takes the colour of the same\npixel in the colour stream (the server aligns colour to depth before\nsending)."],[1242,"**Only valid depth is drawn.** The server marks every depth pixel with a\ncode. The viewer hides:"],[486,"**Open contract questions:** where the protocol contract is still open,\nthe mock follows the client's pending change requests (0007, 0008, 0009,\n0012, 0014), listed at the top of `mockServer.ts`. A real server may\nbehave differently until those are decided."],[225,"**Opened from another machine and nothing connects:** the dev server\nlistens on `localhost` only, and plain HTTP is a secure context only on\n`localhost`."],[1952,"**Orbbec only.** `vendor` accepts only `orbbec`."],[3200,"**OS.** Ubuntu 26.04 is the only tested OS. The presets hard-code\n`/usr/bin/gcc-15`, `/usr/bin/g++-15` and `/usr/local/cuda`."],[2858,"**Output buffers are pooled.** Masks and filtered depths come from a pool\nsized for everything in flight, so a running pipeline makes no GPU\nallocations or frees (a `cudaFree` waits for all GPU work: 50 ms during a\n50 ms kernel, against 0 µs for returning a buffer to the pool). The pool\ngrows during the first batches and then stays constant."],[3772,"**p50** is the typical value. **p99** is exceeded by 1 in 100 samples;\nthis is the number to compare against targets. **p99.9** and **max** show\nrare stalls. With about 75 batches per 5 s window at 15 fps, p99, p99.9\nand max are close to the single worst sample; use the whole-session report for tails."],[2008,"**Parse and validate the file.** Printing the calibration board loads the\nconfig through the same loader and does not touch cameras:"],[258,"**Pause for setup** and **Stop streaming**: server-side streaming\nchanges."],[2577,"**Periodic keyframes.** Every stream starts with an IDR and repeats one every\n`encoding.gop_length` frames (default 60, which is 4 s at 15 fps). `0` means\nan infinite GOP: only the first frame and on-demand keyframes are IDR."],[744,"**pitch (°)**"],[756,"**pitch** from -90° to 90°, **yaw** and **roll** from -180° to 180°;"],[1003,"**Playback runs too fast or too slow**: `frameRate` in the manifest sets\nthe speed. Set it to the rate the files were recorded at."],[1248,"**Point size.** Points are 2 pixels wide on WebGL2 and 1 pixel wide on\nWebGPU. WebGPU has no adjustable point size yet."],[1293,"**Point-size and splat settings**, and larger points on WebGPU."],[1644,"**Protocol conformance** (`protocol_conformance_tests`) reads the contract\nand test vectors from `../protocol`. If the contract lives elsewhere, set the\nCMake cache variable when you configure, with `<path>` replaced by the\nfolder that contains `wire-format.md`, `schema/` and `vectors/`:\n`cmake --preset dev-debug -DORBBEC_STREAMER_PROTOCOL_CONTRACT_DIR=<path>`."],[205,"**Query parameters:**"],[3090,"**Rate-limited logging.** Drop warnings are logged at most once per second\nper stage, with the number suppressed; the counters stay exact."],[3472,"**Readiness depends only on the camera pose.** A linear depth quantization\nprofile is usable without calibration, and network calibration is\nadvisory."],[209,"**Reading the result:** each page sets `body[data-state]` to `done` or\n`failed` and exposes its report on `window`, for example\n`window.__wiringCheckReport`."],[83,"**Real HEVC decoding in a browser has not been verified yet.**"],[767,"**Rebase on server placement (revision M)** appears when the draft is\nstale (see Troubleshooting). It keeps your pose and\nmakes revision `M` the base, so you can commit."],[27,"**Reconnect:**"],[1092,"**Reconnect**"],[122,"**reconstruction error:** for example `1.50 mm`;"],[1089,"**Refresh**"],[1086,"**Release lock**"],[1134,"**Release lock** returns every client to `unlocked`."],[1095,"**Remove**"],[456,"**Render check**"],[86,"**Rendering in headless Chromium with SwiftShader:**"],[1286,"**Reset to identity**, which puts the anchor back at the scene origin."],[747,"**roll (°)**"],[728,"**rotation:** for example `yaw 30.0 · pitch 0.0 · roll 0.0°`."],[1643,"**RVM smoke tests** (`smoke_rvm_engine_b1` and `smoke_rvm_engine_b2`, label\n`rvm`) need the engines in `models/rvm/generated/` (see\nInstall). Without them, CTest\nreports the two tests as `Not Run` and the run counts as failed. This does\nnot mean the code is broken."],[492,"**Scenario:** `setStreaming`, `setBundleAvailability`, and calibration\nscripts passed in `createMockServer({ calibration })`: duration,\nprogress interval, accepted or failed, new camera poses or a new depth\nprofile, and a depth-code histogram per progress message\n(`depthHistogram`; `syntheticDepthHistogram` in `src/dev/devMock.ts`\nis a ready-made one). The shell's \"Add mock server\" scripts a 6 s\ndepth-quantization run with that histogram."],[3042,"**SDK delivers → bundle handed off** (`sdk->handoff`)"],[621,"**Secure context:** the page itself must be one. `http://localhost:5173`\nqualifies. Opening the dev server from another machine by IP address\nover plain HTTP does not, and the repository has no HTTPS dev\nconfiguration yet."],[726,"**server placement:** the anchor and the revision, for example\n`anchor anchor-dev, revision 3`;"],[1179,"**session:** where the session is:"],[483,"**Sessions:** one `MockServer` holds one server state. Every client that\nopens it gets its own session, and a reconnect opens a new session."],[1228,"**Set up says `the setup workspace is open for <name>; leave it first`:**\nonly one workspace can be open. Leave that one first."],[1080,"**Set up**"],[1172,"**Set up** is available while another client holds the lock. Opening the\nworkspace then shows the refusal; see Troubleshooting."],[1167,"**Set up** is unavailable, with the reason under the button, when:"],[1219,"**Set up** opens the workspace. Within a moment the session line reads\n`active: this client holds the setup lock`, the lock line counts down\nfrom 15 s, and the status label is `locked-by-me`. Other clients show\n`locked-by-other` with this client's name."],[1135,"**Set up** replaces the server list with the setup workspace for this\nserver and takes the lock; leaving the workspace brings the cards back.\nSee Setup workspace."],[1070,"**Shared updates.** Calibration results and placement changes are\n*shared updates*: the server sends them to every client that asked for\nthem."],[1044,"**shared updates**"],[3087,"**Short latest-wins queues.** The upload, processing and encode queues hold\n2 batches each (encode: `encoding.queue_capacity`, default 2). A full queue\ndrops its oldest batch, so after a stall the pipeline continues with the\nnewest frames instead of working through a backlog. In a test with the\nencoder slowed to twice the frame period, batch → hand-off stayed at\n46 ms p50 / 67 ms p90, against 248 / 267 ms with the earlier deep queues."],[3089,"**Side paths on their own threads.** The preview window runs on its own\nthread and only takes a frame when it is idle; a 150 ms preview left the\nprocessing → encode hand-off at 8 µs p50. Debug recorders never block;\nthey drop and count instead."],[1030,"**Source issues:** a list of problems when a recording cannot be opened.\nSee Play back .hevc recordings."],[1174,"**Status label and title:** `Set up: <server name>`, with the card's\nstatus label (`locked-by-me` while you hold the lock)."],[1016,"**Status label:** one word derived from the server's state. See\nStatus labels."],[544,"**The 3D view stays empty:** the browser has no WebGPU or WebGL2, or no\nHEVC decoding. The scenario still passes; the report's `renderer` field\nsays which case applies."],[500,"**The app:** the side panel of http\\://localhost:5173/\nhas a \"Dev: mock server\" section. **Add mock server** adds a mock as a\nnew server card, with the source `mock mock://dev-mock-…`."],[1146,"**The card stays `error` with `reconnect scheduled`:** the client\nretries after 1 s, doubling the wait up to 30 s. Select **Reconnect** to\ntry at once. If it keeps failing, read the **last close** line and see\nAdd a server."],[228,"**The decode check reports a missing file, or the wiring or latency\ncheck fails after about 30 s with no pair uploaded:** the reference\nrecordings in `client/reference/hevc-web/` are missing. See above."],[286,"**The end-to-end benchmark** (`npm run bench:e2e`). It runs the client\nmedia path in Node with the browser parts simulated, and can compare two\ncommits."],[285,"**The latency check page** (`client/dev/latency-check.html`). It runs the\nprobe in a real browser over two recordings and shows the stage table."],[1140,"**The lock is gone after a reconnect:** expected. A lock never survives\na reconnect. Acquire it again."],[1144,"**The lock shows `expires at server time …`:** clock sync has not\nfinished. It needs a few round trips after connecting; the countdown\nappears by itself."],[224,"**The panel says `renderer: rendering-incompatible`:** see\nBrowser requirements."],[181,"**The panel:**"],[3834,"**The part the server code controls.**"],[284,"**The per-stage latency probe** (`client/src/connections/latencyProbe.ts`).\nIt times each frame through the client, from the last network byte to the\nanimation frame after the draw, and reports p50/p90/p99/max per stage.\nIt is off unless a pipeline asks for it. When off, no clock is read on the\nmedia path."],[2856,"**The radius limit is checked at the first batch**, not when the config is\nloaded: `Resolved bilateral radius exceeds maximum_radius_pixels`."],[149,"**The result was not committed:** a result waits for **Commit**. If you\nleft the workspace or lost the lock first, the client discarded its\ncopy (the exit box says\n`The client discarded the uncommitted depth quantization result.`).\nStart the run again and commit it."],[545,"**The run fails after you clicked controls on the page:** the scenario\nexpects to drive the workspaces itself. Reload and run it without\nclicking."],[576,"**The run fails after you pressed Expire the lease by hand:** expected;\nthe scenario expects to hold the lock in most steps. Reload and run it\nwithout pressing buttons."],[2857,"**The RVM engine is fixed** in batch size, image size and downsample\nratio. Changing the number of cameras or the depth profile needs another\nengine."],[616,"**The URL:** the user types it into the panel's \"Add server\" form. It\nmust be an absolute `https:` URL with no fragment."],[484,"**Time:** it comes only from the scheduler you pass in. With a\n`ManualScheduler`, every run is deterministic."],[1017,"**Title:** the server's name, or the URL until the server has answered."],[1149,"**To replay a recording:** **Reconnect** is unavailable while the card\nis connected. Select **Remove**, then open the recording again."],[727,"**translation:** for example `x 0.500 · y 0.000 · z 1.000 m`;"],[503,"**Two clients of one mock:** the\ncards check,\nsetup check and\nplacement check pages."],[1431,"**Upload.** The upload thread copies each frame into pinned host memory\nand starts an asynchronous copy to the GPU."],[3198,"**USB.** Each camera needs a USB 3 (SuperSpeed, 5 Gbit/s) connection. In\n`lsusb -t` the camera interfaces should show `5000M`, not `480M`."],[1283,"**used by:** the servers whose placement names it;"],[120,"**valid samples:** for example `4 000`;"],[1297,"**View toggles.** There are no switches for colour only, depth only or\nthe foreground mask. The viewer always shows coloured points."],[596,"**WebCodecs** with HEVC Main (colour) and HEVC Main10 (depth) for\npoint clouds."],[597,"**WebGPU or WebGL2** for drawing."],[595,"**WebTransport** for live servers."],[1295,"**WebXR (headset) viewing.**"],[653,"**WebXR:** viewing the scene in a headset."],[625,"**WebXR** (Phase 2)."],[131,"**When a button is unavailable**, the reason is written under it. While\na request is waiting for the server's answer, its button shows\n`in progress`."],[3958,"**Where do I ask about protocol or wire-format questions?**\n`protocol/wire-format.md` is the normative contract; cross-team changes go\nthrough `protocol/changes/` (see the repository root `CLAUDE.md`)."],[3957,"**Why can't I calibrate on the server and commit from the client?** The\nserver and client cannot connect to each other yet. See\nCalibration for what each side can do on its\nown."],[3640,"**Width limit.** A concatenated surface is `N × W` wide. The NVENC HEVC\nmaximum is reported by the capability test and is 8192 × 8192 on current\nGPUs, which allows 12 tiles of 640 pixels. Browser decoders may accept less."],[465,"**Wiring check**"],[738,"**x (m)**, **y (m)**, **z (m)**"],[741,"**yaw (°)**"],[3888,"\\< 0.01 ms"],[3889,"\\< 0.01 ms"],[1803,"`--calibrate-camera-pose requires --live <config.yaml>`"],[1809,"`--calibrate-camera-pose requires streams.alignment: color_to_depth`"],[3337,"`--calibrate-camera-pose requires streams.alignment: color_to_depth`"],[3257,"`--calibrate-camera-pose`"],[1655,"`--compression-test`"],[3269,"`--compression-test`"],[2438,"`--config PATH`"],[2491,"`--config: File does not exist: config/dev/live.yaml`"],[3284,"`--config`"],[3299,"`--config` does not select the config for `--live`; `--live` takes the file\nitself."],[2005,"`--config` of `orbbec_streamer` is read only by `--orbbec-live-sync-test`. To\nrun the