heck with real decoded HEVC frames in a browser\")."],[2961,"The presets add `/usr/local/cuda/bin` to `PATH` and `/usr/local/cuda/lib64` to\n`LD_LIBRARY_PATH` for CMake. To run `nvcc` and the tests from your own shell,\nadd them to `~/.bashrc` as well:"],[1587,"The presets compile CUDA code for compute capability 8.9 (RTX 40 series). The\nbinaries also carry `compute_89` PTX, which newer GPUs (compute capability\nabove 8.9) compile at startup, so those work without changes. On a GPU below\ncompute capability 8.9, for example an RTX 30 series card (8.6), the CUDA\nkernels fail to launch and you must build for your architecture."],[2702,"The presets prepend `/usr/local/cuda/bin` to your `PATH`"],[2706,"The presets prepend `/usr/local/cuda/lib64`. For a TensorRT tar install, add its `lib` folder yourself."],[2942,"The presets use `/usr/bin/gcc-15` and `/usr/bin/g++-15` for C++ and as the CUDA host compiler."],[2944,"The presets use the Ninja generator. They need CMake 3.25 or newer."],[2323,"The preview window itself is switched with `run.preview`."],[1491,"The processed batch, after the encode enqueue"],[1445,"The processing CUDA stream, the RVM TensorRT engine, masks and filtered depth"],[2760,"The processing stage"],[3932,"The processing thread is being descheduled (CPU contention). A slow preview window cannot cause this: it runs on its own thread."],[2776,"The processing thread waits for the batch's upload events, runs the mask\nand the depth filter on its own CUDA stream for all cameras, waits for that\nstream to finish, and hands the batch to the encoder. The encoder then works\non a batch whose GPU data is complete."],[2403,"The profile file"],[2388,"The profile was made for another depth range. Recalibrate with `--force`, or delete the file to use the linear mapping."],[1689,"The protocol contract changed and the server does not conform yet. This is expected: it is how the server team learns of a contract change."],[3935,"The recorder (disk, FFV1 encode or local decode) cannot keep up, or failed. The pipeline is unaffected."],[427,"The recordings are probably missing from `client/reference/hevc-web/`."],[437,"The render loop ticks that slowly because the renderer is software\n(SwiftShader, typical in headless Chromium)."],[193,"The renderer, with a synthetic two-camera scene"],[212,"The report JSON sits in a collapsed \"report JSON\" panel at the bottom\nright."],[3776,"The report window starts when the pipeline starts, so the first report\nincludes start-up effects."],[3485,"The revision in `camera-pose.json`; `0` without a file"],[3193,"The Robust Video Matting (RVM) engine file that TensorRT runs is needed only\nwhen:"],[750,"The rotation is applied as roll first, then pitch, then yaw\n(`R = Ry(yaw) · Rx(pitch) · Rz(roll)`). A positive yaw turns +Z towards\n+X."],[419,"The rotation line showed about 20 ms and 24 `isConfigSupported` calls."],[410,"The rotation line shows a first upload about 1.2 ms after a new stream,\nand about 12 ms after a reconnect. It shows 2 `isConfigSupported` calls."],[1058,"The row is highlighted when the bundle is unavailable or paused, or its\nrender status is a problem."],[1768,"The run needs 20 accepted views and gives up after 120 seconds."],[2762,"The RVM engine"],[2386,"The RVM engine has not been built, or `rvm_engine_path` is relative to another directory."],[2186,"The RVM engine is built for a fixed batch size (`b2` in the file name is two\ncameras) and a fixed geometry (`640x576`). It must match the number of active\ncameras and the depth size."],[1687,"The RVM engines are not built. Build them, or exclude them with `-LE rvm`."],[2985,"The RVM model and weights are GPL-3.0. Confirm that this licence suits you\nbefore you distribute the engine."],[2996,"The RVM submodule is not initialised, so `external/RobustVideoMatting` is an empty folder. Initialise the submodules as in Get the source."],[266,"The same scenario runs in Node on a simulated clock as part of\n`npm test` (`client/src/tests/serverCards.test.ts`)."],[541,"The same scenario runs in Node on a simulated clock as part of `npm test`\n(`client/src/tests/placementEditor.test.ts`)."],[573,"The same scenario runs in Node on a simulated clock as part of `npm test`\n(`client/src/tests/setupWorkspace.test.ts`)."],[1334,"The same server was added twice. Only one card per server is drawn."],[1774,"The saved file (`calibration.camera_pose_path`) looks like this. The matrix\nis column-major, in metres, so the last column (entries 12–14) is the\ntranslation:"],[247,"The scenario, in order:"],[527,"The scenario, in order:"],[560,"The scenario, in order:"],[2981,"The script needs PyTorch, torchvision, ONNX and NVIDIA ModelOpt. `pyproject.toml`\nand `uv.lock` pin them. Install them with uv.\nuv is not packaged for Ubuntu; install it with its official installer, which\nputs it in `~/.local/bin`, then open a new shell:"],[1509,"The SDK's global timestamp: the device clock mapped to the host clock. Every camera's clock is re-synchronised to the host every 60 s."],[502,"The section exists only in the dev server. A production build\n(`npm run build`) contains no mock code."],[143,"The section shows the state line and\n`Not available yet: waits for change request 0018.` Change request 0018\n(network calibration stream) is proposed, not yet part of the protocol\ncontract. It is tracked in `client/docs/development/ROADMAP.md`,\n\"Phase 1C — connections (remaining)\", item \"Temporary\nnetwork-calibration stream\"."],[142,"The section shows the state line and the red `TODO` placeholder, nothing\nelse. The camera-calibration screen is a placeholder; there is no way to\nstart a camera-pose calibration from the client yet. It is tracked in\n`client/docs/development/ROADMAP.md`, \"Phase 1D — UI\", item \"Focused\nsetup workspace; camera-calibration placeholder …\"."],[775,"The server accepted it; the new placement is on its way."],[2353,"The server always writes `setup.json` into `directory` after the cameras\nstart, even with recording off. It is a local debug file, not part of the\nclient protocol."],[1413,"The server and client each work well on their own today, but they cannot yet\ntalk to each other: WebTransport serving is not implemented (see\nServe to browsers). A working first stream today\nmeans running the server against your own camera and watching it capture,\nprocess and encode in real time: see First stream\nbelow."],[1212,"The server announced the lock free without a release from you."],[1550,"The server builds with CMake presets, Ninja and vcpkg. A small `Makefile` wraps\nthe common commands. This page covers configuring, building, building for a\ndifferent GPU and running the tests. Finish Install first. All\ncommands run in `server/`."],[2884,"The server captures colour and depth from one or more hardware-synchronised\nOrbbec cameras, aligns colour to depth in the Orbbec SDK, segments and filters\nthe frames on the GPU, and encodes colour (HEVC Main) and depth (HEVC Main10)\nwith NVENC.\nBrowsers will receive the streams over WebTransport; that serving path is not\navailable yet (see Serve to browsers)."],[2683,"The server code, CMake files and scripts read only the variables below. The\nscripts in `server/scripts/` read no environment variables; they find `git`,\n`nvcc`, `nvidia-smi` and `trtexec` on `PATH`."],[1856,"The server does not reassign the primary role. If the primary camera is\nmissing at start-up, the secondaries get no trigger."],[1885,"The server enables the SDK's **global timestamp** on every camera before\nit starts streaming. The SDK maps each camera's device clock to the host\nclock, so timestamps of different cameras are comparable. A camera\nwithout global-timestamp support stops start-up with\n`Orbbec global timestamps are required ...`."],[3183,"The server encodes colour with NVENC HEVC Main and depth with HEVC Main10, and\nruns its image processing in CUDA. The GPU's NVENC must support all of the\nfeatures below. `orbbec_streamer --nvenc-test` checks them and names any that\nare missing:"],[2522,"The server encodes every synchronised frame set on the GPU with NVENC. Colour\nand depth are two independent HEVC streams that together form one logical\nbundle. Encoding is on when `encoding.enabled: true`; the encoded bundles go\nto the debug recorder today and to browsers once serving exists (see\nServe to browsers)."],[3447,"The server keeps one authoritative setup state: whether the rig is\ncalibrated, whether media may flow, who holds the setup lock, and the\nrevisions clients need to interpret the media. Clients will read it from the\nsnapshot and follow its updates; today you see it in the server log. The wire\nform is defined in `protocol/wire-format.md` §10–§12 and §18."],[2927,"The server lives in `server/` of the monorepo. CMake also reads the protocol\ncontract in `../protocol`, so clone the whole repository with its submodules:"],[1822,"The server logs `camera-pose calibration run 1 failed: ...` and keeps running without a new calibration. Stop it with Ctrl+C and start the command again."],[509,"The server must be `streaming`, with the bundle available."],[1711,"The server needs a valid camera pose before it is ready to serve clients."],[3097,"The server prints stage-by-stage percentiles every 5 s and for the whole\nsession at shutdown. Compare `sdk->handoff` (the server's own part) and\n`capture->handoff` (end to end on the server host) against the tables above.\nEvery metric is explained in\nRead the telemetry, with reference values in\nWhat good looks like."],[779,"The server refused it. The draft is kept."],[1204,"The server refused the lock for another reason."],[1210,"The server rejected a renewal."],[3157,"The server runs on one Linux machine with an NVIDIA GPU and one or more Orbbec\ncameras connected over USB. This page lists what that machine needs and how to\ncheck each item. The next step is Install."],[816,"The server sent a placement with scale or shear."],[1762,"The server takes the setup lock as the local operator and starts a\ncalibration run. This works with `autocalibrate: false`, and it also\nrecalibrates an existing valid pose."],[3024,"The server treats latency as part of correctness: it must not add avoidable\ndelay on top of an uncertain network. This page explains where the time goes\ntoday, which targets apply, and what is still planned. All figures are from\nthe measured baseline of 2026-09-26\n(`server/docs/architecture/latency-review/baseline-2026-09-26.md`) unless\nmarked as a target. The plan behind them is\n`server/docs/architecture/latency-review-2026-09-26.md`."],[1580,"The server, with its built-in smoke tests"],[822,"The server's cloud is not in the 3D view right now (the session is still starting, or the card shows a conflict)."],[798,"The server's placement moved before your commit arrived (a rare race: normally the client blocks a stale commit first). `stale-revision` is the mock server's code; a real server may use another."],[3438,"The server's setup and readiness model, how it maps to the wire, the revisions, the setup lease, autocalibrate and setup.json."],[1331,"The server's setup for this bundle is not consistent."],[2488,"The server's setup state reports the depth-quantization calibration as\n`valid` when the file was loaded and `missing` (\"using the linear default\nprofile\") otherwise. Either way the server is ready: only the camera pose is\nrequired (see Camera pose calibration). The profile\nand its table are part of the setup metadata that clients receive; the\nnetwork listener that delivers it to browsers is not implemented yet. Running\na depth-quantization calibration from a client is also not supported yet (the\nserver rejects that calibration kind)."],[619,"The server's TLS certificate must be trusted by the browser."],[1216,"The session to the server ended. A lock never survives a reconnect."],[1206,"The session was not live when you opened the workspace."],[552,"The setup check (`client/dev/setup-check.html`, code in\n`client/src/dev/setupCheck.tsx` and `client/src/dev/setupScenario.ts`) is\na dev-only page for the setup workspace\nand its calibration sections. It is never part\nof the production build."],[2306,"The setup lock (lease) that protects calibration from concurrent clients is\nfixed at 15 s in the server and is not configurable."],[496,"The setup lock is exclusive. It stays held while its owner heartbeats\nevery 5 s, and it expires 15 s after the last heartbeat."],[479,"the setup lock, calibration and placement commits;"],[1160,"The setup workspace is a focused view for **one server at a time**. You\nopen it from that server's card with **Set up**. It then replaces the side\npanel's content; the 3D view stays usable."],[201,"The setup workspace through a scripted calibration; see Setup check"],[1820,"The shared views of that pair disagree by more than 15 mm RMS. Common causes: a bent board, a board moving during capture, or cameras that are not in hardware sync. Check `sync` in the config and hold the board still in each position."],[1362,"The short version, from `server/`:"],[1370,"The shortest path to a built server, linking out to the full server documentation for every detail."],[1299,"The side panel shows `renderer: webgpu` or `renderer: webgl2`."],[7,"The side panel's \"Add server\" form opens a WebTransport session to one\ncapture server. Each server you add gets a server card in the\n\"Servers\" list. You can add several servers, and all their point\nclouds are drawn in the same 3D view."],[1282,"The side panel's **World anchors** section, below the server cards, lists\nevery anchor that a connected server's placement names. It needs no setup\nlock. For each anchor it shows:"],[981,"The size, profile, level or bit depth changes mid-file. Split the file there, or re-encode."],[3389,"The spike runs a WebTransport server with synthetic colour and depth frames\nshaped like the wire format, plus a test page. Use it to check that a\nbrowser on your machine can open a WebTransport session with a pinned\ncertificate. It does not use cameras or the C++ server."],[977,"The SPS cannot be read. The file is corrupt or uses syntax the client does not parse."],[3645,"The start-up log shows the layout and the per-camera bitrates:"],[1855,"The start-up order matters for hardware sync: the server writes the sync\nsettings to every camera first, starts the secondaries, and starts the\nprimary last, so every secondary is armed before the first trigger. Frames\nare passed on only after every camera is streaming and the clock sync below\nis enabled; earlier frames are discarded."],[3448,"The state machine (`src/control/SetupController`) is implemented and tested.\nThe network layer that carries it to clients is not available yet; see\nWhat works today."],[932,"the status label reads `streaming`;"],[1039,"The stream layout (`concatenated` or `per-camera`) and the bundle count, then one row per bundle: its camera count, its availability, and its render status."],[3570,"The stream layout decides how the server packs several cameras into HEVC\nstreams. It is set once in the server config with `encoding.session_mode`.\nClients read it from the stream descriptors and cannot change it."],[1364,"The terminal redraws a rate table roughly every 5 seconds. After the\nwarm-up, every stage should reach your configured frame rate with 0 drops.\nSee Read the telemetry for what each line means,\nand Run the server for a full\nworked log."],[1635,"the test `orbbec_live_sync_integration_test`"],[1377,"The tested machine is Ubuntu 26.04 with an NVIDIA RTX 4090 (compute\ncapability 8.9), CUDA 13, TensorRT 11 and Orbbec cameras on USB 3. See\nRequirements for the full list and a check\ncommand for each item, including what to do on an older GPU."],[2964,"The tested version is TensorRT `11.1.0.106-1+cuda13.3`. Plain `tensorrt-dev`\ninstalls the newest build, currently `11.3.0.99-1+cuda13.4`, which targets\nCUDA 13.4 and is not tested. The repository also has `11.2.1.2-1+cuda13.3`,\nwhich targets the tested CUDA 13.3 but is itself not tested. To stay on the tested stack, see\nTroubleshooting."],[991,"The tile size and the camera's `depthIntrinsics` size differ. Make them equal."],[933,"the title is the manifest's `serverName` (`Recorded rig`);"],[3926,"The two cameras' capture threads are delivering at different times, often because of CPU load (alignment runs on the CPU per camera)."],[983,"The two files have different frame counts. Trim them to the same frames."],[3014,"The udev rule is missing. Run `sudo /opt/OrbbecSDK_v2.8.7/shared/install_udev_rules.sh`, then replug the camera."],[3377,"The UDP port and the certificate settings will live in a gateway section of\nthe server config. That section does not exist yet."],[264,"the UI engineer's two reruns after the per-session counts fix:\n`done`, 7 of 7 steps, no errors. The last step reported B at\n`decoded 1, uploaded 1, dropped 0 this session`. A screenshot a moment\nlater showed both columns `ready, drawing`, with decoded pairs equal to\nuploaded on each card (A 35 / 35, B 12 / 12)."],[2774,"The upload thread does not wait for the copy. A slot is reused only when no\nstage holds its frame any more and its copy has finished. Slots are created\non demand up to a limit that the server computes from the queue sizes (41\nwith `config/dev/live.yaml`); with those sizes, at most about 45 MB of\npinned host memory and the same on the GPU. When every slot is in use, the\nnew batch is dropped and counted; see\nRead the telemetry."],[2770,"The upload thread takes each batch from the upload queue and, for every\nframe:"],[11,"The URL must follow these rules. The form checks them before connecting:"],[1348,"The view is slow or jerky"],[1301,"The viewer shows a coloured point cloud on a dark background. Gaps appear\nwhere the depth was invalid or out of range."],[1252,"The viewer uses an orbit camera. It turns around a target point that\nstarts 2 m in front of the scene origin. At start the camera sits 3 m from\nthe target, slightly above it, looking forward along +Z."],[3615,"The whole frame set is skipped"],[3861,"The whole-session latency report follows, in the same format as the 5 s\nreport. Use it for tail latencies."],[2912,"The wire contract between server and browser is `protocol/wire-format.md` in\nthe repository."],[215,"the wiring and latency checks fail only after about 30 s with \"no pair\nuploaded\". The dev server answers a missing `.hevc` path with its HTML\npage, not a 404."],[210,"The wiring check's read-back overlay:"],[2800,"The working segmenter. Needs a TensorRT engine (Install)."],[1163,"The workspace also has a **Placement** section, where you edit the\nserver's placement as a local draft and commit it; see\nPlacement editing. A placement draft is\nkept in memory when you leave the workspace (a reload loses it), and is\nonly sent when you select **Commit placement**."],[135,"The workspace does not hold the lock (acquiring, leaving or ended)."],[1222,"The workspace does not move the 3D camera to the server's point cloud yet."],[1162,"The workspace never commits anything by itself. A calibration result comes\ninto force only when you select **Commit**. When you leave, or the lock or\nthe connection is lost, the client discards its own copy of an\nuncommitted result. What the server does with it is not defined by the\nprotocol contract yet (change request 0012 is open); the mock server\ndrops it."],[1166,"The workspace opens and asks the server for the setup lock at once."],[1340,"Their placements put them in the same place, or they use different anchors that both sit at the scene origin in this browser."],[1363,"Then edit `config/local/live.yaml`: set each camera's `serial_number`, and\neither build the RVM engine or set `mask.backend: fill_all` to run without\nsegmentation."],[2982,"Then install the Python packages and run the script:"],[600,"Then open http\\://localhost:5173/."],[1386,"There are three calibration kinds. Each one is a server-side state with an\noptional client-side workspace to run it from. Today the server and client\ncannot talk to each other at all (see Serve to browsers),\nso every client-side calibration in this table works only against the\nclient's own built-in mock server, not against a real `orbbec_streamer`."],[2930,"There are two submodules:"],[592,"There is a `client/package-lock.json`, so install with `npm ci`."],[3700,"There is no config section for telemetry and no metrics endpoint yet.\nNetwork metrics (per-client queues, drops, stalls) will come with the\nWebTransport server; see Serve to browsers."],[2354,"There is no telemetry section. The server logs rates, drops and\nstage-by-stage latency on a fixed schedule."],[807,"There is nothing to commit."],[586,"These are notes for the docs team, not a tutorial. Each fact below was\nchecked against `client/package.json`, `client/vite.config.ts`,\n`client/index.html` and the client source on 2026-09-28. The user-facing\npages are Run the dev build,\nBrowser requirements and\nAdd a server."],[654,"These are tracked in `client/docs/development/ROADMAP.md` under\n\"Phase 1D — UI\" and \"Phase 2 — media and rendering\"."],[2712,"These CMake cache variables are passed with `-D` and are not environment\nvariables, but people often need them:"],[438,"These two stages are only meaningful on a real GPU."],[77,"These were observed on the project's test machine. Other browsers have not\nbeen tested yet."],[2010,"This check does not validate `mask.backend` or\n`processing.depth_filter_backend`; those names are checked when the live\npipeline starts."],[801,"This client does not hold the lock: you were forced out of setup, or the lock expired."],[1208,"This client's lock ran out, for example because renewals did not reach the server."],[3647,"This describes how the server produces what the contract specifies. The\nnormative definition is `protocol/wire-format.md` (§4 records, §6\ndescriptors