1,"To keep a log file and the rate tables as plain log lines:"],[379,"To measure real decode, network and display time, use a real server and a\nreal browser decoder. The probe measures the same stages there."],[1287,"To move an anchor:"],[204,"To run a page without clicking:"],[127,"To stop a run, select **Cancel depth quantization**. The line reads\n`Cancel: accepted; the run is cancelled and nothing is committed`. The\nstate line then shows the state the server reports (the mock server\nreturns to the state from before the run)."],[886,"To try the feature without a recording, generate a synthetic pair of test\npatterns with FFmpeg and libx265 (tested with FFmpeg 8 and Node 24). The\n\"depth\" file here is a colour test pattern encoded as Main10, so the point\ncloud it produces is meaningless. It only shows that playback works."],[1289,"To undo, select **Reset to identity**."],[389,"To use BYOB reads on the media streams:"],[1693,"Too many NVENC sessions at once: GeForce drivers limit concurrent encoder sessions and report status 21 (`NV_ENC_ERR_INCOMPATIBLE_CLIENT_KEY`). `ctest` runs the NVENC tests one at a time (they share the `nvenc` resource lock), so this appears only when another program is encoding at the same time, such as a running server, OBS or a second `ctest`. Stop it and rerun."],[3723,"Total batches dropped since start: evicted from the full upload queue (2 batches), plus batches dropped because every GPU upload slot was in use."],[3758,"Total batches the recorder dropped because it fell behind. Recording never slows the pipeline; it drops instead."],[2044,"Total calibration duration including warm-up. Must be 1 to 60."],[3851,"Total encoded bytes."],[3731,"Total evicted from the full encode queue (`encoding.queue_capacity`, default 2)."],[3727,"Total evicted from the full processing queue (2 batches)."],[2446,"Total run time in seconds, **including** warm-up. Must be 1–60 and larger than `setup.warmup_seconds`."],[3699,"Totals and whole-session latency"],[1255,"Touch"],[3565,"Trade-offs"],[3362,"Transport choice"],[2103,"Trigger output delay."],[2095,"Trigger-to-image delay, applied to every camera."],[6,"Troubleshooting"],[46,"Troubleshooting"],[103,"Troubleshooting"],[162,"Troubleshooting"],[234,"Troubleshooting"],[281,"Troubleshooting"],[476,"Troubleshooting"],[517,"Troubleshooting"],[551,"Troubleshooting"],[715,"Troubleshooting"],[851,"Troubleshooting"],[1013,"Troubleshooting"],[1159,"Troubleshooting"],[1238,"Troubleshooting"],[1358,"Troubleshooting"],[1549,"Troubleshooting"],[1708,"Troubleshooting"],[1845,"Troubleshooting"],[1982,"Troubleshooting"],[2405,"Troubleshooting"],[2655,"Troubleshooting"],[2766,"Troubleshooting"],[2924,"Troubleshooting"],[3156,"Troubleshooting"],[3228,"Troubleshooting"],[3356,"Troubleshooting"],[3569,"Troubleshooting"],[3686,"Troubleshooting"],[3943,"Troubleshooting & FAQ"],[3354,"Try the WebTransport spike"],[749,"Turn about the +Z axis."],[743,"Turn about the vertical (+Y) axis."],[1072,"Turning it off stops them at once. Turning it on takes effect when the\nserver accepts."],[2600,"Turns encoding on"],[2225,"Turns on encoding. Required for GPU-output recording and, later, for serving."],[2083,"Turns on hardware sync. Requires exactly one camera with `role: primary`. With sync off, at most one camera may be primary."],[3590,"Two NVENC sessions per camera, `2 × N` in total."],[1339,"Two servers' clouds overlap"],[2025,"Type"],[2038,"Type"],[2051,"Type"],[2077,"Type"],[2118,"Type"],[2144,"Type"],[2189,"Type"],[2219,"Type"],[2274,"Type"],[2308,"Type"],[2326,"Type"],[751,"Type a number. It applies as soon as it is valid, and your 3D view\nfollows. A comma works as the decimal mark."],[176,"Type check, then production build into `client/dist/`"],[1288,"Type in its fields. A valid value applies at once, and every server\nthat uses the anchor moves with it in your 3D view. **Arrow Up** and\n**Arrow Down** step by 0.01 m or 1° (**Shift**: ten times that)."],[172,"TypeScript check, no